re-rust/pulls/175/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/acad85cc2163100dcc80b7ae7e7e22a0a16bc620"}},"author_association":"MEMBER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3753394429","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/175#issuecomment-3753394429","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/175","id":3753394429,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7fuED9","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T08:08:07Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T10:15:48Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds FDD and GTS git submodules; registers an analytics SDK and analytics crate in the Cargo workspace; implements a new analytics module (SDK + implementation) with GTS routing, query validation, field handling, REST endpoints, and RFC 7807 error handling; and adds extensive FDD-Adapter and analytics design/spec documentation.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Git Submodules & Workspace** <br> `.gitmodules`, `Cargo.toml` | Added `guidelines/FDD` and `guidelines/GTS` submodules; registered `modules/analytics/analytics-sdk` and `modules/analytics/analytics` as workspace members. |\n| **Top-level App & Config** <br> `apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml`, `apps/hyperspot-server/src/registered_modules.rs`, `config/no-db.yaml` | Added `analytics` crate dependency in server manifest; imported analytics crate as `_`; added `modules.analytics` entry in no-db config. |\n| **Documentation & Contributor Guides** <br> `AGENTS.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `README.md` | Replaced/redirected multiple guideline references to FDD pages and FDD-Adapter specs; added Feature-Driven Design links and reordered contributing items. |\n| **Guidelines / FDD-Adapter Specs** <br> `guidelines/FDD-Adapter/*` (many files), `guidelines/FDD-Adapter/AGENTS.md`, `guidelines/DNA`, `guidelines/GTS` | Added extensive FDD-Adapter specification set (API contracts, build/deploy, conventions, domain model, patterns, module structure, testing, tech stack, etc.) and updated submodule pointers. |\n| **Lint / API Validation** <br> `dylint_lints/de08_rest_api_conventions/.../lib.rs` | Extended endpoint path validation to recognize OData v4 system resources (segments starting with `$`) and skip validation for them. |\n| **Analytics SDK crate** <br> `modules/analytics/analytics-sdk/Cargo.toml`, `modules/analytics/analytics-sdk/src/{lib.rs,api.rs,errors.rs,models.rs}`, `modules/analytics/analytics-sdk/src/gts/{mod.rs,schema.rs}` | New SDK crate exposing `AnalyticsApi` trait (async, currently no methods), `AnalyticsError`/`AnalyticsResult`, GTS types `SchemaV1` and `QueryReturnsSchemaV1` with (de)serialization, validation, and utility methods. |\n| **Analytics implementation crate (manifest & wiring)** <br> `modules/analytics/analytics/Cargo.toml`, `modules/analytics/analytics/src/lib.rs`, `modules/analytics/analytics/src/{config.rs,local_client.rs,module.rs,infra/mod.rs,models/tests.rs}` | New analytics crate with config scaffold, LocalAnalyticsClient implementing SDK trait, AnalyticsModule implementing ModKit traits (Module/DbModule/RestfulModule) and wiring a shared GTS router; test utilities (MockOpenApiRegistry). |\n| **Domain: GTS core** <br> `modules/analytics/analytics/src/domain/gts_core/{mod.rs,identifier.rs,field_handler.rs,query_validator.rs,router.rs,routing_table.rs}` | Implemented GTS identifier parsing, FieldHandler (categorization, request/response filtering, computed injection, patch validation, projection), QueryValidator (indexed-field checks), RoutingTable (HashMap-based registration/lookup), and GtsCoreRouter (routing API). |\n| **API: REST GTS core** <br> `modules/analytics/analytics/src/api/rest/{mod.rs,gts_core/{mod.rs,dto.rs,error_handler.rs,handlers.rs,routes.rs}}` | Added REST DTOs, RFC 7807 ProblemDetails and GtsCoreError mapping, handlers for CRUD + OData endpoints (GET/POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE, $metadata), and OperationBuilder-based route registration with OpenAPI metadata. |\n| **API surface & tests** <br> `modules/analytics/analytics/src/api/mod.rs`, `modules/analytics/analytics/src/tests.rs`, `modules/analytics/analytics/tests/*` | Exposed `gts_core` submodule; added MockOpenApiRegistry, unit and integration tests for routing, error mapping, 404/501 scenarios, and module trait conformance. |\n| **Analytics architecture & features docs** <br> `modules/analytics/architecture/*`, `modules/analytics/architecture/features/**/*` | Added ADRs, BUSINESS/DESIGN docs, FEATURES manifest, and many detailed feature DESIGN/CHANGES files (GTS core, query capabilities, datasources, dashboards, plugins, reporting, schema features, tenancy, etc.). |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    actor Client\n    participant ApiGateway\n    participant AnalyticsModule\n    participant GtsCoreRouter\n    participant DomainHandler\n    participant OpenApiRegistry\n\n    Client->>ApiGateway: HTTP request (/analytics/v1/gts/...)\n    ApiGateway->>AnalyticsModule: Axum handler (extract SecurityCtx, OData)\n    AnalyticsModule->>GtsCoreRouter: route(gts_id)\n    alt route -> handler\n        GtsCoreRouter->>DomainHandler: delegate request\n        DomainHandler-->>AnalyticsModule: response (data)\n        AnalyticsModule->>OpenApiRegistry: register operation (startup/test)\n        AnalyticsModule-->>ApiGateway: HTTP 200 JSON (or 204)\n        ApiGateway-->>Client: Response\n    else no delegate\n        GtsCoreRouter-->>AnalyticsModule: None\n        AnalyticsModule->>ApiGateway: ProblemDetails (501/404)\n        ApiGateway-->>Client: Error response (RFC7807 JSON)\n    end\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐇 I hopped through specs and code tonight,  \n> > I planted routes and schemas tight,  \n> > GTS and FDD now hand in paw,  \n> > Problems dressed in details — hurrah!  \n> > A tiny rabbit cheers the analytics light.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 2 | ❌ 1</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>❌ Failed checks (1 warning)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status     | Explanation                                                                           | Resolution                                                                         |\n| :----------------: | :--------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docstring Coverage | ⚠️ Warning | Docstring coverage is 53.54% which is insufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%. | Write docstrings for the functions missing them to satisfy the coverage threshold. |\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (2 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name    | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| :---------------: | :------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n|    Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title '[WiP][DO NOT MERGE] feat(analytics): based on FDD in progress implementation' clearly describes the main change: an in-progress Feature-Driven Design (FDD) based implementation of the Analytics module. It is specific, related to the core changeset, and appropriately flagged as work-in-progress. |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Recent review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 2c8fb7d5db13a4e9275d857e299a059105b90ed0 and acad85cc2163100dcc80b7ae7e7e22a0a16bc620.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (1)</summary>\n\n* `guidelines/FDD`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (1)</summary>\n\n* guidelines/FDD\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3753394429/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3807796739","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/175#issuecomment-3807796739","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/175","id":3807796739,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7i9l4D","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users