de_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6eAKW2","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,299 @@\n+# Module Code Generation Pipeline\n+\n+This document defines a repeatable, **human-controlled** pipeline for generating new modules with LLMs.\n+It is designed to be:\n+\n+- **LLM-actionable** (unambiguous inputs/outputs and prompt templates)\n+- **Human-auditable** (review gates, checklists, clear phase boundaries)\n+- **Project-aligned** (ModKit + DDD-light + SDK pattern, observability, security)\n+\n+## Roles\n+\n+- **Human owner**: decides scope, accepts/declines changes, merges PRs.\n+- **TOP-GRADE LLM**: creates architecture/code skeletons and higher-level reasoning.\n+- **LOW-GRADE LLM**: fixes compilation/lints without changing intended behavior.\n+\n+## Non-negotiable project constraints\n+\n+- Follow:\n+  - `guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`\n+  - `docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`\n+  - `docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`\n+- SDK pattern:\n+  - `<module>-sdk` contains **public API** (traits/models/errors; transport-agnostic)\n+  - `<module>` contains **implementation** (domain, infra, REST, local client)\n+- All SDK API methods take `&SecurityCtx`.\n+- REST is wired via ModKit `OperationBuilder` (type-safe routes + OpenAPI).\n+- Always keep `make all` green before moving to the next phase.\n+\n+## Standard artifacts (authoritative filenames)\n+\n+All are under `modules/{module_name}/docs/`:\n+\n+- `1_INTENT_DESIGN.md`\n+- `2_INTENT_FACTS.md`\n+- `3_INTENT_SCENARIOS.md`\n+- `4_ACTUAL_DESIGN.md`\n+- `5_ACTUAL_FACTS.md`\n+- `6_ACTUAL_SCENARIOS.md`\n+- `7_INTENT_VS_ACTUAL.md`\n+\n+\n+## Code generation flow\n+\n+- Follow the 5 phases below separately\n+- Stop after every phase, submit a PR and get approvals from stakeholders\n+\n+| # | Phase | Delivery |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| 1 | Intent design | `1_INTENT_DESIGN.md` |\n+| 2 | Intent facts + scenarios | `2_INTENT_FACTS.md`, `3_INTENT_SCENARIOS.md` |\n+| 3 | Code for v1 scenarios | all the needed modules code, compilable, v2+ code stubs, actual design `4_ACTUAL_DESIGN.md`, `5_ACTUAL_FACTS.md`, `6_ACTUAL_SCENARIOS.md`, `7_INTENT_VS_ACTUAL.md` |\n+| 4 | Tests for v1 scenarios | all the needed modules tests, compilable, v2+ code stubs |\n+\n+For v2+ - repeat 3,4 above, actualize the code, tests, `4_ACTUAL_DESIGN.md`, `5_ACTUAL_FACTS.md`, `6_ACTUAL_SCENARIOS.md`, `7_INTENT_VS_ACTUAL.md` after each phase.\n+\n+## Phase 1: Intent design\n+\n+Phase 1 outcome:\n+- `1_INTENT_DESIGN.md` - generated, cross-reviewed by models, reviewed by humans, committed\n+\n+### 1.1 - Prepare environment\n+\n+1. Install needed tools (e.g. Windsurf, Cursor, Github Copilot)\n+2. Pick model tiers for this project.\n+   - TOP-GRADE example: Claude Opus 4.5, GPT 5.2\n+   - LOW-GRADE example: SWE-1.5, Codex\n+\n+### 1.2 - Scaffold module layout\n+\n+1. Create module folder: `modules/{module_name}/`\n+2. Create docs folder: `modules/{module_name}/docs/`\n+3. Ensure you follow the canonical layout and SDK pattern from `guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`.\n+\n+### 1.3 - Write intent design (`1_INTENT_DESIGN.md`)\n+\n+Use your favorite SDD (e.g. openspec-proposal) to generate `1_INTENT_DESIGN.md`.","path":"guidelines/CODE_GEN_PIPELINE.md","commit_id":"18b44005d235f0c87434397e8bb0310fa2e0928d","original_commit_id":"06cb74af0d049ca1275effdd774700db9fae15b8","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I agree, we need to specify the tool to use or a list of tools.","created_at":"2025-12-29T12:13:19Z","updated_at":"2025-12-29T13:17:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/164#discussion_r2650842550","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/164","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2650842550"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/164#discussion_r2650842550"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/164"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2650842550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":76,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2649892292,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":76,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2650844727","pull_request_review_id":3615733354,"id":2650844727,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6eAK43","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,299 @@\n+# Module Code Generation Pipeline\n+\n+This document defines a repeatable, **human-controlled** pipeline for generating new modules with LLMs.\n+It is designed to be:\n+\n+- **LLM-actionable** (unambiguous inputs/outputs and prompt templates)\n+- **Human-auditable** (review gates, checklists, clear phase boundaries)\n+- **Project-aligned** (ModKit + DDD-light + SDK pattern, observability, security)\n+\n+## Roles\n+\n+- **Human owner**: decides scope, accepts/declines changes, merges PRs.\n+- **TOP-GRADE LLM**: creates architecture/code skeletons and higher-level reasoning.\n+- **LOW-GRADE LLM**: fixes compilation/lints without changing intended behavior.\n+\n+## Non-negotiable project constraints\n+\n+- Follow:\n+  - `guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`\n+  - `docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`\n+  - `docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`\n+- SDK pattern:\n+  - `<module>-sdk` contains **public API** (traits/models/errors; transport-agnostic)\n+  - `<module>` contains **implementation** (domain, infra, REST, local client)\n+- All SDK API methods take `&SecurityCtx`.\n+- REST is wired via ModKit `OperationBuilder` (type-safe routes + OpenAPI).\n+- Always keep `make all` green before moving to the next phase.\n+\n+## Standard artifacts (authoritative filenames)\n+\n+All are under `modules/{module_name}/docs/`:\n+\n+- `1_INTENT_DESIGN.md`\n+- `2_INTENT_FACTS.md`\n+- `3_INTENT_SCENARIOS.md`\n+- `4_ACTUAL_DESIGN.md`\n+- `5_ACTUAL_FACTS.md`\n+- `6_ACTUAL_SCENARIOS.md`\n+- `7_INTENT_VS_ACTUAL.md`\n+\n+\n+## Code generation flow\n+\n+- Follow the 5 phases below separately\n+- Stop after every phase, submit a PR and get approvals from stakeholders\n+\n+| # | Phase | Delivery |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| 1 | Intent design | `1_INTENT_DESIGN.md` |\n+| 2 | Intent facts + scenarios | `2_INTENT_FACTS.md`, `3_INTENT_SCENARIOS.md` |\n+| 3 | Code for v1 scenarios | all the needed modules code, compilable, v2+ code stubs, actual design `4_ACTUAL_DESIGN.md`, `5_ACTUAL_FACTS.md`, `6_ACTUAL_SCENARIOS.md`, `7_INTENT_VS_ACTUAL.md` |\n+| 4 | Tests for v1 scenarios | all the needed modules tests, compilable, v2+ code stubs |\n+\n+For v2+ - repeat 3,4 above, actualize the code, tests, `4_ACTUAL_DESIGN.md`, `5_ACTUAL_FACTS.md`, `6_ACTUAL_SCENARIOS.md`, `7_INTENT_VS_ACTUAL.md` after each phase.\n+\n+## Phase 1: Intent design\n+\n+Phase 1 outcome:\n+- `1_INTENT_DESIGN.md` - generated, cross-reviewed by models, reviewed by humans, committed\n+\n+### 1.1 - Prepare environment\n+\n+1. Install needed tools (e.g. Windsurf, Cursor, Github Copilot)\n+2. Pick model tiers for this project.\n+   - TOP-GRADE example: Claude Opus 4.5, GPT 5.2\n+   - LOW-GRADE example: SWE-1.5, Codex\n+\n+### 1.2 - Scaffold module layout\n+\n+1. Create module folder: `modules/{module_name}/`\n+2. Create docs folder: `modules/{module_name}/docs/`\n+3. Ensure you follow the canonical layout and SDK pattern from `guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`.\n+\n+### 1.3 - Write intent design (`1_INTENT_DESIGN.md`)\n+\n+Use your favorite SDD (e.g. openspec-proposal) to generate `1_INTENT_DESIGN.md`.\n+\n+Prompt (for TOP-GRADE models):\n+\n+```\n+Create `modules/{module_name}/docs/1_INTENT_DESIGN.md`.\n+\n+Input: my description of the module purpose + use cases.\n+\n+Must follow:\n+- guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md\n+- docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md\n+\n+Output must include:\n+- Module category (generic/gateway/worker)\n+- Public API surface (SDK trait methods)\n+- Data model overview\n+- Persistence needs\n+- Security/tenancy assumptions (SecurityCtx usage)\n+- Observability plan (tracing + logs)\n+- GTS schema and instances definitions\n+```\n+\n+### 1.4 - Pre-PR self-review\n+\n+- Review the scope and missing invariants.\n+- Review by other independent cloud models **ChatGPT**, **Gemini** and **Claude**\n+\n+```\n+Review my 1_INTENT_DESIGN.md, criticize it, identify clear gaps regarding the industry","path":"guidelines/CODE_GEN_PIPELINE.md","commit_id":"18b44005d235f0c87434397e8bb0310fa2e0928d","original_commit_id":"06cb74af0d049ca1275effdd774700db9fae15b8","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscrip