432831/e90313f4-9d3a-4b63-8b54-cfe14e7ec20d) to ensure uploads and comments are reliably processed by Codecov.\n\n## [Codecov](https://app.codecov.io/gh/hypernetix/hyperspot/pull/161?dropdown=coverage&src=pr&el=h1&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=github&utm_content=comment&utm_campaign=pr+comments&utm_term=None) Report\n:white_check_mark: All modified and coverable lines are covered by tests.\n\n:loudspeaker: Thoughts on this report? [Let us know!](https://github.com/codecov/feedback/issues/255)","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3693251925/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":160,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/160","source_state":"closed","source_author":"Artifizer","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #160] fix: prevent unsafe PID conversion in process termination","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"claude/find-fix-bug-mjmytc9p95xomh53-IdK9G","pr_head_sha":"91cb0c52e951893e63f16727dab719c77b188153","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"Artifizer","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/160","id":3131338789,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs66pHAl","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/160","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/160.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/160.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/160","number":160,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix: prevent unsafe PID conversion in process termination","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed a critical bug in send_terminate_signal() where u32 to i32 conversion could silently fail and default to PID 0. On Unix systems, sending signals to PID 0 targets all processes in the process group, which could terminate unintended processes.\r\n\r\nChanges:\r\n- Replace unwrap_or(0) with proper match statement\r\n- Add warning log when PID exceeds i32::MAX\r\n- Return false when conversion fails instead of using dangerous default\r\n\r\nThis prevents potential security/safety issues where wrong processes could be terminated during shutdown.","created_at":"2025-12-26T15:15:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T12:08:45Z","closed_at":"2026-01-19T12:08:25Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"53d57fdb86a94fc16e536d23b5ff05193d63a0f2","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/160/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/160/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https:/