 review.\n| [Files with missing lines](https://app.codecov.io/gh/hypernetix/hyperspot/pull/125?dropdown=coverage&src=pr&el=tree&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=github&utm_content=comment&utm_campaign=pr+comments&utm_term=None) | Patch % | Lines |\n|---|---|---|\n| [...es/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/models.rs](https://app.codecov.io/gh/hypernetix/hyperspot/pull/125?src=pr&el=tree&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=github&utm_content=comment&utm_campaign=pr+comments&utm_term=None#diff-bW9kdWxlcy90eXBlcy1yZWdpc3RyeS90eXBlcy1yZWdpc3RyeS1zZGsvc3JjL21vZGVscy5ycw==) | 65.45% | [76 Missing :warning: ](https://app.codecov.io/gh/hypernetix/hyperspot/pull/125?src=pr&el=tree&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=github&utm_content=comment&utm_campaign=pr+comments&utm_term=None) |\n\n:loudspeaker: Thoughts on this report? [Let us know!](https://github.com/codecov/feedback/issues/255)","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3674607722/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623767405","pull_request_review_id":3583706882,"id":2623767405,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cY4Nt","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,208 @@\n+# Design: Types Registry Module - Phase 1.1\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+HyperSpot requires a centralized GTS (Global Type System) registry to manage type definitions and instances across the platform. This enables:\n+- Cross-vendor type interoperability\n+- Schema validation for API payloads\n+- Fine-grained access control based on type identifiers\n+- Extensible plugin architectures\n+\n+Phase 1.1 focuses on establishing the foundational contracts and in-memory storage, deferring REST API (Phase 1.2) and database persistence (Phase 1.3) to later phases.\n+\n+**Stakeholders**: Platform developers, module authors, third-party integrators\n+\n+## Goals / Non-Goals\n+\n+### Goals\n+- Define SDK API trait for inter-module communication\n+- Implement in-memory storage for GTS entities\n+- Integrate gts-rust library for standard GTS operations (OP#1-OP#11)\n+- Follow HyperSpot module conventions (DDD-light, SDK pattern)\n+- Ensure thread-safe concurrent access\n+","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/design.md","commit_id":"cfa6c0b8b81fbcc2832868ce86ff5f6a0a7ceadb","original_commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think it will be nice to consume GTS specifications from jsons on module start or use RustEmbed","created_at":"2025-12-16T15:29:52Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T15:48:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2623767405","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623767405"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2623767405"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623767405/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":23,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":23,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623794005","pull_request_review_id":3583706882,"id":2623794005,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cY-tV","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to register GTS entities (types and instances) in the registry.\n+\n+A GTS entity consists of:\n+- **GTS ID**: A valid GTS identifier (e.g., `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1~` for types, `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1.0` for instances)\n+- **Kind**: Either `Type` (schema) or `Instance` (object)\n+- **Content**: JSON Schema for types, JSON object for instances\n+- **Metadata**: Optional metadata (description, tags, created_at, updated_at)\n+\n+Registration SHALL:\n+- Validate the GTS ID format using OP#1 (ID Validation)\n+- Extract and parse the GTS ID components using OP#3 (ID Parsing)\n+- Optionally validate GTS references within the content using OP#7 (Relationship Resolution)\n+- Generate a deterministic UUID from the GTS ID using OP#5 (ID to UUID Mapping)\n+- Store the entity in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register a type entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS type identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON Schema as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register an instance entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS instance identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON object as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid GTS ID format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an invalid GTS identifier `invalid-gts-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns a validation error with details about the invalid format\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate entity registration\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the same GTS ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a conflict error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Listing\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to list GTS entities with filtering and pagination support.\n+\n+Listing SHALL support:\n+- Filtering by GTS ID pattern using OP#4 (ID Pattern Matching) with wildcards\n+- Filtering by entity kind (Type, Instance, or both)\n+- Filtering by vendor, package, namespace, or type components\n+- Cursor-based pagination with configurable limit\n+- Query execution using OP#10 (Query Execution)\n+\n+#### Scenario: List all entities with pagination\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains 100 GTS entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `limit=25`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the first 25 entities\n+- **AND** the response includes a cursor for the next page\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by wildcard pattern\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains entities from vendors `acme` and `globex`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only entities from vendor `acme`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by kind\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains both type and instance entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `kind=Type`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only type entities (ending with `~`)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return empty list when no matches\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains no entities matching pattern `gts.unknown.*`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with that pattern\n+- **THEN** the system returns an empty list with no error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Retrieval\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to retrieve a single GTS entity by its identifier.\n+\n+Retrieval SHALL:\n+- Accept a valid GTS ID\n+- Return the full entity including content and metadata\n+- Support attribute access using OP#11 (Attribute Access) with `@` selector\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity by exact ID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns the complete entity with content and metadata\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity attribute\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **AND** the entity has a property `name` with value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~@name`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return not found for non-existent entity\n+\n+- **GIVEN** no entity with GTS ID `gts.unknown.pkg.ns.type.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a not found error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Validation (OP#1)\n+\n+The system SHALL validate GTS identifier syntax according to the GTS specification.\n+\n+Valid GTS identifiers MUST:\n+- Start with `gts.` prefix\n+- Contain segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type`\n+- Include version: `v<MAJOR>` or `v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>`\n+- End with `~` for type identifiers, no suffix for instance identifiers\n+- Use only lowercase ASCII letters, digits, and underscores in segments\n+- Have segments starting with a letter or underscore\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as a type (schema)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct instance identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as an instance (object)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with invalid prefix\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `invalid.acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Invalid GTS prefix\"\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with uppercase characters\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.Acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Segments must be lowercase\"\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Parsing (OP#3)\n+\n+The system SHALL parse GTS identifiers into their constituent components.\n+\n+Parsing SHALL extract:\n+- `vendor`: The vendor/organization identifier\n+- `package`: The package/module identifier\n+- `namespace`: The namespace category (or `_` placeholder)\n+- `type_name`: The type name\n+- `version_major`: The major version number\n+- `version_minor`: The optional minor version number\n+- `is_type`: Whether the identifier represents a type (true) or instance (false)\n+- `segments`: For chained identifiers, all segments in order\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse simple type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains:\n+  - `vendor = \"acme\"`\n+  - `package = \"core\"`\n+  - `namespace = \"events\"`\n+  - `type_name = \"user_created\"`\n+  - `version_major = 1`\n+  - `version_minor = Some(2)`\n+  - `is_type = true`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse chained identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.x.core.events.event.v1~acme.app._.custom_event.v2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains 2 segments\n+- **AND** the first segment has vendor `x` and is a base type\n+- **AND** the second segment has vendor `acme` and is a derived type\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Pattern Matching (OP#4)\n+\n+The system SHALL match GTS identifiers against patterns containing wildcards.\n+\n+Pattern matching SHALL support:\n+- `*` wildcard matching any single segment\n+- `**` wildcard matching zero or more segments\n+- Exact segment matching\n+\n+#### Scenario: Match with single wildcard\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*.events.*`\n+- **AND** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system matches the identifier against the pattern\n+- **THEN** the match succeeds\n+\n+#### Scenario: No match with different vendor\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **AND** the identifier `gts.globex.core.events.order.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system matches the identifier against the pattern\n+- **THEN** the match fails\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID to UUID Mapping (OP#5)\n+\n+The system SHALL generate deterministic UUIDs from GTS identifiers.\n+\n+UUID generation SHALL:\n+- Produce the same UUID for the same GTS ID (deterministic)\n+- Use UUID v5 with a GTS-specific namespace\n+- Support scoping by major version (same UUID for v1.0 and v1.5)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Generate deterministic UUID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system generates a UUID twice\n+- **THEN** both UUIDs are identical\n+\n+#### Scenario: Same major version produces same UUID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifiers `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0` and `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.5`\n+- **WHEN** the system generates UUIDs with major scope\n+- **THEN** both UUIDs are identical\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Schema Validation (OP#6)\n+\n+The system SHALL validate JSON object instances against their corresponding JSON Schema types.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate instance against schema\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` with JSON Schema requiring `userId` field\n+- **AND** an instance `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0` with `userId` field\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the instance\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid instance\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` with JSON Schema requiring `userId` field\n+- **AND** an instance missing the `userId` field\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the instance\n+- **THEN** validation fails with details about the missing field\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Relationship Resolution (OP#7)\n+\n+The system SHALL resolve inter-dependencies between GTS entities and detect broken references.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Resolve valid references\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type that references another registered type via `x-gts-ref`\n+- **WHEN** the system resolves relationships\n+- **THEN** all references are resolved successfully\n+\n+#### Scenario: Detect broken reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type that references a non-existent type `gts.unknown.pkg.ns.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system resolves relationships\n+- **THEN** the system reports the broken reference\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Compatibility Checking (OP#8)\n+\n+The system SHALL verify schema compatibility between different MINOR versions.\n+\n+Compatibility modes:\n+- **Backward**: Old instances work with new schema\n+- **Forward**: New instances work with old schema\n+- **Full**: Both backward and forward compatible\n+\n+#### Scenario: Check backward compatibility\n+\n+- **GIVEN** schema v1.0 and schema v1.1 where v1.1 adds an optional field\n+- **WHEN** the system checks backward compatibility\n+- **THEN** the schemas are backward compatible\n+\n+#### Scenario: Detect backward incompatibility\n+\n+- **GIVEN** schema v1.0 and schema v1.1 where v1.1 removes a required field\n+- **WHEN** the system checks backward compatibility\n+- **THEN** the schemas are NOT backward compatible\n+- **AND** the system reports the incompatibility reason\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Version Casting (OP#9)\n+\n+The system SHALL transform instances between compatible MINOR versions.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Cast instance to newer version\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an instance conforming to v1.0\n+- **AND** v1.1 adds an optional field with default value\n+- **WHEN** the system casts the instance to v1.1\n+- **THEN** the casted instance includes the new field with default value\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Query Execution (OP#10)\n+\n+The system SHALL filter identifier collections using the GTS query language.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query with attribute filter\n+\n+- **GIVEN** entities with various `status` values\n+- **WHEN** the user queries `gts.acme.core.*[status=active]`\n+- **THEN** only entities with `status=active` are returned\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Attribute Access (OP#11)\n+\n+The system SHALL retrieve property values using the attribute selector (`@`).\n+\n+#### Scenario: Access top-level attribute\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with property `name = \"UserCreated\"`\n+- **WHEN** the user accesses `entity@name`\n+- **THEN** the value `\"UserCreated\"` is returned\n+\n+#### Scenario: Access nested attribute\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with nested property `metadata.version = \"1.0\"`\n+- **WHEN** the user accesses `entity@metadata.version`\n+- **THEN** the value `\"1.0\"` is returned\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: In-Memory Storage\n+\n+The system SHALL provide thread-safe in-memory storage for GTS entities in Phase 1.1.\n+\n+Storage SHALL:\n+- Support concurrent read/write access\n+- Maintain entity ordering by registration time\n+- Support efficient lookup by GTS ID\n+- Support efficient pattern-based queries","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-module/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"25a4db2e48c5155c97163bb1b926b771a8d18301","original_commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Accroding to InMemoryStorage representation (above) how we are going to search by pattern effectively? InMemoryStorage contains key/value structures only.","created_at":"2025-12-16T15:37:45Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T15:48:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2623794005","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623794005"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2623794005"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623794005/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":460,"original_line":358,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":358,"position":460,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623805747","pull_request_review_id":3583706882,"id":2623805747,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cZBkz","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,208 @@\n+# Design: Types Registry Module - Phase 1.1\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+HyperSpot requires a centralized GTS (Global Type System) registry to manage type definitions and instances across the platform. This enables:\n+- Cross-vendor type interoperability\n+- Schema validation for API payloads\n+- Fine-grained access control based on type identifiers\n+- Extensible plugin architectures\n+\n+Phase 1.1 focuses on establishing the foundational contracts and in-memory storage, deferring REST API (Phase 1.2) and database persistence (Phase 1.3) to later phases.\n+\n+**Stakeholders**: Platform developers, module authors, third-party integrators\n+\n+## Goals / Non-Goals\n+\n+### Goals\n+- Define SDK API trait for inter-module communication\n+- Implement in-memory storage for GTS entities\n+- Integrate gts-rust library for standard GTS operations (OP#1-OP#11)\n+- Follow HyperSpot module conventions (DDD-light, SDK pattern)\n+- Ensure thread-safe concurrent access\n+\n+### Non-Goals (Phase 1.1)\n+- REST API exposure (Phase 1.2)\n+- Database persistence (Phase 1.3)\n+- Tenant-level isolation (Phase 1.3)\n+- Dynamic provisioning via API (Phase 2)\n+- Event publishing on entity changes (Phase 2)\n+\n+## Decisions\n+\n+### 1. Use gts-rust as External Dependency\n+\n+**Decision**: Integrate the official [gts-rust](https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust) library for GTS operations.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Official reference implementation ensures spec compliance\n+- Provides all 11 GTS operations out of the box\n+- Maintained by the GTS specification authors\n+- Avoids reimplementing complex parsing/validation logic\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- Reimplement GTS operations in-house → Higher effort, risk of spec drift\n+- Use gts-go via FFI → Complexity, performance overhead\n+\n+### 2. SDK Pattern with Separate Crates\n+\n+**Decision**: Follow the standard HyperSpot SDK pattern with two crates:\n+- `types-registry-sdk`: Public API trait, models, errors\n+- `types-registry`: Module implementation\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Consistent with other HyperSpot modules\n+- Consumers only depend on lightweight SDK crate\n+- Clear separation of public API and implementation\n+\n+### 3. In-Memory Storage with DashMap\n+\n+**Decision**: Use `DashMap` for thread-safe in-memory storage.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Lock-free concurrent reads (common case)\n+- Fine-grained locking for writes\n+- Already used in HyperSpot (modkit patterns)\n+- Simple API, no async complexity\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- `RwLock<HashMap>` → Coarse-grained locking, potential contention\n+- `tokio::sync::RwLock` → Async overhead for simple operations\n+- SQLite in-memory → Overkill for Phase 1.1\n+\n+### 4. GTS Entity Model\n+\n+**Decision**: Define a unified `GtsEntity` model:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct GtsEntity {\n+    pub id: Uuid,              // Deterministic UUID from GTS ID (OP#5)\n+    pub gts_id: String,        // Full GTS identifier string\n+    pub kind: GtsEntityKind,   // Type or Instance\n+    pub content: serde_json::Value,  // JSON Schema or JSON object\n+    pub metadata: GtsEntityMetadata,\n+    pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+    pub updated_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum GtsEntityKind {\n+    Type,      // Schema definition (ends with ~)\n+    Instance,  // Object instance (no ~ suffix)\n+}\n+\n+pub struct GtsEntityMetadata {\n+    pub description: Option<String>,\n+    pub tags: Vec<String>,\n+    pub vendor: String,\n+    pub package: String,\n+    pub namespace: String,\n+    pub type_name: String,\n+    pub version_major: u32,\n+    pub version_minor: Option<u32>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Captures all GTS identifier components for efficient querying\n+- Stores content as `serde_json::Value` for flexibility\n+- Metadata extracted from GTS ID for filtering without parsing\n+\n+### 5. API Method Signatures\n+\n+**Decision**: All SDK API methods accept `&SecurityCtx` as first parameter:\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait TypesRegistryApi: Send + Sync {\n+    async fn register(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        entity: NewGtsEntity,\n+    ) -> Result<GtsEntity, TypesRegistryError>;\n+\n+    async fn list(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        query: ListQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Page<GtsEntity>, TypesRegistryError>;\n+\n+    async fn get(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        gts_id: &str,\n+    ) -> Result<GtsEntity, TypesRegistryError>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Consistent with HyperSpot conventions\n+- Enables future tenant isolation (Phase 1.3)\n+- Supports audit logging\n+\n+### 6. Optional Validation on Registration\n+\n+**Decision**: Support optional validation flag on registration:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct NewGtsEntity {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+    pub content: serde_json::Value,\n+    pub description: Option<String>,\n+    pub tags: Vec<String>,\n+    pub validate_references: bool,  // If true, validate x-gts-ref references\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Allows fast registration without validation for trusted sources\n+- Enables strict validation for untrusted input\n+- Matches gts-rust registry behavior\n+\n+## Data Model\n+\n+### Storage Structure\n+\n+```\n+InMemoryStorage {\n+    entities: DashMap<String, GtsEntity>,  // Key: GTS ID string\n+    by_uuid: DashMap<Uuid, String>,        // UUID → GTS ID lookup\n+    by_vendor: DashMap<String, HashSet<String>>,  // Vendor → GTS IDs index","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/design.md","commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","original_commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Dashmap is thread-safe but HashSet is not thread-safe. Need to double-check if it's ok for us.","created_at":"2025-12-16T15:41:26Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T15:48:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2623805747","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623805747"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2623805747"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623805747/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":169,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":169,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623814129","pull_request_review_id":3583706882,"id":2623814129,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cZDnx","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,208 @@\n+# Design: Types Registry Module - Phase 1.1\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+HyperSpot requires a centralized GTS (Global Type System) registry to manage type definitions and instances across the platform. This enables:\n+- Cross-vendor type interoperability\n+- Schema validation for API payloads\n+- Fine-grained access control based on type identifiers\n+- Extensible plugin architectures\n+\n+Phase 1.1 focuses on establishing the foundational contracts and in-memory storage, deferring REST API (Phase 1.2) and database persistence (Phase 1.3) to later phases.\n+\n+**Stakeholders**: Platform developers, module authors, third-party integrators\n+\n+## Goals / Non-Goals\n+\n+### Goals\n+- Define SDK API trait for inter-module communication\n+- Implement in-memory storage for GTS entities\n+- Integrate gts-rust library for standard GTS operations (OP#1-OP#11)\n+- Follow HyperSpot module conventions (DDD-light, SDK pattern)\n+- Ensure thread-safe concurrent access\n+\n+### Non-Goals (Phase 1.1)\n+- REST API exposure (Phase 1.2)\n+- Database persistence (Phase 1.3)\n+- Tenant-level isolation (Phase 1.3)\n+- Dynamic provisioning via API (Phase 2)\n+- Event publishing on entity changes (Phase 2)\n+\n+## Decisions\n+\n+### 1. Use gts-rust as External Dependency\n+\n+**Decision**: Integrate the official [gts-rust](https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust) library for GTS operations.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Official reference implementation ensures spec compliance\n+- Provides all 11 GTS operations out of the box\n+- Maintained by the GTS specification authors\n+- Avoids reimplementing complex parsing/validation logic\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- Reimplement GTS operations in-house → Higher effort, risk of spec drift\n+- Use gts-go via FFI → Complexity, performance overhead\n+\n+### 2. SDK Pattern with Separate Crates\n+\n+**Decision**: Follow the standard HyperSpot SDK pattern with two crates:\n+- `types-registry-sdk`: Public API trait, models, errors\n+- `types-registry`: Module implementation\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Consistent with other HyperSpot modules\n+- Consumers only depend on lightweight SDK crate\n+- Clear separation of public API and implementation\n+\n+### 3. In-Memory Storage with DashMap\n+\n+**Decision**: Use `DashMap` for thread-safe in-memory storage.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Lock-free concurrent reads (common case)\n+- Fine-grained locking for writes\n+- Already used in HyperSpot (modkit patterns)\n+- Simple API, no async complexity\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- `RwLock<HashMap>` → Coarse-grained locking, potential contention\n+- `tokio::sync::RwLock` → Async overhead for simple operations\n+- SQLite in-memory → Overkill for Phase 1.1\n+\n+### 4. GTS Entity Model\n+\n+**Decision**: Define a unified `GtsEntity` model:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct GtsEntity {\n+    pub id: Uuid,              // Deterministic UUID from GTS ID (OP#5)\n+    pub gts_id: String,        // Full GTS identifier string\n+    pub kind: GtsEntityKind,   // Type or Instance\n+    pub content: serde_json::Value,  // JSON Schema or JSON object","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/design.md","commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","original_commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Probably we shloud use enum here? like:\n```Rust\n#[serde(tag = \"kind\", content = \"content\")]\npub enum GtsContent {\n    Type {\n        schema: serde_json::Value, // JSON Schema\n    },\n    Instance {\n        object: serde_json::Value, // JSON Object\n    },\n}\n```","created_at":"2025-12-16T15:44:09Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T15:48:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2623814129","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623814129"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2623814129"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623814129/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":82,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":82,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623829878","pull_request_review_id":3583706882,"id":2623829878,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cZHd2","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,208 @@\n+# Design: Types Registry Module - Phase 1.1\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+HyperSpot requires a centralized GTS (Global Type System) registry to manage type definitions and instances across the platform. This enables:\n+- Cross-vendor type interoperability\n+- Schema validation for API payloads\n+- Fine-grained access control based on type identifiers\n+- Extensible plugin architectures\n+\n+Phase 1.1 focuses on establishing the foundational contracts and in-memory storage, deferring REST API (Phase 1.2) and database persistence (Phase 1.3) to later phases.\n+\n+**Stakeholders**: Platform developers, module authors, third-party integrators\n+\n+## Goals / Non-Goals\n+\n+### Goals\n+- Define SDK API trait for inter-module communication\n+- Implement in-memory storage for GTS entities\n+- Integrate gts-rust library for standard GTS operations (OP#1-OP#11)\n+- Follow HyperSpot module conventions (DDD-light, SDK pattern)\n+- Ensure thread-safe concurrent access\n+\n+### Non-Goals (Phase 1.1)\n+- REST API exposure (Phase 1.2)\n+- Database persistence (Phase 1.3)\n+- Tenant-level isolation (Phase 1.3)\n+- Dynamic provisioning via API (Phase 2)\n+- Event publishing on entity changes (Phase 2)\n+\n+## Decisions\n+\n+### 1. Use gts-rust as External Dependency\n+\n+**Decision**: Integrate the official [gts-rust](https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust) library for GTS operations.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Official reference implementation ensures spec compliance\n+- Provides all 11 GTS operations out of the box\n+- Maintained by the GTS specification authors\n+- Avoids reimplementing complex parsing/validation logic\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- Reimplement GTS operations in-house → Higher effort, risk of spec drift\n+- Use gts-go via FFI → Complexity, performance overhead\n+\n+### 2. SDK Pattern with Separate Crates\n+\n+**Decision**: Follow the standard HyperSpot SDK pattern with two crates:\n+- `types-registry-sdk`: Public API trait, models, errors\n+- `types-registry`: Module implementation\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Consistent with other HyperSpot modules\n+- Consumers only depend on lightweight SDK crate\n+- Clear separation of public API and implementation\n+\n+### 3. In-Memory Storage with DashMap\n+\n+**Decision**: Use `DashMap` for thread-safe in-memory storage.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Lock-free concurrent reads (common case)\n+- Fine-grained locking for writes\n+- Already used in HyperSpot (modkit patterns)\n+- Simple API, no async complexity\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- `RwLock<HashMap>` → Coarse-grained locking, potential contention\n+- `tokio::sync::RwLock` → Async overhead for simple operations\n+- SQLite in-memory → Overkill for Phase 1.1\n+\n+### 4. GTS Entity Model\n+\n+**Decision**: Define a unified `GtsEntity` model:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct GtsEntity {\n+    pub id: Uuid,              // Deterministic UUID from GTS ID (OP#5)\n+    pub gts_id: String,        // Full GTS identifier string\n+    pub kind: GtsEntityKind,   // Type or Instance\n+    pub content: serde_json::Value,  // JSON Schema or JSON object\n+    pub metadata: GtsEntityMetadata,\n+    pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+    pub updated_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum GtsEntityKind {\n+    Type,      // Schema definition (ends with ~)\n+    Instance,  // Object instance (no ~ suffix)\n+}\n+\n+pub struct GtsEntityMetadata {\n+    pub description: Option<String>,\n+    pub tags: Vec<String>,\n+    pub vendor: String,\n+    pub package: String,\n+    pub namespace: String,\n+    pub type_name: String,\n+    pub version_major: u32,\n+    pub version_minor: Option<u32>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Captures all GTS identifier components for efficient querying\n+- Stores content as `serde_json::Value` for flexibility\n+- Metadata extracted from GTS ID for filtering without parsing\n+\n+### 5. API Method Signatures\n+\n+**Decision**: All SDK API methods accept `&SecurityCtx` as first parameter:\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait TypesRegistryApi: Send + Sync {\n+    async fn register(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        entity: NewGtsEntity,\n+    ) -> Result<GtsEntity, TypesRegistryError>;\n+\n+    async fn list(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        query: ListQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Page<GtsEntity>, TypesRegistryError>;\n+\n+    async fn get(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        gts_id: &str,\n+    ) -> Result<GtsEntity, TypesRegistryError>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Consistent with HyperSpot conventions\n+- Enables future tenant isolation (Phase 1.3)\n+- Supports audit logging\n+\n+### 6. Optional Validation on Registration\n+\n+**Decision**: Support optional validation flag on registration:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct NewGtsEntity {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+    pub content: serde_json::Value,\n+    pub description: Option<String>,\n+    pub tags: Vec<String>,\n+    pub validate_references: bool,  // If true, validate x-gts-ref references\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Allows fast registration without validation for trusted sources\n+- Enables strict validation for untrusted input\n+- Matches gts-rust registry behavior\n+\n+## Data Model\n+\n+### Storage Structure\n+\n+```\n+InMemoryStorage {","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/design.md","commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","original_commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Look like for pattern matching we will do full scan of in-memory keys. It's ok for first version but need to address it somehow in document or in project issues.","created_at":"2025-12-16T15:48:52Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T15:48:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2623829878","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623829878"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2623829878"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623829878/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":166,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":166,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623882488","pull_request_review_id":3583861560,"id":2623882488,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cZUT4","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,208 @@\n+# Design: Types Registry Module - Phase 1.1\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+HyperSpot requires a centralized GTS (Global Type System) registry to manage type definitions and instances across the platform. This enables:\n+- Cross-vendor type interoperability\n+- Schema validation for API payloads\n+- Fine-grained access control based on type identifiers\n+- Extensible plugin architectures\n+\n+Phase 1.1 focuses on establishing the foundational contracts and in-memory storage, deferring REST API (Phase 1.2) and database persistence (Phase 1.3) to later phases.\n+\n+**Stakeholders**: Platform developers, module authors, third-party integrators\n+\n+## Goals / Non-Goals\n+\n+### Goals\n+- Define SDK API trait for inter-module communication\n+- Implement in-memory storage for GTS entities\n+- Integrate gts-rust library for standard GTS operations (OP#1-OP#11)\n+- Follow HyperSpot module conventions (DDD-light, SDK pattern)\n+- Ensure thread-safe concurrent access\n+\n+### Non-Goals (Phase 1.1)\n+- REST API exposure (Phase 1.2)\n+- Database persistence (Phase 1.3)\n+- Tenant-level isolation (Phase 1.3)\n+- Dynamic provisioning via API (Phase 2)\n+- Event publishing on entity changes (Phase 2)\n+\n+## Decisions\n+\n+### 1. Use gts-rust as External Dependency\n+\n+**Decision**: Integrate the official [gts-rust](https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust) library for GTS operations.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Official reference implementation ensures spec compliance\n+- Provides all 11 GTS operations out of the box\n+- Maintained by the GTS specification authors\n+- Avoids reimplementing complex parsing/validation logic\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- Reimplement GTS operations in-house → Higher effort, risk of spec drift\n+- Use gts-go via FFI → Complexity, performance overhead\n+\n+### 2. SDK Pattern with Separate Crates\n+\n+**Decision**: Follow the standard HyperSpot SDK pattern with two crates:\n+- `types-registry-sdk`: Public API trait, models, errors\n+- `types-registry`: Module implementation\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Consistent with other HyperSpot modules\n+- Consumers only depend on lightweight SDK crate\n+- Clear separation of public API and implementation\n+\n+### 3. In-Memory Storage with DashMap\n+\n+**Decision**: Use `DashMap` for thread-safe in-memory storage.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Lock-free concurrent reads (common case)\n+- Fine-grained locking for writes\n+- Already used in HyperSpot (modkit patterns)\n+- Simple API, no async complexity\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- `RwLock<HashMap>` → Coarse-grained locking, potential contention\n+- `tokio::sync::RwLock` → Async overhead for simple operations\n+- SQLite in-memory → Overkill for Phase 1.1\n+\n+### 4. GTS Entity Model\n+\n+**Decision**: Define a unified `GtsEntity` model:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct GtsEntity {\n+    pub id: Uuid,              // Deterministic UUID from GTS ID (OP#5)\n+    pub gts_id: String,        // Full GTS identifier string\n+    pub kind: GtsEntityKind,   // Type or Instance\n+    pub content: serde_json::Value,  // JSON Schema or JSON object\n+    pub metadata: GtsEntityMetadata,\n+    pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+    pub updated_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum GtsEntityKind {\n+    Type,      // Schema definition (ends with ~)\n+    Instance,  // Object instance (no ~ suffix)\n+}\n+\n+pub struct GtsEntityMetadata {\n+    pub description: Option<String>,\n+    pub tags: Vec<String>,\n+    pub vendor: String,\n+    pub package: String,\n+    pub namespace: String,\n+    pub type_name: String,\n+    pub version_major: u32,\n+    pub version_minor: Option<u32>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Captures all GTS identifier components for efficient querying\n+- Stores content as `serde_json::Value` for flexibility\n+- Metadata extracted from GTS ID for filtering without parsing\n+\n+### 5. API Method Signatures\n+\n+**Decision**: All SDK API methods accept `&SecurityCtx` as first parameter:\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait TypesRegistryApi: Send + Sync {\n+    async fn register(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        entity: NewGtsEntity,\n+    ) -> Result<GtsEntity, TypesRegistryError>;\n+\n+    async fn list(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        query: ListQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Page<GtsEntity>, TypesRegistryError>;\n+\n+    async fn get(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        gts_id: &str,\n+    ) -> Result<GtsEntity, TypesRegistryError>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Consistent with HyperSpot conventions\n+- Enables future tenant isolation (Phase 1.3)\n+- Supports audit logging\n+\n+### 6. Optional Validation on Registration\n+\n+**Decision**: Support optional validation flag on registration:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct NewGtsEntity {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+    pub content: serde_json::Value,\n+    pub description: Option<String>,\n+    pub tags: Vec<String>,\n+    pub validate_references: bool,  // If true, validate x-gts-ref references\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Allows fast registration without validation for trusted sources\n+- Enables strict validation for untrusted input\n+- Matches gts-rust registry behavior\n+\n+## Data Model\n+\n+### Storage Structure\n+\n+```\n+InMemoryStorage {","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/design.md","commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","original_commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"in phase 1.3 we'll have persistent db storage https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/issues/63","created_at":"2025-12-16T16:04:45Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T16:04:45Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2623882488","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623882488"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2623882488"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2623882488/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":166,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2623829878,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":166,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624385888","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624385888,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cbPNg","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to register GTS entities (types and instances) in the registry.\n+\n+A GTS entity consists of:\n+- **GTS ID**: A valid GTS identifier (e.g., `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1~` for types, `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1.0` for instances)\n+- **Kind**: Either `Type` (schema) or `Instance` (object)\n+- **Content**: JSON Schema for types, JSON object for instances\n+- **Metadata**: Optional metadata (description, tags, created_at, updated_at)\n+\n+Registration SHALL:\n+- Validate the GTS ID format using OP#1 (ID Validation)\n+- Extract and parse the GTS ID components using OP#3 (ID Parsing)\n+- Optionally validate GTS references within the content using OP#7 (Relationship Resolution)\n+- Generate a deterministic UUID from the GTS ID using OP#5 (ID to UUID Mapping)\n+- Store the entity in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register a type entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS type identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON Schema as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"generated deterministic UUID (Using OP#5), right?","created_at":"2025-12-16T18:53:15Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624385888","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624385888"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624385888"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624385888/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":27,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":27,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624389212","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624389212,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cbQBc","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to register GTS entities (types and instances) in the registry.\n+\n+A GTS entity consists of:\n+- **GTS ID**: A valid GTS identifier (e.g., `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1~` for types, `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1.0` for instances)","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"We should talk about well-known instances, not all possible instances","created_at":"2025-12-16T18:54:30Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624389212","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624389212"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624389212"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624389212/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":10,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":10,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624389966","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624389966,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cbQNO","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to register GTS entities (types and instances) in the registry.\n+\n+A GTS entity consists of:\n+- **GTS ID**: A valid GTS identifier (e.g., `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1~` for types, `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1.0` for instances)\n+- **Kind**: Either `Type` (schema) or `Instance` (object)\n+- **Content**: JSON Schema for types, JSON object for instances\n+- **Metadata**: Optional metadata (description, tags, created_at, updated_at)\n+\n+Registration SHALL:\n+- Validate the GTS ID format using OP#1 (ID Validation)\n+- Extract and parse the GTS ID components using OP#3 (ID Parsing)\n+- Optionally validate GTS references within the content using OP#7 (Relationship Resolution)\n+- Generate a deterministic UUID from the GTS ID using OP#5 (ID to UUID Mapping)\n+- Store the entity in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register a type entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS type identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON Schema as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register an instance entity successfully","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Register an instance entity successfully\n->\nRegister a well-known (named) instance entity successfully","created_at":"2025-12-16T18:54:48Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624389966","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624389966"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624389966"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624389966/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":30,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":30,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624406391","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624406391,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cbUN3","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to register GTS entities (types and instances) in the registry.\n+\n+A GTS entity consists of:\n+- **GTS ID**: A valid GTS identifier (e.g., `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1~` for types, `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1.0` for instances)\n+- **Kind**: Either `Type` (schema) or `Instance` (object)\n+- **Content**: JSON Schema for types, JSON object for instances\n+- **Metadata**: Optional metadata (description, tags, created_at, updated_at)\n+\n+Registration SHALL:\n+- Validate the GTS ID format using OP#1 (ID Validation)\n+- Extract and parse the GTS ID components using OP#3 (ID Parsing)\n+- Optionally validate GTS references within the content using OP#7 (Relationship Resolution)\n+- Generate a deterministic UUID from the GTS ID using OP#5 (ID to UUID Mapping)\n+- Store the entity in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register a type entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS type identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON Schema as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register an instance entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS instance identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON object as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid GTS ID format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an invalid GTS identifier `invalid-gts-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns a validation error with details about the invalid format\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate entity registration\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the same GTS ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a conflict error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Listing\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to list GTS entities with filtering and pagination support.\n+\n+Listing SHALL support:\n+- Filtering by GTS ID pattern using OP#4 (ID Pattern Matching) with wildcards\n+- Filtering by entity kind (Type, Instance, or both)\n+- Filtering by vendor, package, namespace, or type components","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-module/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"25a4db2e48c5155c97163bb1b926b771a8d18301","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"it's better to explain how it differs from wildcard, if I filter entities by vendor `globex`, than I should get something like this, that I can't get using wildcard:\n\n```\ngts.a.b.c.d.v1~globex.app.x.y.v1\ngts.k.l.m.n.v1~globex.app.a.b.v1\ngts.acme.x.y.z.v1~acme.a.b.c.v1~globex.app.a.b.v1\n```\n\nMake it makes sense to add as GTS OP#12 or so as separate PR\n\n","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:00:47Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624406391","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624406391"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624406391"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624406391/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":145,"original_line":59,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":59,"position":145,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624425792","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624425792,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cbY9A","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to register GTS entities (types and instances) in the registry.\n+\n+A GTS entity consists of:\n+- **GTS ID**: A valid GTS identifier (e.g., `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1~` for types, `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1.0` for instances)\n+- **Kind**: Either `Type` (schema) or `Instance` (object)\n+- **Content**: JSON Schema for types, JSON object for instances\n+- **Metadata**: Optional metadata (description, tags, created_at, updated_at)\n+\n+Registration SHALL:\n+- Validate the GTS ID format using OP#1 (ID Validation)\n+- Extract and parse the GTS ID components using OP#3 (ID Parsing)\n+- Optionally validate GTS references within the content using OP#7 (Relationship Resolution)\n+- Generate a deterministic UUID from the GTS ID using OP#5 (ID to UUID Mapping)\n+- Store the entity in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register a type entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS type identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON Schema as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register an instance entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS instance identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON object as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid GTS ID format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an invalid GTS identifier `invalid-gts-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns a validation error with details about the invalid format\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate entity registration\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the same GTS ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a conflict error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Listing\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to list GTS entities with filtering and pagination support.\n+\n+Listing SHALL support:\n+- Filtering by GTS ID pattern using OP#4 (ID Pattern Matching) with wildcards\n+- Filtering by entity kind (Type, Instance, or both)\n+- Filtering by vendor, package, namespace, or type components\n+- Cursor-based pagination with configurable limit\n+- Query execution using OP#10 (Query Execution)\n+\n+#### Scenario: List all entities with pagination\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains 100 GTS entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `limit=25`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the first 25 entities\n+- **AND** the response includes a cursor for the next page\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by wildcard pattern\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains entities from vendors `acme` and `globex`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only entities from vendor `acme`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by kind\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains both type and instance entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `kind=Type`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only type entities (ending with `~`)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return empty list when no matches\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains no entities matching pattern `gts.unknown.*`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with that pattern\n+- **THEN** the system returns an empty list with no error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Retrieval\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to retrieve a single GTS entity by its identifier.\n+\n+Retrieval SHALL:\n+- Accept a valid GTS ID\n+- Return the full entity including content and metadata\n+- Support attribute access using OP#11 (Attribute Access) with `@` selector\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity by exact ID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns the complete entity with content and metadata\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity attribute\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **AND** the entity has a property `name` with value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~@name`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return not found for non-existent entity\n+\n+- **GIVEN** no entity with GTS ID `gts.unknown.pkg.ns.type.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a not found error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Validation (OP#1)\n+\n+The system SHALL validate GTS identifier syntax according to the GTS specification.\n+\n+Valid GTS identifiers MUST:\n+- Start with `gts.` prefix\n+- Contain segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type`\n+- Include version: `v<MAJOR>` or `v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>`\n+- End with `~` for type identifiers, no suffix for instance identifiers\n+- Use only lowercase ASCII letters, digits, and underscores in segments\n+- Have segments starting with a letter or underscore\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as a type (schema)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct instance identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as an instance (object)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with invalid prefix\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `invalid.acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Invalid GTS prefix\"\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with uppercase characters\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.Acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Segments must be lowercase\"\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Parsing (OP#3)\n+\n+The system SHALL parse GTS identifiers into their constituent components.\n+\n+Parsing SHALL extract:\n+- `vendor`: The vendor/organization identifier\n+- `package`: The package/module identifier\n+- `namespace`: The namespace category (or `_` placeholder)\n+- `type_name`: The type name\n+- `version_major`: The major version number\n+- `version_minor`: The optional minor version number\n+- `is_type`: Whether the identifier represents a type (true) or instance (false)\n+- `segments`: For chained identifiers, all segments in order\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse simple type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains:\n+  - `vendor = \"acme\"`\n+  - `package = \"core\"`\n+  - `namespace = \"events\"`\n+  - `type_name = \"user_created\"`\n+  - `version_major = 1`\n+  - `version_minor = Some(2)`\n+  - `is_type = true`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse chained identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.x.core.events.event.v1~acme.app._.custom_event.v2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains 2 segments\n+- **AND** the first segment has vendor `x` and is a base type\n+- **AND** the second segment has vendor `acme` and is a derived type\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Pattern Matching (OP#4)\n+\n+The system SHALL match GTS identifiers against patterns containing wildcards.\n+\n+Pattern matching SHALL support:\n+- `*` wildcard matching any single segment\n+- `**` wildcard matching zero or more segments","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"No, it's not a part of spec (maybe it makes sense to improve the spec).\nIt says:\n\nhttps://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-spec?tab=readme-ov-file#10-collecting-identifiers-with-wildcards\n\n```\n## 10. Collecting Identifiers with Wildcards\n\n**Important:** An identifier containing a wildcard (`*`) is a **pattern for matching** and may not serve as a canonical identifier for a type or instance.\n\nA single wildcard (`*`) character can be used to find all identifiers matching a given prefix. The wildcard is a greedy operator that matches any sequence of characters after it, including the `~` chain separator.\n\n**Rules for using wildcards:**\n1. The wildcard (`*`) must be used only **once**.\n2. The wildcard must appear at the **end** of the pattern.\n3. The wildcard must not be used in combination with an attribute selector (`@`) or query (`[]`).\n4. The pattern must start at the beginning of a valid segment. For example, `gts.x.llm.chat.msg*` is invalid if `msg` is not a complete segment. `gts.x.llm.chat.message.v*` is valid because `v` is the start of the version segment.\n5. **Minor version semantics**: When a pattern specifies only a major version (e.g., `v0.*`), it matches candidates with any minor version of that major version (e.g., `v0.1~`, `v0.2~`, etc.). This is because the minor version is optional, and omitting it semantically means \"any minor version\".\n```","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:07:53Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624425792","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624425792"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624425792"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624425792/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":203,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":203,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624462981","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624462981,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cbiCF","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to register GTS entities (types and instances) in the registry.\n+\n+A GTS entity consists of:\n+- **GTS ID**: A valid GTS identifier (e.g., `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1~` for types, `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1.0` for instances)\n+- **Kind**: Either `Type` (schema) or `Instance` (object)\n+- **Content**: JSON Schema for types, JSON object for instances\n+- **Metadata**: Optional metadata (description, tags, created_at, updated_at)\n+\n+Registration SHALL:\n+- Validate the GTS ID format using OP#1 (ID Validation)\n+- Extract and parse the GTS ID components using OP#3 (ID Parsing)\n+- Optionally validate GTS references within the content using OP#7 (Relationship Resolution)\n+- Generate a deterministic UUID from the GTS ID using OP#5 (ID to UUID Mapping)\n+- Store the entity in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register a type entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS type identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON Schema as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register an instance entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS instance identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON object as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid GTS ID format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an invalid GTS identifier `invalid-gts-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns a validation error with details about the invalid format\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate entity registration\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the same GTS ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a conflict error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Listing\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to list GTS entities with filtering and pagination support.\n+\n+Listing SHALL support:\n+- Filtering by GTS ID pattern using OP#4 (ID Pattern Matching) with wildcards\n+- Filtering by entity kind (Type, Instance, or both)\n+- Filtering by vendor, package, namespace, or type components\n+- Cursor-based pagination with configurable limit\n+- Query execution using OP#10 (Query Execution)\n+\n+#### Scenario: List all entities with pagination\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains 100 GTS entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `limit=25`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the first 25 entities\n+- **AND** the response includes a cursor for the next page\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by wildcard pattern\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains entities from vendors `acme` and `globex`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only entities from vendor `acme`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by kind\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains both type and instance entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `kind=Type`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only type entities (ending with `~`)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return empty list when no matches\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains no entities matching pattern `gts.unknown.*`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with that pattern\n+- **THEN** the system returns an empty list with no error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Retrieval\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to retrieve a single GTS entity by its identifier.\n+\n+Retrieval SHALL:\n+- Accept a valid GTS ID\n+- Return the full entity including content and metadata\n+- Support attribute access using OP#11 (Attribute Access) with `@` selector\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity by exact ID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns the complete entity with content and metadata\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity attribute\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **AND** the entity has a property `name` with value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~@name`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return not found for non-existent entity\n+\n+- **GIVEN** no entity with GTS ID `gts.unknown.pkg.ns.type.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a not found error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Validation (OP#1)\n+\n+The system SHALL validate GTS identifier syntax according to the GTS specification.\n+\n+Valid GTS identifiers MUST:\n+- Start with `gts.` prefix\n+- Contain segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type`\n+- Include version: `v<MAJOR>` or `v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>`\n+- End with `~` for type identifiers, no suffix for instance identifiers\n+- Use only lowercase ASCII letters, digits, and underscores in segments\n+- Have segments starting with a letter or underscore\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as a type (schema)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct instance identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as an instance (object)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with invalid prefix\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `invalid.acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Invalid GTS prefix\"\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with uppercase characters\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.Acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Segments must be lowercase\"\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Parsing (OP#3)\n+\n+The system SHALL parse GTS identifiers into their constituent components.\n+\n+Parsing SHALL extract:\n+- `vendor`: The vendor/organization identifier\n+- `package`: The package/module identifier\n+- `namespace`: The namespace category (or `_` placeholder)\n+- `type_name`: The type name\n+- `version_major`: The major version number\n+- `version_minor`: The optional minor version number\n+- `is_type`: Whether the identifier represents a type (true) or instance (false)\n+- `segments`: For chained identifiers, all segments in order\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse simple type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains:\n+  - `vendor = \"acme\"`\n+  - `package = \"core\"`\n+  - `namespace = \"events\"`\n+  - `type_name = \"user_created\"`\n+  - `version_major = 1`\n+  - `version_minor = Some(2)`\n+  - `is_type = true`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse chained identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.x.core.events.event.v1~acme.app._.custom_event.v2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains 2 segments\n+- **AND** the first segment has vendor `x` and is a base type\n+- **AND** the second segment has vendor `acme` and is a derived type\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Pattern Matching (OP#4)\n+\n+The system SHALL match GTS identifiers against patterns containing wildcards.\n+\n+Pattern matching SHALL support:\n+- `*` wildcard matching any single segment\n+- `**` wildcard matching zero or more segments\n+- Exact segment matching\n+\n+#### Scenario: Match with single wildcard\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*.events.*`","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Double \"*\" is not acceptable by the spec","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:21:46Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624462981","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624462981"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624462981"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624462981/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":208,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":208,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624472295","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624472295,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cbkTn","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to register GTS entities (types and instances) in the registry.\n+\n+A GTS entity consists of:\n+- **GTS ID**: A valid GTS identifier (e.g., `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1~` for types, `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1.0` for instances)\n+- **Kind**: Either `Type` (schema) or `Instance` (object)\n+- **Content**: JSON Schema for types, JSON object for instances\n+- **Metadata**: Optional metadata (description, tags, created_at, updated_at)\n+\n+Registration SHALL:\n+- Validate the GTS ID format using OP#1 (ID Validation)\n+- Extract and parse the GTS ID components using OP#3 (ID Parsing)\n+- Optionally validate GTS references within the content using OP#7 (Relationship Resolution)\n+- Generate a deterministic UUID from the GTS ID using OP#5 (ID to UUID Mapping)\n+- Store the entity in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register a type entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS type identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON Schema as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register an instance entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS instance identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON object as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid GTS ID format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an invalid GTS identifier `invalid-gts-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns a validation error with details about the invalid format\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate entity registration\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the same GTS ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a conflict error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Listing\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to list GTS entities with filtering and pagination support.\n+\n+Listing SHALL support:\n+- Filtering by GTS ID pattern using OP#4 (ID Pattern Matching) with wildcards\n+- Filtering by entity kind (Type, Instance, or both)\n+- Filtering by vendor, package, namespace, or type components\n+- Cursor-based pagination with configurable limit\n+- Query execution using OP#10 (Query Execution)\n+\n+#### Scenario: List all entities with pagination\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains 100 GTS entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `limit=25`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the first 25 entities\n+- **AND** the response includes a cursor for the next page\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by wildcard pattern\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains entities from vendors `acme` and `globex`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only entities from vendor `acme`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by kind\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains both type and instance entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `kind=Type`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only type entities (ending with `~`)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return empty list when no matches\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains no entities matching pattern `gts.unknown.*`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with that pattern\n+- **THEN** the system returns an empty list with no error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Retrieval\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to retrieve a single GTS entity by its identifier.\n+\n+Retrieval SHALL:\n+- Accept a valid GTS ID\n+- Return the full entity including content and metadata\n+- Support attribute access using OP#11 (Attribute Access) with `@` selector\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity by exact ID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns the complete entity with content and metadata\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity attribute\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **AND** the entity has a property `name` with value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~@name`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return not found for non-existent entity\n+\n+- **GIVEN** no entity with GTS ID `gts.unknown.pkg.ns.type.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a not found error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Validation (OP#1)\n+\n+The system SHALL validate GTS identifier syntax according to the GTS specification.\n+\n+Valid GTS identifiers MUST:\n+- Start with `gts.` prefix\n+- Contain segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type`\n+- Include version: `v<MAJOR>` or `v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>`\n+- End with `~` for type identifiers, no suffix for instance identifiers\n+- Use only lowercase ASCII letters, digits, and underscores in segments\n+- Have segments starting with a letter or underscore\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as a type (schema)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct instance identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as an instance (object)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with invalid prefix\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `invalid.acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Invalid GTS prefix\"\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with uppercase characters\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.Acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Segments must be lowercase\"\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Parsing (OP#3)\n+\n+The system SHALL parse GTS identifiers into their constituent components.\n+\n+Parsing SHALL extract:\n+- `vendor`: The vendor/organization identifier\n+- `package`: The package/module identifier\n+- `namespace`: The namespace category (or `_` placeholder)\n+- `type_name`: The type name\n+- `version_major`: The major version number\n+- `version_minor`: The optional minor version number\n+- `is_type`: Whether the identifier represents a type (true) or instance (false)\n+- `segments`: For chained identifiers, all segments in order\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse simple type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains:\n+  - `vendor = \"acme\"`\n+  - `package = \"core\"`\n+  - `namespace = \"events\"`\n+  - `type_name = \"user_created\"`\n+  - `version_major = 1`\n+  - `version_minor = Some(2)`\n+  - `is_type = true`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse chained identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.x.core.events.event.v1~acme.app._.custom_event.v2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains 2 segments\n+- **AND** the first segment has vendor `x` and is a base type\n+- **AND** the second segment has vendor `acme` and is a derived type\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Pattern Matching (OP#4)\n+\n+The system SHALL match GTS identifiers against patterns containing wildcards.\n+\n+Pattern matching SHALL support:\n+- `*` wildcard matching any single segment\n+- `**` wildcard matching zero or more segments\n+- Exact segment matching\n+\n+#### Scenario: Match with single wildcard\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*.events.*`\n+- **AND** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system matches the identifier against the pattern\n+- **THEN** the match succeeds\n+\n+#### Scenario: No match with different vendor\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **AND** the identifier `gts.globex.core.events.order.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system matches the identifier against the pattern\n+- **THEN** the match fails\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID to UUID Mapping (OP#5)\n+\n+The system SHALL generate deterministic UUIDs from GTS identifiers.\n+\n+UUID generation SHALL:","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I would simply say it should invoke appropriate gts-rust method, not to re-invent it's own semantic","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:25:14Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624472295","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624472295"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624472295"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624472295/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":226,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":226,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624475023","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624475023,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cbk-P","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to register GTS entities (types and instances) in the registry.\n+\n+A GTS entity consists of:\n+- **GTS ID**: A valid GTS identifier (e.g., `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1~` for types, `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1.0` for instances)\n+- **Kind**: Either `Type` (schema) or `Instance` (object)\n+- **Content**: JSON Schema for types, JSON object for instances\n+- **Metadata**: Optional metadata (description, tags, created_at, updated_at)\n+\n+Registration SHALL:\n+- Validate the GTS ID format using OP#1 (ID Validation)\n+- Extract and parse the GTS ID components using OP#3 (ID Parsing)\n+- Optionally validate GTS references within the content using OP#7 (Relationship Resolution)\n+- Generate a deterministic UUID from the GTS ID using OP#5 (ID to UUID Mapping)\n+- Store the entity in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register a type entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS type identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON Schema as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register an instance entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS instance identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON object as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid GTS ID format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an invalid GTS identifier `invalid-gts-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns a validation error with details about the invalid format\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate entity registration\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the same GTS ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a conflict error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Listing\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to list GTS entities with filtering and pagination support.\n+\n+Listing SHALL support:\n+- Filtering by GTS ID pattern using OP#4 (ID Pattern Matching) with wildcards\n+- Filtering by entity kind (Type, Instance, or both)\n+- Filtering by vendor, package, namespace, or type components\n+- Cursor-based pagination with configurable limit\n+- Query execution using OP#10 (Query Execution)\n+\n+#### Scenario: List all entities with pagination\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains 100 GTS entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `limit=25`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the first 25 entities\n+- **AND** the response includes a cursor for the next page\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by wildcard pattern\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains entities from vendors `acme` and `globex`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only entities from vendor `acme`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by kind\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains both type and instance entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `kind=Type`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only type entities (ending with `~`)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return empty list when no matches\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains no entities matching pattern `gts.unknown.*`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with that pattern\n+- **THEN** the system returns an empty list with no error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Retrieval\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to retrieve a single GTS entity by its identifier.\n+\n+Retrieval SHALL:\n+- Accept a valid GTS ID\n+- Return the full entity including content and metadata\n+- Support attribute access using OP#11 (Attribute Access) with `@` selector\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity by exact ID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns the complete entity with content and metadata\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity attribute\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **AND** the entity has a property `name` with value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~@name`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return not found for non-existent entity\n+\n+- **GIVEN** no entity with GTS ID `gts.unknown.pkg.ns.type.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a not found error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Validation (OP#1)\n+\n+The system SHALL validate GTS identifier syntax according to the GTS specification.\n+\n+Valid GTS identifiers MUST:\n+- Start with `gts.` prefix\n+- Contain segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type`\n+- Include version: `v<MAJOR>` or `v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>`\n+- End with `~` for type identifiers, no suffix for instance identifiers\n+- Use only lowercase ASCII letters, digits, and underscores in segments\n+- Have segments starting with a letter or underscore\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as a type (schema)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct instance identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as an instance (object)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with invalid prefix\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `invalid.acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Invalid GTS prefix\"\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with uppercase characters\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.Acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Segments must be lowercase\"\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Parsing (OP#3)\n+\n+The system SHALL parse GTS identifiers into their constituent components.\n+\n+Parsing SHALL extract:\n+- `vendor`: The vendor/organization identifier\n+- `package`: The package/module identifier\n+- `namespace`: The namespace category (or `_` placeholder)\n+- `type_name`: The type name\n+- `version_major`: The major version number\n+- `version_minor`: The optional minor version number\n+- `is_type`: Whether the identifier represents a type (true) or instance (false)\n+- `segments`: For chained identifiers, all segments in order\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse simple type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains:\n+  - `vendor = \"acme\"`\n+  - `package = \"core\"`\n+  - `namespace = \"events\"`\n+  - `type_name = \"user_created\"`\n+  - `version_major = 1`\n+  - `version_minor = Some(2)`\n+  - `is_type = true`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse chained identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.x.core.events.event.v1~acme.app._.custom_event.v2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains 2 segments\n+- **AND** the first segment has vendor `x` and is a base type\n+- **AND** the second segment has vendor `acme` and is a derived type\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Pattern Matching (OP#4)\n+\n+The system SHALL match GTS identifiers against patterns containing wildcards.\n+\n+Pattern matching SHALL support:\n+- `*` wildcard matching any single segment\n+- `**` wildcard matching zero or more segments\n+- Exact segment matching\n+\n+#### Scenario: Match with single wildcard\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*.events.*`\n+- **AND** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system matches the identifier against the pattern\n+- **THEN** the match succeeds\n+\n+#### Scenario: No match with different vendor\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **AND** the identifier `gts.globex.core.events.order.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system matches the identifier against the pattern\n+- **THEN** the match fails\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID to UUID Mapping (OP#5)\n+\n+The system SHALL generate deterministic UUIDs from GTS identifiers.\n+\n+UUID generation SHALL:\n+- Produce the same UUID for the same GTS ID (deterministic)\n+- Use UUID v5 with a GTS-specific namespace\n+- Support scoping by major version (same UUID for v1.0 and v1.5)","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The gts-rust works differently, it converts the full name to UUID, not just major part, otherwise all the minor versions would have the same UUID that is wrong\n\nYou can see all the tests in the spec:\nhttps://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-spec/tree/main/tests","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:26:15Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624475023","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624475023"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624475023"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624475023/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":229,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":229,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624475893","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624475893,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cblL1","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to register GTS entities (types and instances) in the registry.\n+\n+A GTS entity consists of:\n+- **GTS ID**: A valid GTS identifier (e.g., `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1~` for types, `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1.0` for instances)\n+- **Kind**: Either `Type` (schema) or `Instance` (object)\n+- **Content**: JSON Schema for types, JSON object for instances\n+- **Metadata**: Optional metadata (description, tags, created_at, updated_at)\n+\n+Registration SHALL:\n+- Validate the GTS ID format using OP#1 (ID Validation)\n+- Extract and parse the GTS ID components using OP#3 (ID Parsing)\n+- Optionally validate GTS references within the content using OP#7 (Relationship Resolution)\n+- Generate a deterministic UUID from the GTS ID using OP#5 (ID to UUID Mapping)\n+- Store the entity in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register a type entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS type identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON Schema as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register an instance entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS instance identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON object as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid GTS ID format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an invalid GTS identifier `invalid-gts-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns a validation error with details about the invalid format\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate entity registration\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the same GTS ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a conflict error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Listing\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to list GTS entities with filtering and pagination support.\n+\n+Listing SHALL support:\n+- Filtering by GTS ID pattern using OP#4 (ID Pattern Matching) with wildcards\n+- Filtering by entity kind (Type, Instance, or both)\n+- Filtering by vendor, package, namespace, or type components\n+- Cursor-based pagination with configurable limit\n+- Query execution using OP#10 (Query Execution)\n+\n+#### Scenario: List all entities with pagination\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains 100 GTS entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `limit=25`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the first 25 entities\n+- **AND** the response includes a cursor for the next page\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by wildcard pattern\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains entities from vendors `acme` and `globex`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only entities from vendor `acme`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by kind\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains both type and instance entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `kind=Type`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only type entities (ending with `~`)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return empty list when no matches\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains no entities matching pattern `gts.unknown.*`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with that pattern\n+- **THEN** the system returns an empty list with no error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Retrieval\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to retrieve a single GTS entity by its identifier.\n+\n+Retrieval SHALL:\n+- Accept a valid GTS ID\n+- Return the full entity including content and metadata\n+- Support attribute access using OP#11 (Attribute Access) with `@` selector\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity by exact ID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns the complete entity with content and metadata\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity attribute\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **AND** the entity has a property `name` with value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~@name`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return not found for non-existent entity\n+\n+- **GIVEN** no entity with GTS ID `gts.unknown.pkg.ns.type.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a not found error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Validation (OP#1)\n+\n+The system SHALL validate GTS identifier syntax according to the GTS specification.\n+\n+Valid GTS identifiers MUST:\n+- Start with `gts.` prefix\n+- Contain segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type`\n+- Include version: `v<MAJOR>` or `v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>`\n+- End with `~` for type identifiers, no suffix for instance identifiers\n+- Use only lowercase ASCII letters, digits, and underscores in segments\n+- Have segments starting with a letter or underscore\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as a type (schema)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct instance identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as an instance (object)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with invalid prefix\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `invalid.acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Invalid GTS prefix\"\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with uppercase characters\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.Acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Segments must be lowercase\"\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Parsing (OP#3)\n+\n+The system SHALL parse GTS identifiers into their constituent components.\n+\n+Parsing SHALL extract:\n+- `vendor`: The vendor/organization identifier\n+- `package`: The package/module identifier\n+- `namespace`: The namespace category (or `_` placeholder)\n+- `type_name`: The type name\n+- `version_major`: The major version number\n+- `version_minor`: The optional minor version number\n+- `is_type`: Whether the identifier represents a type (true) or instance (false)\n+- `segments`: For chained identifiers, all segments in order\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse simple type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains:\n+  - `vendor = \"acme\"`\n+  - `package = \"core\"`\n+  - `namespace = \"events\"`\n+  - `type_name = \"user_created\"`\n+  - `version_major = 1`\n+  - `version_minor = Some(2)`\n+  - `is_type = true`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse chained identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.x.core.events.event.v1~acme.app._.custom_event.v2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains 2 segments\n+- **AND** the first segment has vendor `x` and is a base type\n+- **AND** the second segment has vendor `acme` and is a derived type\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Pattern Matching (OP#4)\n+\n+The system SHALL match GTS identifiers against patterns containing wildcards.\n+\n+Pattern matching SHALL support:\n+- `*` wildcard matching any single segment\n+- `**` wildcard matching zero or more segments\n+- Exact segment matching\n+\n+#### Scenario: Match with single wildcard\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*.events.*`\n+- **AND** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system matches the identifier against the pattern\n+- **THEN** the match succeeds\n+\n+#### Scenario: No match with different vendor\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **AND** the identifier `gts.globex.core.events.order.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system matches the identifier against the pattern\n+- **THEN** the match fails\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID to UUID Mapping (OP#5)\n+\n+The system SHALL generate deterministic UUIDs from GTS identifiers.\n+\n+UUID generation SHALL:\n+- Produce the same UUID for the same GTS ID (deterministic)\n+- Use UUID v5 with a GTS-specific namespace\n+- Support scoping by major version (same UUID for v1.0 and v1.5)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Generate deterministic UUID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system generates a UUID twice\n+- **THEN** both UUIDs are identical\n+\n+#### Scenario: Same major version produces same UUID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifiers `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0` and `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.5`","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"No, it doesn't match the reference implementation in gts-rust","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:26:34Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624475893","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624475893"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624475893"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624475893/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":239,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":239,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624494041","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624494041,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cbpnZ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-module/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"25a4db2e48c5155c97163bb1b926b771a8d18301","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think that we can simplify everything for now and have our stable GtsEntity struct's for contracts and then map what gts-spec returns to own own GtsEntity stable format, not to be completely dependent on gts-rust\n\nAlso, some GTS operations described here are very different from what is already implemented in:\nhttps://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust\n\nand covered by spec tests:\nhttps://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-spec/tree/main/tests\n\n... I left the comments in the places I found it\n\nIf something is missing, we can add new OP# and new tests to the spec (e.g. get GTS IDs by vendor, app, namespace, type)","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:33:19Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T20:00:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624494041","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624494041"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624494041"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624494041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624505407","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624505407,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cbsY_","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to register GTS entities (types and instances) in the registry.\n+\n+A GTS entity consists of:\n+- **GTS ID**: A valid GTS identifier (e.g., `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1~` for types, `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1.0` for instances)\n+- **Kind**: Either `Type` (schema) or `Instance` (object)\n+- **Content**: JSON Schema for types, JSON object for instances\n+- **Metadata**: Optional metadata (description, tags, created_at, updated_at)\n+\n+Registration SHALL:\n+- Validate the GTS ID format using OP#1 (ID Validation)\n+- Extract and parse the GTS ID components using OP#3 (ID Parsing)\n+- Optionally validate GTS references within the content using OP#7 (Relationship Resolution)\n+- Generate a deterministic UUID from the GTS ID using OP#5 (ID to UUID Mapping)\n+- Store the entity in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register a type entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS type identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON Schema as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register an instance entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS instance identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON object as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid GTS ID format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an invalid GTS identifier `invalid-gts-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns a validation error with details about the invalid format\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate entity registration\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the same GTS ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a conflict error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Listing\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to list GTS entities with filtering and pagination support.\n+\n+Listing SHALL support:\n+- Filtering by GTS ID pattern using OP#4 (ID Pattern Matching) with wildcards\n+- Filtering by entity kind (Type, Instance, or both)\n+- Filtering by vendor, package, namespace, or type components\n+- Cursor-based pagination with configurable limit\n+- Query execution using OP#10 (Query Execution)\n+\n+#### Scenario: List all entities with pagination\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains 100 GTS entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `limit=25`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the first 25 entities\n+- **AND** the response includes a cursor for the next page\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by wildcard pattern\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains entities from vendors `acme` and `globex`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only entities from vendor `acme`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by kind\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains both type and instance entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `kind=Type`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only type entities (ending with `~`)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return empty list when no matches\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains no entities matching pattern `gts.unknown.*`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with that pattern\n+- **THEN** the system returns an empty list with no error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Retrieval\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to retrieve a single GTS entity by its identifier.\n+\n+Retrieval SHALL:\n+- Accept a valid GTS ID\n+- Return the full entity including content and metadata\n+- Support attribute access using OP#11 (Attribute Access) with `@` selector\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity by exact ID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns the complete entity with content and metadata\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity attribute\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **AND** the entity has a property `name` with value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~@name`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return not found for non-existent entity\n+\n+- **GIVEN** no entity with GTS ID `gts.unknown.pkg.ns.type.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a not found error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Validation (OP#1)\n+\n+The system SHALL validate GTS identifier syntax according to the GTS specification.\n+\n+Valid GTS identifiers MUST:\n+- Start with `gts.` prefix\n+- Contain segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type`\n+- Include version: `v<MAJOR>` or `v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>`\n+- End with `~` for type identifiers, no suffix for instance identifiers\n+- Use only lowercase ASCII letters, digits, and underscores in segments\n+- Have segments starting with a letter or underscore\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as a type (schema)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct instance identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as an instance (object)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with invalid prefix\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `invalid.acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Invalid GTS prefix\"\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with uppercase characters\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.Acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Segments must be lowercase\"\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Parsing (OP#3)\n+\n+The system SHALL parse GTS identifiers into their constituent components.\n+\n+Parsing SHALL extract:\n+- `vendor`: The vendor/organization identifier\n+- `package`: The package/module identifier\n+- `namespace`: The namespace category (or `_` placeholder)\n+- `type_name`: The type name\n+- `version_major`: The major version number\n+- `version_minor`: The optional minor version number\n+- `is_type`: Whether the identifier represents a type (true) or instance (false)\n+- `segments`: For chained identifiers, all segments in order\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse simple type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains:\n+  - `vendor = \"acme\"`\n+  - `package = \"core\"`\n+  - `namespace = \"events\"`\n+  - `type_name = \"user_created\"`\n+  - `version_major = 1`\n+  - `version_minor = Some(2)`\n+  - `is_type = true`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse chained identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.x.core.events.event.v1~acme.app._.custom_event.v2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains 2 segments\n+- **AND** the first segment has vendor `x` and is a base type\n+- **AND** the second segment has vendor `acme` and is a derived type\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Pattern Matching (OP#4)\n+\n+The system SHALL match GTS identifiers against patterns containing wildcards.\n+\n+Pattern matching SHALL support:\n+- `*` wildcard matching any single segment\n+- `**` wildcard matching zero or more segments\n+- Exact segment matching\n+\n+#### Scenario: Match with single wildcard\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*.events.*`\n+- **AND** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system matches the identifier against the pattern\n+- **THEN** the match succeeds\n+\n+#### Scenario: No match with different vendor\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **AND** the identifier `gts.globex.core.events.order.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system matches the identifier against the pattern\n+- **THEN** the match fails\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID to UUID Mapping (OP#5)\n+\n+The system SHALL generate deterministic UUIDs from GTS identifiers.\n+\n+UUID generation SHALL:\n+- Produce the same UUID for the same GTS ID (deterministic)\n+- Use UUID v5 with a GTS-specific namespace\n+- Support scoping by major version (same UUID for v1.0 and v1.5)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Generate deterministic UUID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system generates a UUID twice\n+- **THEN** both UUIDs are identical\n+\n+#### Scenario: Same major version produces same UUID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifiers `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0` and `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.5`\n+- **WHEN** the system generates UUIDs with major scope\n+- **THEN** both UUIDs are identical\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Schema Validation (OP#6)\n+\n+The system SHALL validate JSON object instances against their corresponding JSON Schema types.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate instance against schema\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` with JSON Schema requiring `userId` field\n+- **AND** an instance `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0` with `userId` field\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the instance\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid instance\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` with JSON Schema requiring `userId` field\n+- **AND** an instance missing the `userId` field\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the instance\n+- **THEN** validation fails with details about the missing field\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Relationship Resolution (OP#7)\n+\n+The system SHALL resolve inter-dependencies between GTS entities and detect broken references.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Resolve valid references\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type that references another registered type via `x-gts-ref`\n+- **WHEN** the system resolves relationships\n+- **THEN** all references are resolved successfully\n+\n+#### Scenario: Detect broken reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type that references a non-existent type `gts.unknown.pkg.ns.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system resolves relationships\n+- **THEN** the system reports the broken reference\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Compatibility Checking (OP#8)\n+\n+The system SHALL verify schema compatibility between different MINOR versions.\n+\n+Compatibility modes:\n+- **Backward**: Old instances work with new schema\n+- **Forward**: New instances work with old schema\n+- **Full**: Both backward and forward compatible\n+\n+#### Scenario: Check backward compatibility\n+\n+- **GIVEN** schema v1.0 and schema v1.1 where v1.1 adds an optional field\n+- **WHEN** the system checks backward compatibility\n+- **THEN** the schemas are backward compatible\n+\n+#### Scenario: Detect backward incompatibility\n+\n+- **GIVEN** schema v1.0 and schema v1.1 where v1.1 removes a required field\n+- **WHEN** the system checks backward compatibility\n+- **THEN** the schemas are NOT backward compatible\n+- **AND** the system reports the incompatibility reason\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Version Casting (OP#9)\n+\n+The system SHALL transform instances between compatible MINOR versions.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Cast instance to newer version\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an instance conforming to v1.0\n+- **AND** v1.1 adds an optional field with default value\n+- **WHEN** the system casts the instance to v1.1\n+- **THEN** the casted instance includes the new field with default value\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Query Execution (OP#10)\n+\n+The system SHALL filter identifier collections using the GTS query language.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query with attribute filter\n+\n+- **GIVEN** entities with various `status` values\n+- **WHEN** the user queries `gts.acme.core.*[status=active]`","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This example (wildcard + query) is not specified in the spec, but I think it can be quite misleading and return very different types, e.g. events with .status = active and subscriptions and users, etc. Doesn't make much sense I believe","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:37:29Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624505407","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624505407"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624505407"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624505407/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":327,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":327,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624524232","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624524232,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cbw_I","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,240 @@\n+# Design: Types Registry Module - Phase 1.1\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+HyperSpot requires a centralized GTS (Global Type System) registry to manage type definitions and instances across the platform. This enables:\n+- Cross-vendor type interoperability\n+- Schema validation for API payloads\n+- Fine-grained access control based on type identifiers\n+- Extensible plugin architectures\n+\n+Phase 1.1 focuses on establishing the foundational contracts and in-memory storage, deferring REST API (Phase 1.2) and database persistence (Phase 1.3) to later phases.\n+\n+**Reference Implementation**: `examples/modkit/users_info` — follow this structure for SDK pattern, module layout, and ClientHub integration.\n+\n+**Stakeholders**: Platform developers, module authors, third-party integrators\n+\n+## Goals / Non-Goals\n+\n+### Goals\n+- Define SDK API trait for inter-module communication\n+- Implement in-memory storage for GTS entities\n+- Integrate gts-rust library for standard GTS operations (OP#1-OP#11)\n+- Follow HyperSpot module conventions (DDD-light, SDK pattern)\n+- Ensure thread-safe concurrent access","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/design.md","commit_id":"cfa6c0b8b81fbcc2832868ce86ff5f6a0a7ceadb","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implement unit tests with 95% code coverage as it's critical component","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:44:09Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624524232","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624524232"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624524232"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624524232/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":24,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":24,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624540689","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624540689,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cb1AR","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,240 @@\n+# Design: Types Registry Module - Phase 1.1\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+HyperSpot requires a centralized GTS (Global Type System) registry to manage type definitions and instances across the platform. This enables:\n+- Cross-vendor type interoperability\n+- Schema validation for API payloads\n+- Fine-grained access control based on type identifiers\n+- Extensible plugin architectures\n+\n+Phase 1.1 focuses on establishing the foundational contracts and in-memory storage, deferring REST API (Phase 1.2) and database persistence (Phase 1.3) to later phases.\n+\n+**Reference Implementation**: `examples/modkit/users_info` — follow this structure for SDK pattern, module layout, and ClientHub integration.\n+\n+**Stakeholders**: Platform developers, module authors, third-party integrators\n+\n+## Goals / Non-Goals\n+\n+### Goals\n+- Define SDK API trait for inter-module communication\n+- Implement in-memory storage for GTS entities\n+- Integrate gts-rust library for standard GTS operations (OP#1-OP#11)\n+- Follow HyperSpot module conventions (DDD-light, SDK pattern)\n+- Ensure thread-safe concurrent access\n+\n+### Non-Goals (Phase 1.1)\n+- REST API exposure (Phase 1.2)\n+- Database persistence (Phase 1.3)\n+- Tenant-level isolation (Phase 1.3)\n+- Dynamic provisioning via API (Phase 2)\n+- Event publishing on entity changes (Phase 2)\n+\n+## Decisions\n+\n+### 1. Use gts-rust as External Dependency\n+\n+**Decision**: Integrate the official [gts-rust](https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust) library for GTS operations.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Official reference implementation ensures spec compliance\n+- Provides all 11 GTS operations out of the box\n+- Maintained by the GTS specification authors\n+- Avoids reimplementing complex parsing/validation logic\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- Reimplement GTS operations in-house → Higher effort, risk of spec drift\n+- Use gts-go via FFI → Complexity, performance overhead\n+\n+### 2. SDK Pattern with Separate Crates\n+\n+**Decision**: Follow the standard HyperSpot SDK pattern with two crates (mirroring `examples/modkit/users_info`):\n+\n+**SDK Crate (`types-registry-sdk/`):**\n+```\n+types-registry-sdk/\n+├── Cargo.toml\n+└── src/\n+    ├── lib.rs          # Re-exports: TypesRegistryApi, models, errors\n+    ├── api.rs          # TypesRegistryApi trait definition\n+    ├── models.rs       # GtsEntity, NewGtsEntity, GtsEntityKind, etc.\n+    └── errors.rs       # TypesRegistryError enum\n+```\n+\n+**Module Crate (`types-registry/`):**\n+```\n+types-registry/\n+├── Cargo.toml\n+└── src/\n+    ├── lib.rs              # Re-exports SDK + module\n+    ├── module.rs           # #[modkit::module] declaration\n+    ├── local_client.rs     # TypesRegistryLocalClient implements SDK trait\n+    ├── config.rs           # TypesRegistryConfig\n+    ├── domain/\n+    │   ├── mod.rs\n+    │   ├── service.rs      # Domain service with business logic\n+    │   ├── error.rs        # DomainError\n+    │   ├── repo.rs         # GtsRepository trait (port)\n+    │   └── ports/          # Output ports (EventPublisher, etc.)\n+    └── infra/\n+        └── storage/\n+            └── in_memory_repo.rs  # In-memory repository implementation\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Consistent with `users_info` example and other HyperSpot modules\n+- Consumers only depend on lightweight SDK crate\n+- Clear separation of public API and implementation\n+- DDD-light structure with ports/adapters\n+\n+### 3. In-Memory Storage with DashMap\n+\n+**Decision**: Use `DashMap` for thread-safe in-memory storage.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Lock-free concurrent reads (common case)\n+- Fine-grained locking for writes\n+- Already used in HyperSpot (modkit patterns)\n+- Simple API, no async complexity\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- `RwLock<HashMap>` → Coarse-grained locking, potential contention\n+- `tokio::sync::RwLock` → Async overhead for simple operations\n+- SQLite in-memory → Overkill for Phase 1.1\n+\n+### 4. GTS Entity Model\n+\n+**Decision**: Define a unified `GtsEntity` model:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct GtsEntity {","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/design.md","commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Let's agree on how you are going to use this GtsEntity:\n\nI'd expect to reuse (or refer) gts-rust::GtsEntity and the whole it's cache, and have separate hashmap with metadata objects for GTS UUID.Later, when you have a DB, you will just populate this cache from DB\n\nThen you can map that gts-rust::GtsEntity to your interface GtsEntity\n\nIs that correct assumption?\n","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:50:29Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624540689","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624540689"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624540689"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624540689/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":110,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":110,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624541804","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624541804,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cb1Rs","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,240 @@\n+# Design: Types Registry Module - Phase 1.1\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+HyperSpot requires a centralized GTS (Global Type System) registry to manage type definitions and instances across the platform. This enables:\n+- Cross-vendor type interoperability\n+- Schema validation for API payloads\n+- Fine-grained access control based on type identifiers\n+- Extensible plugin architectures\n+\n+Phase 1.1 focuses on establishing the foundational contracts and in-memory storage, deferring REST API (Phase 1.2) and database persistence (Phase 1.3) to later phases.\n+\n+**Reference Implementation**: `examples/modkit/users_info` — follow this structure for SDK pattern, module layout, and ClientHub integration.\n+\n+**Stakeholders**: Platform developers, module authors, third-party integrators\n+\n+## Goals / Non-Goals\n+\n+### Goals\n+- Define SDK API trait for inter-module communication\n+- Implement in-memory storage for GTS entities\n+- Integrate gts-rust library for standard GTS operations (OP#1-OP#11)\n+- Follow HyperSpot module conventions (DDD-light, SDK pattern)\n+- Ensure thread-safe concurrent access\n+\n+### Non-Goals (Phase 1.1)\n+- REST API exposure (Phase 1.2)\n+- Database persistence (Phase 1.3)\n+- Tenant-level isolation (Phase 1.3)\n+- Dynamic provisioning via API (Phase 2)\n+- Event publishing on entity changes (Phase 2)\n+\n+## Decisions\n+\n+### 1. Use gts-rust as External Dependency\n+\n+**Decision**: Integrate the official [gts-rust](https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust) library for GTS operations.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Official reference implementation ensures spec compliance\n+- Provides all 11 GTS operations out of the box\n+- Maintained by the GTS specification authors\n+- Avoids reimplementing complex parsing/validation logic\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- Reimplement GTS operations in-house → Higher effort, risk of spec drift\n+- Use gts-go via FFI → Complexity, performance overhead\n+\n+### 2. SDK Pattern with Separate Crates\n+\n+**Decision**: Follow the standard HyperSpot SDK pattern with two crates (mirroring `examples/modkit/users_info`):\n+\n+**SDK Crate (`types-registry-sdk/`):**\n+```\n+types-registry-sdk/\n+├── Cargo.toml\n+└── src/\n+    ├── lib.rs          # Re-exports: TypesRegistryApi, models, errors\n+    ├── api.rs          # TypesRegistryApi trait definition\n+    ├── models.rs       # GtsEntity, NewGtsEntity, GtsEntityKind, etc.\n+    └── errors.rs       # TypesRegistryError enum\n+```\n+\n+**Module Crate (`types-registry/`):**\n+```\n+types-registry/\n+├── Cargo.toml\n+└── src/\n+    ├── lib.rs              # Re-exports SDK + module\n+    ├── module.rs           # #[modkit::module] declaration\n+    ├── local_client.rs     # TypesRegistryLocalClient implements SDK trait\n+    ├── config.rs           # TypesRegistryConfig\n+    ├── domain/\n+    │   ├── mod.rs\n+    │   ├── service.rs      # Domain service with business logic\n+    │   ├── error.rs        # DomainError\n+    │   ├── repo.rs         # GtsRepository trait (port)\n+    │   └── ports/          # Output ports (EventPublisher, etc.)\n+    └── infra/\n+        └── storage/\n+            └── in_memory_repo.rs  # In-memory repository implementation\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Consistent with `users_info` example and other HyperSpot modules\n+- Consumers only depend on lightweight SDK crate\n+- Clear separation of public API and implementation\n+- DDD-light structure with ports/adapters\n+\n+### 3. In-Memory Storage with DashMap\n+\n+**Decision**: Use `DashMap` for thread-safe in-memory storage.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Lock-free concurrent reads (common case)\n+- Fine-grained locking for writes\n+- Already used in HyperSpot (modkit patterns)\n+- Simple API, no async complexity\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- `RwLock<HashMap>` → Coarse-grained locking, potential contention\n+- `tokio::sync::RwLock` → Async overhead for simple operations\n+- SQLite in-memory → Overkill for Phase 1.1\n+\n+### 4. GTS Entity Model\n+\n+**Decision**: Define a unified `GtsEntity` model:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct GtsEntity {\n+    pub id: Uuid,              // Deterministic UUID from GTS ID (OP#5)\n+    pub gts_id: String,        // Full GTS identifier string\n+    pub kind: GtsEntityKind,   // Type or Instance\n+    pub content: serde_json::Value,  // JSON Schema or JSON object\n+    pub metadata: GtsEntityMetadata,\n+    pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+    pub updated_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum GtsEntityKind {\n+    Type,      // Schema definition (ends with ~)\n+    Instance,  // Object instance (no ~ suffix)\n+}\n+\n+pub struct GtsEntityMetadata {","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/design.md","commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","original_commit_id":"46e8a4dfd4bfff935f0e6d84606bd0a5d6a837f9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"again, is it going to be just an interface or main data storage type?","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:50:55Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624541804","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624541804"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624541804"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624541804/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":125,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":125,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624554559","pull_request_review_id":3584528413,"id":2624554559,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6cb4Y_","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,208 @@\n+# Design: Types Registry Module - Phase 1.1\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+HyperSpot requires a centralized GTS (Global Type System) registry to manage type definitions and instances across the platform. This enables:\n+- Cross-vendor type interoperability\n+- Schema validation for API payloads\n+- Fine-grained access control based on type identifiers\n+- Extensible plugin architectures\n+\n+Phase 1.1 focuses on establishing the foundational contracts and in-memory storage, deferring REST API (Phase 1.2) and database persistence (Phase 1.3) to later phases.\n+\n+**Stakeholders**: Platform developers, module authors, third-party integrators\n+\n+## Goals / Non-Goals\n+\n+### Goals\n+- Define SDK API trait for inter-module communication\n+- Implement in-memory storage for GTS entities\n+- Integrate gts-rust library for standard GTS operations (OP#1-OP#11)\n+- Follow HyperSpot module conventions (DDD-light, SDK pattern)\n+- Ensure thread-safe concurrent access\n+\n+### Non-Goals (Phase 1.1)\n+- REST API exposure (Phase 1.2)\n+- Database persistence (Phase 1.3)\n+- Tenant-level isolation (Phase 1.3)\n+- Dynamic provisioning via API (Phase 2)\n+- Event publishing on entity changes (Phase 2)\n+\n+## Decisions\n+\n+### 1. Use gts-rust as External Dependency\n+\n+**Decision**: Integrate the official [gts-rust](https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust) library for GTS operations.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Official reference implementation ensures spec compliance\n+- Provides all 11 GTS operations out of the box\n+- Maintained by the GTS specification authors\n+- Avoids reimplementing complex parsing/validation logic\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- Reimplement GTS operations in-house → Higher effort, risk of spec drift\n+- Use gts-go via FFI → Complexity, performance overhead\n+\n+### 2. SDK Pattern with Separate Crates\n+\n+**Decision**: Follow the standard HyperSpot SDK pattern with two crates:\n+- `types-registry-sdk`: Public API trait, models, errors\n+- `types-registry`: Module implementation\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Consistent with other HyperSpot modules\n+- Consumers only depend on lightweight SDK crate\n+- Clear separation of public API and implementation\n+\n+### 3. In-Memory Storage with DashMap\n+\n+**Decision**: Use `DashMap` for thread-safe in-memory storage.\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Lock-free concurrent reads (common case)\n+- Fine-grained locking for writes\n+- Already used in HyperSpot (modkit patterns)\n+- Simple API, no async complexity\n+\n+**Alternatives considered**:\n+- `RwLock<HashMap>` → Coarse-grained locking, potential contention\n+- `tokio::sync::RwLock` → Async overhead for simple operations\n+- SQLite in-memory → Overkill for Phase 1.1\n+\n+### 4. GTS Entity Model\n+\n+**Decision**: Define a unified `GtsEntity` model:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct GtsEntity {\n+    pub id: Uuid,              // Deterministic UUID from GTS ID (OP#5)\n+    pub gts_id: String,        // Full GTS identifier string\n+    pub kind: GtsEntityKind,   // Type or Instance\n+    pub content: serde_json::Value,  // JSON Schema or JSON object\n+    pub metadata: GtsEntityMetadata,\n+    pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+    pub updated_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum GtsEntityKind {\n+    Type,      // Schema definition (ends with ~)\n+    Instance,  // Object instance (no ~ suffix)\n+}\n+\n+pub struct GtsEntityMetadata {\n+    pub description: Option<String>,\n+    pub tags: Vec<String>,\n+    pub vendor: String,\n+    pub package: String,\n+    pub namespace: String,\n+    pub type_name: String,\n+    pub version_major: u32,\n+    pub version_minor: Option<u32>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Captures all GTS identifier components for efficient querying\n+- Stores content as `serde_json::Value` for flexibility\n+- Metadata extracted from GTS ID for filtering without parsing\n+\n+### 5. API Method Signatures\n+\n+**Decision**: All SDK API methods accept `&SecurityCtx` as first parameter:\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait TypesRegistryApi: Send + Sync {\n+    async fn register(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        entity: NewGtsEntity,\n+    ) -> Result<GtsEntity, TypesRegistryError>;\n+\n+    async fn list(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        query: ListQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Page<GtsEntity>, TypesRegistryError>;\n+\n+    async fn get(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        gts_id: &str,\n+    ) -> Result<GtsEntity, TypesRegistryError>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Consistent with HyperSpot conventions\n+- Enables future tenant isolation (Phase 1.3)\n+- Supports audit logging\n+\n+### 6. Optional Validation on Registration\n+\n+**Decision**: Support optional validation flag on registration:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct NewGtsEntity {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+    pub content: serde_json::Value,\n+    pub description: Option<String>,\n+    pub tags: Vec<String>,\n+    pub validate_references: bool,  // If true, validate x-gts-ref references\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Rationale**:\n+- Allows fast registration without validation for trusted sources\n+- Enables strict validation for untrusted input\n+- Matches gts-rust registry behavior\n+\n+## Data Model\n+\n+### Storage Structure\n+\n+```\n+InMemoryStorage {","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-phase1/design.md","commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","original_commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"For now I'd just use gts-rust in-memory cash and make it safe if needed...","created_at":"2025-12-16T19:55:30Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T19:56:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624554559","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624554559"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2624554559"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2624554559/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":166,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2623829878,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":166,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634876647","pull_request_review_id":3598350434,"id":2634876647,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6dDQbn","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@\n+//! `TypesRegistryApi` trait definition.\n+//!\n+//! This trait defines the public API for the `types-registry` module.\n+//! All methods require a `SecurityCtx` for authorization and access control.\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityCtx;\n+\n+use crate::error::TypesRegistryError;\n+use crate::models::{GtsEntity, ListQuery};\n+\n+/// Public API trait for the `types-registry` module.\n+///\n+/// This trait can be consumed by other modules via `ClientHub`:\n+/// ```ignore\n+/// let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryApi>()?;\n+/// let entity = client.get(&ctx, \"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\").await?;\n+/// ```\n+///\n+/// All methods require a `SecurityCtx` for proper authorization and access control.\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait TypesRegistryApi: Send + Sync {","path":"modules/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/api.rs","commit_id":"25a4db2e48c5155c97163bb1b926b771a8d18301","original_commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"PROPOSAL: Starting with this PR, I suggest renaming all these clients from XXXXApi to XXXClient, as the Api suffix is confusing. @Artifizer what do you think?","created_at":"2025-12-19T12:01:26Z","updated_at":"2025-12-19T12:54:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634876647","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634876647"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634876647"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634876647/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":22,"original_line":22,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":22,"position":22,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634939727","pull_request_review_id":3598350434,"id":2634939727,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6dDf1P","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@\n+//! `TypesRegistryApi` trait definition.\n+//!\n+//! This trait defines the public API for the `types-registry` module.\n+//! All methods require a `SecurityCtx` for authorization and access control.\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityCtx;\n+\n+use crate::error::TypesRegistryError;\n+use crate::models::{GtsEntity, ListQuery};\n+\n+/// Public API trait for the `types-registry` module.\n+///\n+/// This trait can be consumed by other modules via `ClientHub`:\n+/// ```ignore\n+/// let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryApi>()?;\n+/// let entity = client.get(&ctx, \"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\").await?;\n+/// ```\n+///\n+/// All methods require a `SecurityCtx` for proper authorization and access control.\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait TypesRegistryApi: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Register GTS entities (types or instances) in batch.\n+    ///\n+    /// Each JSON value in the input should contain a valid GTS entity\n+    /// with a `$id` field containing the GTS identifier.\n+    ///\n+    /// # Arguments\n+    ///\n+    /// * `ctx` - Security context for authorization\n+    /// * `entities` - JSON values representing GTS entities to register\n+    ///\n+    /// # Returns\n+    ///\n+    /// A vector of registered `GtsEntity` objects on success.\n+    ///\n+    /// # Errors\n+    ///\n+    /// * `InvalidGtsId` - If any entity has an invalid GTS ID format\n+    /// * `AlreadyExists` - If any entity with the same GTS ID already exists\n+    /// * `ValidationFailed` - If any entity fails schema validation\n+    async fn register(","path":"modules/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/api.rs","commit_id":"25a4db2e48c5155c97163bb1b926b771a8d18301","original_commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"At the moment register accepts a batch of JSON payloads and relies on $id inside the JSON to identify entities.\r\n\r\nUsing serde_json::Value as the payload type is ok, but the API would benefit from making the following aspects explicitly:\r\n\r\n1. Whether the entity is a Type or an Instance\r\n2. The canonical GTS ID (instead of discovering it only by parsing JSON)\r\n\r\nThis would allow earlier validation, clearer error reporting, and avoid ambiguity between schema registration and instance registration for end-users of this API.\r\n\r\n**Suggested direction:**\r\n\r\nKeep serde_json::Value for content\r\n\r\nAdd registration entity like:\r\n```Rust\r\npub enum RegisterEntity {\r\n  Type {\r\n    gts_type_id: String,            // must have trailing ~, right?\r\n    schema: serde_json::Value,      // JSON Schema\r\n  },\r\n  Instance {\r\n    gts_instance_id: String,        // WITHOUT ~\r\n    type_id: String,                    // strong type\r\n    object: serde_json::Value,      // JSON object\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n","created_at":"2025-12-19T12:25:50Z","updated_at":"2025-12-19T13:28:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634939727","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634939727"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634939727"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634939727/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":62,"original_line":42,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":42,"position":62,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634942671","pull_request_review_id":3598350434,"id":2634942671,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6dDgjP","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@\n+//! `TypesRegistryApi` trait definition.\n+//!\n+//! This trait defines the public API for the `types-registry` module.\n+//! All methods require a `SecurityCtx` for authorization and access control.\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityCtx;\n+\n+use crate::error::TypesRegistryError;\n+use crate::models::{GtsEntity, ListQuery};\n+\n+/// Public API trait for the `types-registry` module.\n+///\n+/// This trait can be consumed by other modules via `ClientHub`:\n+/// ```ignore\n+/// let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryApi>()?;\n+/// let entity = client.get(&ctx, \"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\").await?;\n+/// ```\n+///\n+/// All methods require a `SecurityCtx` for proper authorization and access control.\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait TypesRegistryApi: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Register GTS entities (types or instances) in batch.\n+    ///\n+    /// Each JSON value in the input should contain a valid GTS entity\n+    /// with a `$id` field containing the GTS identifier.\n+    ///\n+    /// # Arguments\n+    ///\n+    /// * `ctx` - Security context for authorization\n+    /// * `entities` - JSON values representing GTS entities to register\n+    ///\n+    /// # Returns\n+    ///\n+    /// A vector of registered `GtsEntity` objects on success.\n+    ///\n+    /// # Errors\n+    ///\n+    /// * `InvalidGtsId` - If any entity has an invalid GTS ID format\n+    /// * `AlreadyExists` - If any entity with the same GTS ID already exists\n+    /// * `ValidationFailed` - If any entity fails schema validation\n+    async fn register(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        entities: Vec<serde_json::Value>,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<GtsEntity>, TypesRegistryError>;","path":"modules/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/api.rs","commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","original_commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"For batch-style APIs, it may be useful to return per-item results (ok/error) rather than all-or-nothing behavior, especially for any tooling","created_at":"2025-12-19T12:26:55Z","updated_at":"2025-12-19T12:54:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634942671","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634942671"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634942671"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634942671/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":46,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":46,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634955066","pull_request_review_id":3598350434,"id":2634955066,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6dDjk6","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,311 @@\n+//! Public models for the `types-registry` module.\n+//!\n+//! These are transport-agnostic data structures that define the contract\n+//! between the `types-registry` module and its consumers.\n+\n+use serde::{de::DeserializeOwned, Deserialize, Serialize};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+// Re-export GtsIdSegment from gts-rust\n+pub use gts::GtsIdSegment;\n+\n+/// The kind of GTS entity.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum GtsEntityKind {\n+    /// A type definition (GTS ID ends with `~`)\n+    Type,\n+    /// An instance of a type (GTS ID does not end with `~`)\n+    Instance,\n+}\n+\n+impl GtsEntityKind {\n+    /// Returns `true` if this is a type definition.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub const fn is_type(self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, Self::Type)\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns `true` if this is an instance.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub const fn is_instance(self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, Self::Instance)\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// A registered GTS entity.\n+///\n+/// This represents either a type definition or an instance that has been\n+/// registered in the Types Registry.\n+///\n+/// # Type Parameter\n+///\n+/// - `C`: The content type. Use `serde_json::Value` for dynamic content,\n+///   or a concrete struct for type-safe access.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```ignore\n+/// // Dynamic entity (default)\n+/// let entity: GtsEntity = registry.get(&ctx, \"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\").await?;\n+///\n+/// // Type-safe entity\n+/// let entity: GtsEntity<MySchema> = registry.get(&ctx, gts_id).await?;\n+/// ```\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]\n+pub struct GtsEntity<C = serde_json::Value>\n+where\n+    C: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Clone,\n+{\n+    /// Deterministic UUID generated from the GTS ID.\n+    ///\n+    /// This UUID is generated using UUID v5 with a GTS namespace,\n+    /// ensuring the same GTS ID always produces the same UUID.\n+    pub id: Uuid,\n+\n+    /// The full GTS identifier string.\n+    ///\n+    /// For types: `gts.vendor.package.namespace.name.version~`\n+    /// For instances: `gts.vendor.package.namespace.name.version~instance.id`\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+\n+    /// All parsed segments from the GTS ID.\n+    ///\n+    /// For simple IDs, this contains one segment.\n+    /// For chained IDs (instances), this contains multiple segments.\n+    pub segments: Vec<GtsIdSegment>,\n+\n+    /// The kind of entity (Type or Instance).\n+    pub kind: GtsEntityKind,\n+\n+    /// The entity content (schema for types, object for instances).\n+    pub content: C,\n+\n+    /// Optional description of the entity.\n+    pub description: Option<String>,\n+}\n+\n+/// Type alias for dynamic GTS entities using `serde_json::Value` as content.\n+pub type DynGtsEntity = GtsEntity<serde_json::Value>;\n+\n+impl<C> GtsEntity<C>\n+where\n+    C: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Clone,\n+{\n+    /// Creates a new `GtsEntity` with the given components.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(\n+        id: Uuid,\n+        gts_id: impl Into<String>,\n+        segments: Vec<GtsIdSegment>,\n+        kind: GtsEntityKind,\n+        content: C,\n+        description: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            id,\n+            gts_id: gts_id.into(),\n+            segments,\n+            kind,\n+            content,\n+            description,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns `true` if this entity is a type definition.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub const fn is_type(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.kind.is_type()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns `true` if this entity is an instance.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub const fn is_instance(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.kind.is_instance()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns the primary segment (first segment in the chain).\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn primary_segment(&self) -> Option<&GtsIdSegment> {\n+        self.segments.first()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns the vendor from the primary segment.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn vendor(&self) -> Option<&str> {\n+        self.primary_segment().map(|s| s.vendor.as_str())\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns the package from the primary segment.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn package(&self) -> Option<&str> {\n+        self.primary_segment().map(|s| s.package.as_str())\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns the namespace from the primary segment.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn namespace(&self) -> Option<&str> {\n+        self.primary_segment().map(|s| s.namespace.as_str())\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Query parameters for listing GTS entities.\n+///\n+/// All fields are optional. When a field is `None`, no filtering\n+/// is applied for that field.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```\n+/// use types_registry_sdk::ListQuery;\n+///\n+/// // List all entities\n+/// let query = ListQuery::default();\n+///\n+/// // List only types from vendor \"acme\"\n+/// let query = ListQuery::default()\n+///     .with_is_type(true)\n+///     .with_vendor(\"acme\");\n+///\n+/// // List entities matching a pattern\n+/// let query = ListQuery::default()\n+///     .with_pattern(\"gts.acme.core.*\");\n+/// ```\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n+pub struct ListQuery {\n+    /// Optional wildcard pattern for GTS ID matching.\n+    ///\n+    /// Supports `*` as a wildcard character.\n+    pub pattern: Option<String>,\n+\n+    /// Filter for entity kind: `true` for types, `false` for instances.\n+    pub is_type: Option<bool>,\n+\n+    /// Filter by vendor (matches any segment).\n+    pub vendor: Option<String>,\n+\n+    /// Filter by package (matches any segment).\n+    pub package: Option<String>,\n+\n+    /// Filter by namespace (matches any segment).\n+    pub namespace: Option<String>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ListQuery {\n+    /// Creates a new empty `ListQuery`.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new() -> Self {\n+        Self::default()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Sets the pattern filter.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn with_pattern(mut self, pattern: impl Into<String>) -> Self {","path":"modules/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/models.rs","commit_id":"25a4db2e48c5155c97163bb1b926b771a8d18301","original_commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think it will be better to clarify is whether vendor/package/namespace filters apply only to the primary GTS ID segment or to any segment in a chained ID.\n\nMaking this distinction explicit would help avoid surprising query results and simplify future use-cases. \nI mean something like:\n```Rust\npub enum SegmentMatchScope {\n    Primary,   //  just first GTS ID\n    Any,         //  any segment in GTS ID\n}\n\npub struct ListQuery {\n....\n    pub segment_scope: Option<SegmentMatchScope>,\n}\n```","created_at":"2025-12-19T12:31:28Z","updated_at":"2025-12-19T12:54:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634955066","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634955066"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634955066"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634955066/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":586,"original_line":202,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":202,"position":586,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634971626","pull_request_review_id":3598472820,"id":2634971626,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6dDnnq","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@\n+# Types Registry Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to register GTS entities (types and instances) in the registry.\n+\n+A GTS entity consists of:\n+- **GTS ID**: A valid GTS identifier (e.g., `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1~` for types, `gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.v1.0` for instances)\n+- **Kind**: Either `Type` (schema) or `Instance` (object)\n+- **Content**: JSON Schema for types, JSON object for instances\n+- **Metadata**: Optional metadata (description, tags, created_at, updated_at)\n+\n+Registration SHALL:\n+- Validate the GTS ID format using OP#1 (ID Validation)\n+- Extract and parse the GTS ID components using OP#3 (ID Parsing)\n+- Optionally validate GTS references within the content using OP#7 (Relationship Resolution)\n+- Generate a deterministic UUID from the GTS ID using OP#5 (ID to UUID Mapping)\n+- Store the entity in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register a type entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS type identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON Schema as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Register an instance entity successfully\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid GTS instance identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **AND** a valid JSON object as content\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns the registered entity with generated UUID\n+- **AND** the entity is stored in the registry\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid GTS ID format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an invalid GTS identifier `invalid-gts-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the entity data\n+- **THEN** the system returns a validation error with details about the invalid format\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate entity registration\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `register` with the same GTS ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a conflict error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Listing\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to list GTS entities with filtering and pagination support.\n+\n+Listing SHALL support:\n+- Filtering by GTS ID pattern using OP#4 (ID Pattern Matching) with wildcards\n+- Filtering by entity kind (Type, Instance, or both)\n+- Filtering by vendor, package, namespace, or type components\n+- Cursor-based pagination with configurable limit\n+- Query execution using OP#10 (Query Execution)\n+\n+#### Scenario: List all entities with pagination\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains 100 GTS entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `limit=25`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the first 25 entities\n+- **AND** the response includes a cursor for the next page\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by wildcard pattern\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains entities from vendors `acme` and `globex`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only entities from vendor `acme`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Filter entities by kind\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains both type and instance entities\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with `kind=Type`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only type entities (ending with `~`)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return empty list when no matches\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the registry contains no entities matching pattern `gts.unknown.*`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `list` with that pattern\n+- **THEN** the system returns an empty list with no error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS Entity Retrieval\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to retrieve a single GTS entity by its identifier.\n+\n+Retrieval SHALL:\n+- Accept a valid GTS ID\n+- Return the full entity including content and metadata\n+- Support attribute access using OP#11 (Attribute Access) with `@` selector\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity by exact ID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns the complete entity with content and metadata\n+\n+#### Scenario: Get entity attribute\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with GTS ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` exists\n+- **AND** the entity has a property `name` with value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with ID `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~@name`\n+- **THEN** the system returns the value `\"UserCreated\"`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Return not found for non-existent entity\n+\n+- **GIVEN** no entity with GTS ID `gts.unknown.pkg.ns.type.v1~` exists\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get` with that ID\n+- **THEN** the system returns a not found error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Validation (OP#1)\n+\n+The system SHALL validate GTS identifier syntax according to the GTS specification.\n+\n+Valid GTS identifiers MUST:\n+- Start with `gts.` prefix\n+- Contain segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type`\n+- Include version: `v<MAJOR>` or `v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>`\n+- End with `~` for type identifiers, no suffix for instance identifiers\n+- Use only lowercase ASCII letters, digits, and underscores in segments\n+- Have segments starting with a letter or underscore\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as a type (schema)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate correct instance identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+- **AND** the identifier is recognized as an instance (object)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with invalid prefix\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `invalid.acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Invalid GTS prefix\"\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject identifier with uppercase characters\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.Acme.core.events.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the identifier\n+- **THEN** validation fails with error \"Segments must be lowercase\"\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Parsing (OP#3)\n+\n+The system SHALL parse GTS identifiers into their constituent components.\n+\n+Parsing SHALL extract:\n+- `vendor`: The vendor/organization identifier\n+- `package`: The package/module identifier\n+- `namespace`: The namespace category (or `_` placeholder)\n+- `type_name`: The type name\n+- `version_major`: The major version number\n+- `version_minor`: The optional minor version number\n+- `is_type`: Whether the identifier represents a type (true) or instance (false)\n+- `segments`: For chained identifiers, all segments in order\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse simple type identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains:\n+  - `vendor = \"acme\"`\n+  - `package = \"core\"`\n+  - `namespace = \"events\"`\n+  - `type_name = \"user_created\"`\n+  - `version_major = 1`\n+  - `version_minor = Some(2)`\n+  - `is_type = true`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Parse chained identifier\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.x.core.events.event.v1~acme.app._.custom_event.v2~`\n+- **WHEN** the system parses the identifier\n+- **THEN** the result contains 2 segments\n+- **AND** the first segment has vendor `x` and is a base type\n+- **AND** the second segment has vendor `acme` and is a derived type\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID Pattern Matching (OP#4)\n+\n+The system SHALL match GTS identifiers against patterns containing wildcards.\n+\n+Pattern matching SHALL support:\n+- `*` wildcard matching any single segment\n+- `**` wildcard matching zero or more segments\n+- Exact segment matching\n+\n+#### Scenario: Match with single wildcard\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*.events.*`\n+- **AND** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system matches the identifier against the pattern\n+- **THEN** the match succeeds\n+\n+#### Scenario: No match with different vendor\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the pattern `gts.acme.*`\n+- **AND** the identifier `gts.globex.core.events.order.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system matches the identifier against the pattern\n+- **THEN** the match fails\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: GTS ID to UUID Mapping (OP#5)\n+\n+The system SHALL generate deterministic UUIDs from GTS identifiers.\n+\n+UUID generation SHALL:\n+- Produce the same UUID for the same GTS ID (deterministic)\n+- Use UUID v5 with a GTS-specific namespace\n+- Support scoping by major version (same UUID for v1.0 and v1.5)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Generate deterministic UUID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifier `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system generates a UUID twice\n+- **THEN** both UUIDs are identical\n+\n+#### Scenario: Same major version produces same UUID\n+\n+- **GIVEN** the identifiers `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0` and `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.5`\n+- **WHEN** the system generates UUIDs with major scope\n+- **THEN** both UUIDs are identical\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Schema Validation (OP#6)\n+\n+The system SHALL validate JSON object instances against their corresponding JSON Schema types.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validate instance against schema\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` with JSON Schema requiring `userId` field\n+- **AND** an instance `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1.0` with `userId` field\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the instance\n+- **THEN** validation succeeds\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid instance\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type `gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~` with JSON Schema requiring `userId` field\n+- **AND** an instance missing the `userId` field\n+- **WHEN** the system validates the instance\n+- **THEN** validation fails with details about the missing field\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Relationship Resolution (OP#7)\n+\n+The system SHALL resolve inter-dependencies between GTS entities and detect broken references.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Resolve valid references\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type that references another registered type via `x-gts-ref`\n+- **WHEN** the system resolves relationships\n+- **THEN** all references are resolved successfully\n+\n+#### Scenario: Detect broken reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type that references a non-existent type `gts.unknown.pkg.ns.type.v1~`\n+- **WHEN** the system resolves relationships\n+- **THEN** the system reports the broken reference\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Compatibility Checking (OP#8)\n+\n+The system SHALL verify schema compatibility between different MINOR versions.\n+\n+Compatibility modes:\n+- **Backward**: Old instances work with new schema\n+- **Forward**: New instances work with old schema\n+- **Full**: Both backward and forward compatible\n+\n+#### Scenario: Check backward compatibility\n+\n+- **GIVEN** schema v1.0 and schema v1.1 where v1.1 adds an optional field\n+- **WHEN** the system checks backward compatibility\n+- **THEN** the schemas are backward compatible\n+\n+#### Scenario: Detect backward incompatibility\n+\n+- **GIVEN** schema v1.0 and schema v1.1 where v1.1 removes a required field\n+- **WHEN** the system checks backward compatibility\n+- **THEN** the schemas are NOT backward compatible\n+- **AND** the system reports the incompatibility reason\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Version Casting (OP#9)\n+\n+The system SHALL transform instances between compatible MINOR versions.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Cast instance to newer version\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an instance conforming to v1.0\n+- **AND** v1.1 adds an optional field with default value\n+- **WHEN** the system casts the instance to v1.1\n+- **THEN** the casted instance includes the new field with default value\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Query Execution (OP#10)\n+\n+The system SHALL filter identifier collections using the GTS query language.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query with attribute filter\n+\n+- **GIVEN** entities with various `status` values\n+- **WHEN** the user queries `gts.acme.core.*[status=active]`\n+- **THEN** only entities with `status=active` are returned\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Attribute Access (OP#11)\n+\n+The system SHALL retrieve property values using the attribute selector (`@`).\n+\n+#### Scenario: Access top-level attribute\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with property `name = \"UserCreated\"`\n+- **WHEN** the user accesses `entity@name`\n+- **THEN** the value `\"UserCreated\"` is returned\n+\n+#### Scenario: Access nested attribute\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity with nested property `metadata.version = \"1.0\"`\n+- **WHEN** the user accesses `entity@metadata.version`\n+- **THEN** the value `\"1.0\"` is returned\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: In-Memory Storage\n+\n+The system SHALL provide thread-safe in-memory storage for GTS entities in Phase 1.1.\n+\n+Storage SHALL:\n+- Support concurrent read/write access\n+- Maintain entity ordering by registration time\n+- Support efficient lookup by GTS ID\n+- Support efficient pattern-based queries","path":"modules/types-registry/openspec/changes/add-types-registry-module/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"25a4db2e48c5155c97163bb1b926b771a8d18301","original_commit_id":"89a64f6a7b129b5609a573e35bc5c27d331fbed2","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Addressed in the code","created_at":"2025-12-19T12:37:40Z","updated_at":"2025-12-19T12:37:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634971626","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634971626"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634971626"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634971626/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":460,"original_line":358,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2623794005,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":358,"position":460,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634981807","pull_request_review_id":3598350434,"id":2634981807,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6dDqGv","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,311 @@\n+//! Public models for the `types-registry` module.\n+//!\n+//! These are transport-agnostic data structures that define the contract\n+//! between the `types-registry` module and its consumers.\n+\n+use serde::{de::DeserializeOwned, Deserialize, Serialize};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+// Re-export GtsIdSegment from gts-rust\n+pub use gts::GtsIdSegment;\n+\n+/// The kind of GTS entity.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum GtsEntityKind {\n+    /// A type definition (GTS ID ends with `~`)\n+    Type,\n+    /// An instance of a type (GTS ID does not end with `~`)\n+    Instance,\n+}\n+\n+impl GtsEntityKind {\n+    /// Returns `true` if this is a type definition.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub const fn is_type(self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, Self::Type)\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns `true` if this is an instance.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub const fn is_instance(self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, Self::Instance)\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// A registered GTS entity.\n+///\n+/// This represents either a type definition or an instance that has been\n+/// registered in the Types Registry.\n+///\n+/// # Type Parameter\n+///\n+/// - `C`: The content type. Use `serde_json::Value` for dynamic content,\n+///   or a concrete struct for type-safe access.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```ignore\n+/// // Dynamic entity (default)\n+/// let entity: GtsEntity = registry.get(&ctx, \"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\").await?;\n+///\n+/// // Type-safe entity\n+/// let entity: GtsEntity<MySchema> = registry.get(&ctx, gts_id).await?;\n+/// ```\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]\n+pub struct GtsEntity<C = serde_json::Value>\n+where\n+    C: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Clone,\n+{\n+    /// Deterministic UUID generated from the GTS ID.\n+    ///\n+    /// This UUID is generated using UUID v5 with a GTS namespace,\n+    /// ensuring the same GTS ID always produces the same UUID.\n+    pub id: Uuid,\n+\n+    /// The full GTS identifier string.\n+    ///\n+    /// For types: `gts.vendor.package.namespace.name.version~`\n+    /// For instances: `gts.vendor.package.namespace.name.version~instance.id`\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+\n+    /// All parsed segments from the GTS ID.\n+    ///\n+    /// For simple IDs, this contains one segment.\n+    /// For chained IDs (instances), this contains multiple segments.\n+    pub segments: Vec<GtsIdSegment>,\n+\n+    /// The kind of entity (Type or Instance).\n+    pub kind: GtsEntityKind,\n+\n+    /// The entity content (schema for types, object for instances).\n+    pub content: C,\n+\n+    /// Optional description of the entity.\n+    pub description: Option<String>,\n+}\n+\n+/// Type alias for dynamic GTS entities using `serde_json::Value` as content.\n+pub type DynGtsEntity = GtsEntity<serde_json::Value>;","path":"modules/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/models.rs","commit_id":"25a4db2e48c5155c97163bb1b926b771a8d18301","original_commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Probably we can simplify DX here with additional type alisases like:\n\npub struct TypeSchema(pub serde_json::Value);\npub struct InstanceObject(pub serde_json::Value);\n\npub type GtsTypeEntity = GtsEntity<TypeSchema>;\npub type GtsInstanceEntity = GtsEntity<InstanceObject>;","created_at":"2025-12-19T12:41:57Z","updated_at":"2025-12-19T12:54:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634981807","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634981807"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634981807"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634981807/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":86,"original_line":88,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":88,"position":86,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634985626","pull_request_review_id":3598350434,"id":2634985626,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6dDrCa","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,311 @@\n+//! Public models for the `types-registry` module.\n+//!\n+//! These are transport-agnostic data structures that define the contract\n+//! between the `types-registry` module and its consumers.\n+\n+use serde::{de::DeserializeOwned, Deserialize, Serialize};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+// Re-export GtsIdSegment from gts-rust\n+pub use gts::GtsIdSegment;\n+\n+/// The kind of GTS entity.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum GtsEntityKind {\n+    /// A type definition (GTS ID ends with `~`)\n+    Type,\n+    /// An instance of a type (GTS ID does not end with `~`)\n+    Instance,\n+}\n+\n+impl GtsEntityKind {\n+    /// Returns `true` if this is a type definition.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub const fn is_type(self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, Self::Type)\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns `true` if this is an instance.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub const fn is_instance(self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, Self::Instance)\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// A registered GTS entity.\n+///\n+/// This represents either a type definition or an instance that has been\n+/// registered in the Types Registry.\n+///\n+/// # Type Parameter\n+///\n+/// - `C`: The content type. Use `serde_json::Value` for dynamic content,\n+///   or a concrete struct for type-safe access.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```ignore\n+/// // Dynamic entity (default)\n+/// let entity: GtsEntity = registry.get(&ctx, \"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\").await?;\n+///\n+/// // Type-safe entity\n+/// let entity: GtsEntity<MySchema> = registry.get(&ctx, gts_id).await?;\n+/// ```\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]\n+pub struct GtsEntity<C = serde_json::Value>\n+where\n+    C: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Clone,\n+{\n+    /// Deterministic UUID generated from the GTS ID.\n+    ///\n+    /// This UUID is generated using UUID v5 with a GTS namespace,","path":"modules/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/models.rs","commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","original_commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"What is namespace is using for uuidv5 generation? Is it user-defined or GTS specification defined?","created_at":"2025-12-19T12:43:31Z","updated_at":"2025-12-19T12:54:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634985626","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634985626"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2634985626"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2634985626/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":61,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":61,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2635014552","pull_request_review_id":3598350434,"id":2635014552,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6dDyGY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,311 @@\n+//! Public models for the `types-registry` module.\n+//!\n+//! These are transport-agnostic data structures that define the contract\n+//! between the `types-registry` module and its consumers.\n+\n+use serde::{de::DeserializeOwned, Deserialize, Serialize};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+// Re-export GtsIdSegment from gts-rust\n+pub use gts::GtsIdSegment;\n+\n+/// The kind of GTS entity.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum GtsEntityKind {\n+    /// A type definition (GTS ID ends with `~`)\n+    Type,\n+    /// An instance of a type (GTS ID does not end with `~`)\n+    Instance,\n+}\n+\n+impl GtsEntityKind {\n+    /// Returns `true` if this is a type definition.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub const fn is_type(self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, Self::Type)\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns `true` if this is an instance.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub const fn is_instance(self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, Self::Instance)\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// A registered GTS entity.\n+///\n+/// This represents either a type definition or an instance that has been\n+/// registered in the Types Registry.\n+///\n+/// # Type Parameter\n+///\n+/// - `C`: The content type. Use `serde_json::Value` for dynamic content,\n+///   or a concrete struct for type-safe access.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```ignore\n+/// // Dynamic entity (default)\n+/// let entity: GtsEntity = registry.get(&ctx, \"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\").await?;\n+///\n+/// // Type-safe entity\n+/// let entity: GtsEntity<MySchema> = registry.get(&ctx, gts_id).await?;\n+/// ```\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]\n+pub struct GtsEntity<C = serde_json::Value>\n+where\n+    C: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Clone,","path":"modules/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/models.rs","commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","original_commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think the trait bounds on GtsEntity<C> are heavier than necessary.\n\nBy putting C: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Clone on the struct, we force every in-memory use of GtsEntity to require these traits, even when no serialization or cloning is needed.\n\nWe could safely remove the bounds from the struct itself and rely on derive to add the required constraints only when Serialize, Deserialize, or Clone are actually used:\n\n```Rust\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct GtsEntity<C = serde_json::Value> {\n    // fields unchanged\n}\n```","created_at":"2025-12-19T12:54:40Z","updated_at":"2025-12-19T12:54:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2635014552","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2635014552"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2635014552"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2635014552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":57,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":57,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2635243238","pull_request_review_id":3598784768,"id":2635243238,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6dEp7m","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@\n+# Types Registry SDK\n+\n+SDK crate for the Types Registry module, providing the public API contracts for GTS (Global Type System) entity management.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+This crate defines the transport-agnostic interface for the Types Registry module:\n+\n+- **`TypesRegistryApi`** - Async trait for inter-module communication\n+- **`GtsEntity`** - Model representing registered GTS entities (types and instances)\n+- **`ListQuery`** - Query builder for filtering entity listings\n+- **`TypesRegistryError`** - Error types for all operations\n+\n+## Usage\n+\n+### Getting the Client\n+\n+Consumers obtain the client from `ClientHub`:\n+\n+```rust\n+use types_registry_sdk::{TypesRegistryApi, ListQuery};\n+\n+// Get the client from ClientHub\n+let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryApi>()?;\n+```\n+\n+### Registering Entities\n+\n+```rust\n+use serde_json::json;\n+\n+// Register a type schema\n+let schemas = vec![\n+    json!({\n+        \"$id\": \"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\",\n+        \"type\": \"object\",\n+        \"properties\": {\n+            \"user_id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+        }\n+    })\n+];\n+\n+let entities = client.register(&ctx, schemas).await?;\n+```\n+\n+### Listing Entities\n+\n+```rust\n+use types_registry_sdk::ListQuery;\n+\n+// List all entities\n+let all = client.list(&ctx, ListQuery::default()).await?;\n+\n+// List only types from vendor \"acme\"\n+let query = ListQuery::new()\n+    .with_is_type(true)\n+    .with_vendor(\"acme\");\n+let acme_types = client.list(&ctx, query).await?;\n+\n+// List entities matching a pattern\n+let query = ListQuery::new()\n+    .with_pattern(\"gts.acme.core.*\");\n+let matched = client.list(&ctx, query).await?;\n+```\n+\n+### Getting a Single Entity\n+\n+```rust\n+let entity = client.get(&ctx, \"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\").await?;","path":"modules/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/README.md","commit_id":"25a4db2e48c5155c97163bb1b926b771a8d18301","original_commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Can we put types to be used explicitly in 'let xxx ' ?\nThat is especially important in specs and pub interfaces\n","created_at":"2025-12-19T14:18:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-19T16:54:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2635243238","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2635243238"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2635243238"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2635243238/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":70,"original_line":70,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":70,"position":70,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2635252429","pull_request_review_id":3598784768,"id":2635252429,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6dEsLN","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@\n+# Types Registry SDK\n+\n+SDK crate for the Types Registry module, providing the public API contracts for GTS (Global Type System) entity management.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+This crate defines the transport-agnostic interface for the Types Registry module:\n+\n+- **`TypesRegistryApi`** - Async trait for inter-module communication\n+- **`GtsEntity`** - Model representing registered GTS entities (types and instances)\n+- **`ListQuery`** - Query builder for filtering entity listings\n+- **`TypesRegistryError`** - Error types for all operations\n+\n+## Usage\n+\n+### Getting the Client\n+\n+Consumers obtain the client from `ClientHub`:\n+\n+```rust\n+use types_registry_sdk::{TypesRegistryApi, ListQuery};\n+\n+// Get the client from ClientHub\n+let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryApi>()?;\n+```\n+\n+### Registering Entities\n+\n+```rust\n+use serde_json::json;\n+\n+// Register a type schema\n+let schemas = vec![\n+    json!({\n+        \"$id\": \"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\",\n+        \"type\": \"object\",\n+        \"properties\": {\n+            \"user_id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+        }\n+    })\n+];\n+\n+let entities = client.register(&ctx, schemas).await?;\n+```\n+\n+### Listing Entities\n+\n+```rust\n+use types_registry_sdk::ListQuery;\n+\n+// List all entities\n+let all = client.list(&ctx, ListQuery::default()).await?;\n+\n+// List only types from vendor \"acme\"\n+let query = ListQuery::new()\n+    .with_is_type(true)\n+    .with_vendor(\"acme\");\n+let acme_types = client.list(&ctx, query).await?;\n+\n+// List entities matching a pattern\n+let query = ListQuery::new()\n+    .with_pattern(\"gts.acme.core.*\");\n+let matched = client.list(&ctx, query).await?;\n+```\n+\n+### Getting a Single Entity\n+\n+```rust\n+let entity = client.get(&ctx, \"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\").await?;\n+\n+println!(\"GTS ID: {}\", entity.gts_id);\n+println!(\"Kind: {:?}\", entity.kind);\n+println!(\"Vendor: {:?}\", entity.vendor());\n+```\n+\n+## Models\n+\n+### GtsEntity\n+\n+Represents a registered GTS entity:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct GtsEntity<C = serde_json::Value> {\n+    pub id: Uuid,                    // Deterministic UUID from GTS ID\n+    pub gts_id: String,              // Full GTS identifier\n+    pub segments: Vec<GtsIdSegment>, // Parsed segments\n+    pub kind: GtsEntityKind,         // Type or Instance\n+    pub content: C,                  // Schema or object content\n+    pub description: Option<String>, // Optional description","path":"modules/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/README.md","commit_id":"25a4db2e48c5155c97163bb1b926b771a8d18301","original_commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd add gts_uuid here (to avoid redundant string -> UUID translation API)","created_at":"2025-12-19T14:21:30Z","updated_at":"2025-12-19T16:54:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2635252429","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2635252429"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/125#discussion_r2635252429"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/125"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2635252429/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":90,"original_line":90,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":90,"position":90,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2635310652","pull_request_review_id":3598861465,"id":2635310652,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6dE6Y8","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,311 @@\n+//! Public models for the `types-registry` module.\n+//!\n+//! These are transport-agnostic data structures that define the contract\n+//! between the `types-registry` module and its consumers.\n+\n+use serde::{de::DeserializeOwned, Deserialize, Serialize};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+// Re-export GtsIdSegment from gts-rust\n+pub use gts::GtsIdSegment;\n+\n+/// The kind of GTS entity.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum GtsEntityKind {\n+    /// A type definition (GTS ID ends with `~`)\n+    Type,\n+    /// An instance of a type (GTS ID does not end with `~`)\n+    Instance,\n+}\n+\n+impl GtsEntityKind {\n+    /// Returns `true` if this is a type definition.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub const fn is_type(self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, Self::Type)\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns `true` if this is an instance.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub const fn is_instance(self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, Self::Instance)\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// A registered GTS entity.\n+///\n+/// This represents either a type definition or an instance that has been\n+/// registered in the Types Registry.\n+///\n+/// # Type Parameter\n+///\n+/// - `C`: The content type. Use `serde_json::Value` for dynamic content,\n+///   or a concrete struct for type-safe access.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```ignore\n+/// // Dynamic entity (default)\n+/// let entity: GtsEntity = registry.get(&ctx, \"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\").await?;\n+///\n+/// // Type-safe entity\n+/// let entity: GtsEntity<MySchema> = registry.get(&ctx, gts_id).await?;\n+/// ```\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]\n+pub struct GtsEntity<C = serde_json::Value>\n+where\n+    C: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Clone,","path":"modules/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/models.rs","commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","original_commit_id":"eb403747e7f7362067daf8c5687ca00d72982345","user":