loyment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4396367577","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/66#issuecomment-4396367577","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/66","id":4396367577,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABBgs-2Q","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-07T10:37:18Z","updated_at":"2026-05-07T10:37:18Z","body":"Declining, new PR is coming.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4396367577/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2610705742","pull_request_review_id":3567589614,"id":2610705742,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6bnDVO","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,761 @@\n+# Event Broker Module\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The Event Broker is a high-performance event streaming module for HyperSpot. It provides a REST API for producing and\n+consuming events with support for batch operations, cursor-based pagination, and long-polling. Events are typed using\n+the Global Type System (GTS) notation and stored with monotonically increasing sequences for reliable ordering and\n+replay.\n+\n+The module acts as a lightweight event log, enabling decoupled communication between microservices and real-time data\n+streaming use cases.\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+The Event Broker follows HyperSpot's modular architecture with clean layer separation:\n+\n+```\n+event_broker/\n+├── src/\n+│   ├── contract/          # Public API (transport-agnostic)\n+│   │   ├── client.rs      # Native Rust client trait (EventBrokerApi)\n+│   │   ├── model.rs       # Core models: Event, Topic, EventType\n+│   │   └── error.rs       # Contract errors: EventBrokerError\n+│   ├── domain/            # Business logic\n+│   │   ├── service.rs     # Event service (produce, consume, storage)\n+│   │   ├── repository.rs  # Repository traits (event persistence)\n+│   │   └── events.rs      # Domain events\n+│   ├── api/               # REST adapters\n+│   │   └── rest/\n+│   │       ├── dto.rs     # REST DTOs (with serde)\n+│   │       ├── handlers.rs # HTTP handlers\n+│   │       ├── routes.rs  # Route registration\n+│   │       ├── mapper.rs  # DTO ↔ Model conversions\n+│   │       └── error.rs   # Problem Details mapping\n+│   ├── infra/             # Infrastructure\n+│   │   └── storage/       # Event storage implementation\n+│   │       ├── repository.rs\n+│   │       └── entity.rs\n+│   ├── gateways/          # Client implementations\n+│   │   └── local.rs       # Local client for ClientHub\n+│   ├── module.rs          # Module registration\n+│   └── config.rs          # Typed configuration\n+└── README.md\n+```\n+\n+### Key Design Principles\n+\n+- **Sequential ordering**: Events are ordered by monotonically increasing sequence numbers\n+- **GTS-typed events**: All events are identified by GTS types identifiers\n+- **Immutable log**: Events are append-only with guaranteed ordering\n+- **Cursor-based pagination**: Efficient traversal of event streams\n+- **Long-polling support**: Reduce polling overhead with wait-for-data semantics\n+\n+## Features\n+\n+### Event Production\n+\n+- **Single event publishing**: `POST /v1/events` with idempotency support\n+- **Batch publishing**: `POST /v1/events:batch` (up to 100 events) atomic writes, per-event error reporting\n+- **Automatic sequence assignment**: Server-assigned monotonic sequence numbers\n+- **Idempotency**: Duplicate sequence detection and conflict resolution\n+\n+### Event Consumption\n+\n+- **Cursor-based listing**: `GET /v1/events` with filtering and pagination\n+- **Long-polling**: `GET /v1/events:poll` - wait up to 30s for new events\n+- **Sequence-based replay**: Read from any historical sequence position\n+- **Type filtering**: Filter by single or multiple event types\n+\n+### Data Management\n+\n+- **Sequential ordering**: Guaranteed ordering within the log\n+- **Efficient storage**: Optimized for high-throughput writes and range reads\n+- **Type registry via ABI**: Topics and event types registered through local Rust client (not REST)","path":"modules/event_broker/README.md","commit_id":"8ce67f51266451472ffa202ba83a96f4ca2d1d54","original_commit_id":"610f549714291b2f924d579e5cdc2f9f54dc0f75","user":{"login":"hitengajjar","id":17683811,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NjgzODEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17683811?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar","html_url":"https://github.com/hitengajjar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"What is ABI?","created_at":"2025-12-11T14:01:29Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T14:01:30Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/66#discussion_r2610705742","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/66","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2610705742"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/66#discussion_r2610705742"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/66"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2610705742/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":138,"original_line":74,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":74,"position":138,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2610716181","pull_request_review_id":3567602238,"id":2610716181,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6bnF4V","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,761 @@\n+# Event Broker Module\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The Event Broker is a high-performance event streaming module for HyperSpot. It provides a REST API for producing and\n+consuming events with support for batch operations, cursor-based pagination, and long-polling. Events are typed using\n+the Global Type System (GTS) notation and stored with monotonically increasing sequences for reliable ordering and\n+replay.\n+\n+The module acts as a lightweight event log, enabling decoupled communication between microservices and real-time data\n+streaming use cases.\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+The Event Broker follows HyperSpot's modular architecture with clean layer separation:\n+\n+```\n+event_broker/\n+├── src/\n+│   ├── contract/          # Public API (transport-agnostic)\n+│   │   ├── client.rs      # Native Rust client trait (EventBrokerApi)\n+│   │   ├── model.rs       # Core models: Event, Topic, EventType\n+│   │   └── error.rs       # Contract errors: EventBrokerError\n+│   ├── domain/            # Business logic\n+│   │   ├── service.rs     # Event service (produce, consume, storage)\n+│   │   ├── repository.rs  # Repository traits (event persistence)\n+│   │   └── events.rs      # Domain events\n+│   ├── api/               # REST adapters\n+│   │   └── rest/\n+│   │       ├── dto.rs     # REST DTOs (with serde)\n+│   │       ├── handlers.rs # HTTP handlers\n+│   │       ├── routes.rs  # Route registration\n+│   │       ├── mapper.rs  # DTO ↔ Model conversions\n+│   │       └── error.rs   # Problem Details mapping\n+│   ├── infra/             # Infrastructure\n+│   │   └── storage/       # Event storage implementation\n+│   │       ├── repository.rs\n+│   │       └── entity.rs\n+│   ├── gateways/          # Client implementations\n+│   │   └── local.rs       # Local client for ClientHub\n+│   ├── module.rs          # Module registration\n+│   └── config.rs          # Typed configuration\n+└── README.md\n+```\n+\n+### Key Design Principles\n+\n+- **Sequential ordering**: Events are ordered by monotonically increasing sequence numbers\n+- **GTS-typed events**: All events are identified by GTS types identifiers\n+- **Immutable log**: Events are append-only with guaranteed ordering\n+- **Cursor-based pagination**: Efficient traversal of event streams\n+- **Long-polling support**: Reduce polling overhead with wait-for-data semantics\n+\n+## Features\n+\n+### Event Production\n+\n+- **Single event publishing**: `POST /v1/events` with idempotency support\n+- **Batch publishing**: `POST /v1/events:batch` (up to 100 events) atomic writes, per-event error reporting\n+- **Automatic sequence assignment**: Server-assigned monotonic sequence numbers\n+- **Idempotency**: Duplicate sequence detection and conflict resolution\n+\n+### Event Consumption\n+\n+- **Cursor-based listing**: `GET /v1/events` with filtering and pagination\n+- **Long-polling**: `GET /v1/events:poll` - wait up to 30s for new events\n+- **Sequence-based replay**: Read from any historical sequence position\n+- **Type filtering**: Filter by single or multiple event types\n+\n+### Data Management\n+\n+- **Sequential ordering**: Guaranteed ordering within the log\n+- **Efficient storage**: Optimized for high-throughput writes and range reads\n+- **Type registry via ABI**: Topics and event types registered through local Rust client (not REST)","path":"modules/event_broker/README.md","commit_id":"8ce67f51266451472ffa202ba83a96f4ca2d1d54","original_commit_id":"610f549714291b2f924d579e5cdc2f9f54dc0f75","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It's Application Binary Interface, native calls","created_at":"2025-12-11T14:04:26Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T14:04:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/66#discussion_r2610716181","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/66","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2610716181"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/66#discussion_r2610716181"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/66"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2610716181/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":138,"original_line":74,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2610705742,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":74,"position":138,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2610751122","pull_request_review_id":3567645207,"id":2610751122,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6bnOaS","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,761 @@\n+# Event Broker Module\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The Event Broker is a high-performance event streaming module for HyperSpot. It provides a REST API for producing and\n+consuming events with support for batch operations, cursor-based pagination, and long-polling. Events are typed using\n+the Global Type System (GTS) notation and stored with monotonically increasing sequences for reliable ordering and\n+replay.\n+\n+The module acts as a lightweight event log, enabling decoupled communication between microservices and real-time data\n+streaming use cases.\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+The Event Broker follows HyperSpot's modular architecture with clean layer separation:\n+\n+```\n+event_broker/\n+├── src/\n+│   ├── contract/          # Public API (transport-agnostic)\n+│   │   ├── client.rs      # Native Rust client trait (EventBrokerApi)\n+│   │   ├── model.rs       # Core models: Event, Topic, EventType\n+│   │   └── error.rs       # Contract errors: EventBrokerError\n+│   ├── domain/            # Business logic\n+│   │   ├── service.rs     # Event service (produce, consume, storage)\n+│   │   ├── repository.rs  # Repository traits (event persistence)\n+│   │   └── events.rs      # Domain events\n+│   ├── api/               # REST adapters\n+│   │   └── rest/\n+│   │       ├── dto.rs     # REST DTOs (with serde)\n+│   │       ├── handlers.rs # HTTP handlers\n+│   │       ├── routes.rs  # Route registration\n+│   │       ├── mapper.rs  # DTO ↔ Model conversions\n+│   │       └── error.rs   # Problem Details mapping\n+│   ├── infra/             # Infrastructure\n+│   │   └── storage/       # Event storage implementation\n+│   │       ├── repository.rs\n+│   │       └── entity.rs\n+│   ├── gateways/          # Client implementations\n+│   │   └── local.rs       # Local client for ClientHub\n+│   ├── module.rs          # Module registration\n+│   └── config.rs          # Typed configuration\n+└── README.md\n+```\n+\n+### Key Design Principles\n+\n+- **Sequential ordering**: Events are ordered by monotonically increasing sequence numbers\n+- **GTS-typed events**: All events are identified by GTS types identifiers\n+- **Immutable log**: Events are append-only with guaranteed ordering\n+- **Cursor-based pagination**: Efficient traversal of event streams\n+- **Long-polling support**: Reduce polling overhead with wait-for-data semantics\n+\n+## Features\n+\n+### Event Production\n+\n+- **Single event publishing**: `POST /v1/events` with idempotency support\n+- **Batch publishing**: `POST /v1/events:batch` (up to 100 events) atomic writes, per-event error reporting\n+- **Automatic sequence assignment**: Server-assigned monotonic sequence numbers\n+- **Idempotency**: Duplicate sequence detection and conflict resolution\n+\n+### Event Consumption\n+\n+- **Cursor-based listing**: `GET /v1/events` with filtering and pagination\n+- **Long-polling**: `GET /v1/events:poll` - wait up to 30s for new events\n+- **Sequence-based replay**: Read from any historical sequence position\n+- **Type filtering**: Filter by single or multiple event types\n+\n+### Data Management\n+\n+- **Sequential ordering**: Guaranteed ordering within the log\n+- **Efficient storage**: Optimized for high-throughput writes and range reads\n+- **Type registry via ABI**: Topics and event types registered through local Rust client (not REST)","path":"modules/event_broker/README.md","commit_id":"8ce67f51266451472ffa202ba83a96f4ca2d1d54","original_commit_id":"610f549714291b2f924d579e5cdc2f9f54dc0f75","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I consider ABI registration to be a temporary solution, until we have type registry service.","created_at":"2025-12-11T14:14:08Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T14:14:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/66#discussion_r2610751122","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/66","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2610751122"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/66#discussion_r2610751122"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/66"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2610751122/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":138,"original_line":74,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2610705742,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":74,"position":138,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2613458852","pull_request_review_id":3570944016,"id":2613458852,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6bxjek","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,756 @@\n+# Event Broker Module\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The Event Broker is a high-performance event streaming module for HyperSpot. It provides a REST API for producing and\n+consuming events with support for batch operations, cursor-based pagination, and long-polling. Events are typed using\n+the Global Type System (GTS) notation and stored with monotonically increasing sequences for reliable ordering and\n+replay.\n+\n+The module acts as a lightweight event log, enabling decoupled communication between microservices and real-time data\n+streaming use cases.\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+The Event Broker follows HyperSpot's modular architecture with clean layer separation:\n+\n+```\n+event_broker/\n+├── src/\n+│   ├── contract/          # Public API (transport-agnostic)\n+│   │   ├── client.rs      # Native Rust client trait (EventBrokerApi)\n+│   │   ├── model.rs       # Core models: Event, Topic, EventType\n+│   │   └── error.rs       # Contract errors: EventBrokerError\n+│   ├── domain/            # Business logic\n+│   │   ├── service.rs     # Event service (produce, consume, storage)\n+│   │   ├── repository.rs  # Repository traits (event persistence)\n+│   │   └── events.rs      # Domain events\n+│   ├── api/               # REST adapters\n+│   │   └── rest/\n+│   │       ├── dto.rs     # REST DTOs (with serde)\n+│   │       ├── handlers.rs # HTTP handlers\n+│   │       ├── routes.rs  # Route registration\n+│   │       ├── mapper.rs  # DTO ↔ Model conversions\n+│   │       └── error.rs   # Problem Details mapping\n+│   ├── infra/             # Infrastructure\n+│   │   └── storage/       # Event storage implementation\n+│   │       ├── repository.rs\n+│   │       └── entity.rs\n+│   ├── gateways/          # Client implementations\n+│   │   └── local.rs       # Local client for ClientHub\n+│   ├── module.rs          # Module registration\n+│   └── config.rs          # Typed configuration\n+└── README.md\n+```\n+\n+### Key Design Principles\n+\n+- **Sequential ordering**: Events are ordered by monotonically increasing sequence numbers","path":"modules/event_broker/README.md","commit_id":"c2d04990498c12f75f52093ccf4fd31b3040b091","original_commit_id":"ef9c07b456b71b18d1375909edb2f130b51b2e31","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"htt