-|-------------|\n+| `module_name` | Logical module name (e.g., \"file_parser\") |\n+| `instance_id` | Instance ID (defaults to random UUID) |\n+| `directory_endpoint` | DirectoryService gRPC endpoint |\n+| `config_path` | Path to configuration file |\n+| `verbose` | Log verbosity (0=default, 1=info, 2=debug, 3=trace) |\n+| `print_config` | Print effective config and exit |\n+| `heartbeat_interval_secs` | Heartbeat interval (default: 5) |\n+\n+### OoP Lifecycle\n+\n+When an OoP module starts:\n+\n+1. **Configuration loading** — loads config from file or `MODKIT_MODULE_CONFIG` env var\n+2. **Logging initialization** — sets up tracing with optional OTEL\n+3. **DirectoryService connection** — connects to the master host's directory service\n+4. **Instance registration** — registers with DirectoryService for discovery\n+5. **Heartbeat loop** — starts background heartbeat task\n+6. **Module lifecycle** — runs the normal module lifecycle (init → migrate → start)\n+7. **Graceful shutdown** — deregisters from DirectoryService on exit\n+\n+### Shutdown Model\n+\n+Shutdown is driven by a single root `CancellationToken` per process:\n+\n+* OS signals (SIGTERM, SIGINT, Ctrl+C) are hooked at bootstrap level\n+* The root token is passed to `RunOptions::Token` for module runtime shutdown\n+* Background tasks (like heartbeat) use child tokens derived from the root\n+* On shutdown, the module deregisters itself from DirectoryService before exiting\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Module Orchestrator & Directory API\n+\n+The **Module Orchestrator** provides service discovery and instance management for both in-process and OoP modules.\n+\n+### DirectoryApi Trait\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryApi: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve a gRPC service by its logical name to an endpoint\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// List all service instances for a given module\n+    async fn list_instances(&self, module: &str) -> Result<Vec<ServiceInstanceInfo>>;\n+\n+    /// Register a new module instance with the directory\n+    async fn register_instance(&self, info: RegisterInstanceInfo) -> Result<()>;\n+\n+    /// Deregister a module instance (for graceful shutdown)\n+    async fn deregister_instance(&self, module: &str, instance_id: &str) -> Result<()>;\n+\n+    /// Send a heartbeat for a module instance to indicate it's still alive\n+    async fn send_heartbeat(&self, module: &str, instance_id: &str) -> Result<()>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Service Endpoint Types\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents an endpoint where a service can be reached\n+pub struct ServiceEndpoint {\n+    pub uri: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl ServiceEndpoint {\n+    pub fn tcp(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self;  // \"http://host:port\"\n+    pub fn uds(path: impl AsRef<Path>) -> Self; // \"unix:///path/to/socket\"\n+}\n+\n+/// Information about a service instance\n+pub struct ServiceInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub endpoint: ServiceEndpoint,\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+\n+/// Information for registering a new module instance\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Using DirectoryApi\n+\n+**From an OoP module** — the DirectoryApi client is injected into the ClientHub:\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+    // DirectoryApi is available via ClientHub in OoP modules\n+    let directory = ctx.client_hub.get::<dyn DirectoryApi>()?;\n+    \n+    // Resolve another service's endpoint\n+    let endpoint = directory.resolve_grpc_service(\"my.package.MyService\").await?;\n+    \n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**From the master host** — the Module Orchestrator registers itself as the DirectoryApi implementation.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Backends\n+\n+Backends manage the lifecycle of out-of-process module instances.\n+\n+### BackendKind\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum BackendKind {\n+    LocalProcess,  // Spawn as local child process\n+    K8s,           // Deploy to Kubernetes (future)","path":"docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"3df73358ee3583a26e64dcc390d34326f023b708","original_commit_id":"89c33a1548a8c165d0b406b13bdd01cdbf35eb01","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It's not obvious. I thought that k8s implementation will be empty or with some kind of ensure_runing() function or whatever. ","created_at":"2025-12-10T21:38:40Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T21:38:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/60#discussion_r2608298906","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/60","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608298906"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/60#discussion_r2608298906"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/60"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608298906/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":408,"original_line":408,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2607908674,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":211,"position":211,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608302289","pull_request_review_id":3564596189,"id":2608302289,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6bd4jR","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@\n+syntax = \"proto3\";\n+\n+package module_orchestrator.v1.directory;\n+\n+import \"google/protobuf/empty.proto\";\n+\n+// DirectoryService provides service discovery for gRPC services.\n+// OoP modules use this to register themselves and discover other services.\n+service DirectoryService {\n+  // Resolve a gRPC service name to an endpoint URI\n+  rpc ResolveGrpcService(ResolveGrpcServiceRequest) returns (ResolveGrpcServiceResponse);","path":"proto/directory/v1/directory.proto","commit_id":"3df73358ee3583a26e64dcc390d34326f023b708","original_commit_id":"89c33a1548a8c165d0b406b13bdd01cdbf35eb01","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It returns endpoint by grpc service name (string)","created_at":"2025-12-10T21:40:06Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T21:40:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/60#discussion_r2608302289","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/60","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608302289"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/60#discussion_r2608302289"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/60"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608302289/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":11,"original_line":11,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2607916634,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":11,"position":11,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608304944","pull_request_review_id":3564599238,"id":2608304944,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6bd5Mw","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,160 @@\n+//! Remote Accum Module\n+//!\n+//! A trivial example gRPC service that performs addition.\n+//! This module demonstrates the OoP (out-of-process) module pattern.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use anyhow::Result;\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use tonic::{Request, Response, Status};\n+\n+use modkit::context::ModuleCtx;\n+use modkit::contracts::{GrpcServiceModule, RegisterGrpcServiceFn};\n+use modkit_security::SecurityCtx;\n+use modkit_transport_grpc::extract_secctx;\n+\n+use crate::contracts::{RemoteAccumApi, RemoteAccumError};\n+use crate::grpc::{AccumService, AccumServiceServer, AddRequest, AddResponse, ACCUM_SERVICE_NAME};\n+\n+/// Facade modules for consumers\n+pub mod contracts {\n+    pub use remote_accum_contracts::*;\n+}\n+\n+pub mod grpc {\n+    pub use remote_accum_grpc::*; // Cargo maps remote_accum-grpc to remote_accum_grpc\n+}\n+\n+/// Remote accumulator module.\n+///\n+/// Implements the RemoteAccumApi trait to provide addition functionality.\n+/// Exposes the service via gRPC through the grpc_hub.\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"remote_accum\",\n+    capabilities = [grpc],\n+    client = crate::contracts::RemoteAccumApi\n+)]\n+pub struct RemoteAccumModule {\n+    // The local implementation wrapped as a trait object\n+    api: Arc<dyn RemoteAccumApi>,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for RemoteAccumModule {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            api: Arc::new(LocalAccumImpl),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Local implementation of the accumulator logic.\n+struct LocalAccumImpl;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl RemoteAccumApi for LocalAccumImpl {\n+    async fn add(&self, _ctx: &SecurityCtx, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, RemoteAccumError> {","path":"examples/oop-modules/remote_accum/remote_accum/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"bdf2b54a65a9c95f1626957e55c5ac3dda694663","original_commit_id":"89c33a1548a8c165d0b406b13bdd01cdbf35eb01","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"1. Yes.\r\n2. Yes. grpc client implementation should be registered in client_hub","created_at":"2025-12-10T21:41:17Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T21:41:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/60#discussion_r2608304944","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/60","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608304944"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/60#discussion_r2608304944"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/60"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608304944/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":56,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2607950581,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":56,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608425036","pull_request_review_id":3564749168,"id":2608425036,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6beWhM","diff_hunk":"@@ -208,6 +211,383 @@ Stopped ── start() ── Starting ──(await_ready? then ready.notify())\n \n ---\n \n+## Out-of-Process Modules (OoP)\n+\n+ModKit supports running modules as separate processes with gRPC-based inter-process communication. This enables:\n+\n+* **Process isolation** — modules run in separate processes for fault isolation\n+* **Language flexibility** — OoP modules can be implemented in any language (with gRPC support)\n+* **Independent scaling** — modules can be scaled independently\n+* **Gradual migration** — existing modules can be moved out-of-process without code changes\n+\n+### RuntimeKind\n+\n+Modules can run in two modes:\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default, Deserialize, Serialize, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\")]\n+pub enum RuntimeKind {\n+    #[default]\n+    Local,  // In-process (default)\n+    Oop,    // Out-of-process\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### OoP Module Configuration\n+\n+Configure OoP modules in your YAML config:\n+\n+```yaml\n+modules:\n+  remote_accum:\n+    runtime:\n+      type: oop\n+      execution:\n+        executable_path: \"~/.hyperspot/bin/remote-accum.exe\"\n+        args: []\n+        working_directory: null\n+        environment:\n+          RUST_LOG: \"info\"\n+    config:\n+      some_setting: \"value\"\n+```\n+\n+**Configuration fields:**\n+\n+* `type: oop` — marks the module as out-of-process\n+* `executable_path` — path to the module binary (supports `~` expansion)\n+* `args` — command-line arguments passed to the executable\n+* `working_directory` — optional working directory for the process\n+* `environment` — environment variables to set for the process\n+\n+### OoP Bootstrap Library\n+\n+Use `modkit_bootstrap::oop` to bootstrap OoP modules:\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_bootstrap::oop::{OopRunOptions, run_oop_with_options};\n+\n+#[tokio::main]\n+async fn main() -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+    let opts = OopRunOptions {\n+        module_name: \"my_module\".to_string(),\n+        instance_id: None,  // Auto-generated UUID\n+        directory_endpoint: \"http://127.0.0.1:50051\".to_string(),\n+        config_path: None,\n+        verbose: 0,\n+        print_config: false,\n+        heartbeat_interval_secs: 5,\n+    };\n+    \n+    run_oop_with_options(opts).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**`OopRunOptions` fields:**\n+\n+| Field | Description |\n+|-------|-------------|\n+| `module_name` | Logical module name (e.g., \"file_parser\") |\n+| `instance_id` | Instance ID (defaults to random UUID) |\n+| `directory_endpoint` | DirectoryService gRPC endpoint |\n+| `config_path` | Path to configuration file |\n+| `verbose` | Log verbosity (0=default, 1=info, 2=debug, 3=trace) |\n+| `print_config` | Print effective config and exit |\n+| `heartbeat_interval_secs` | Heartbeat interval (default: 5) |\n+\n+### OoP Lifecycle\n+\n+When an OoP module starts:\n+\n+1. **Configuration loading** — loads config from file or `MODKIT_MODULE_CONFIG` env var\n+2. **Logging initialization** — sets up tracing with optional OTEL\n+3. **DirectoryService connection** — connects to the master host's directory service\n+4. **Instance registration** — registers with DirectoryService for discovery\n+5. **Heartbeat loop** — starts background heartbeat task\n+6. **Module lifecycle** — runs the normal module lifecycle (init → migrate → start)\n+7. **Graceful shutdown** — deregisters from DirectoryService on exit\n+\n+### Shutdown Model\n+\n+Shutdown is driven by a single root `CancellationToken` per process:\n+\n+* OS signals (SIGTERM, SIGINT, Ctrl+C) are hooked at bootstrap level\n+* The root token is passed to `RunOptions::Token` for module runtime shutdown\n+* Background tasks (like heartbeat) use child tokens derived from the root\n+* On shutdown, the module deregisters itself from DirectoryService before exiting\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Module Orchestrator & Directory API\n+\n+The **Module Orchestrator** provides service discovery and instance management for both in-process and OoP modules.\n+\n+### DirectoryApi Trait\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryApi: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve a gRPC service by its logical name to an endpoint\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// List all service instances for a given module\n+    async fn list_instances(&self, module: &str) -> Result<Vec<ServiceInstanceInfo>>;\n+\n+    /// Register a new module instance with the directory\n+    async fn register_instance(&self, info: RegisterInstanceInfo) -> Result<()>;\n+\n+    /// Deregister a module instance (for graceful shutdown)\n+    async fn deregister_instance(&self, module: &str, instance_id: &str) -> Result<()>;\n+\n+    /// Send a heartbeat for a module instance to indicate it's still alive\n+    async fn send_heartbeat(&self, module: &str, instance_id: &str) -> Result<()>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Service Endpoint Types\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents an endpoint where a service can be reached\n+pub struct ServiceEndpoint {\n+    pub uri: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl ServiceEndpoint {\n+    pub fn tcp(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self;  // \"http://host:port\"\n+    pub fn uds(path: impl AsRef<Path>) -> Self; // \"unix:///path/to/socket\"\n+}\n+\n+/// Information about a service instance\n+pub struct ServiceInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub endpoint: ServiceEndpoint,\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+\n+/// Information for registering a new module instance\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Using DirectoryApi\n+\n+**From an OoP module** — the DirectoryApi client is injected into the ClientHub:\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+    // DirectoryApi is available via ClientHub in OoP modules\n+    let directory = ctx.client_hub.get::<dyn DirectoryApi>()?;\n+    \n+    // Resolve another service's endpoint\n+    let endpoint = directory.resolve_grpc_service(\"my.package.MyService\").await?;\n+    \n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**From the master host** — the Module Orchestrator registers itself as the DirectoryApi implementation.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Backends\n+\n+Backends manage the lifecycle of out-of-process module instances.\n+\n+### BackendKind\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum BackendKind {\n+    LocalProcess,  // Spawn as local child process\n+    K8s,           // Deploy to Kubernetes (future)","path":"docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"3df73358ee3583a26e64dcc390d34326f023b708","original_commit_id":"89c33a1548a8c165d0b406b13bdd01cdbf35eb01","user":{"login":"ast2074","id":192745410,"node_id":"U_kgDOC30Pwg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192745410?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074","html_url":"https://github.com/ast2074","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"If the k8s bootstrap _backend_ impl is felt as empty or almost empty, then that just proves the statement above: \r\nk8s pod _management_ is something separate, and the same could be about local process _management_\r\n\r\nYes, features like on-demand-module-run or on-demand-module-install will require some ensure_runing() etc. functions in the backend:\r\n- with k8s there is no choice to impl them via _direct_ POD deployment or POD creation, only k8s APIs could be used\r\n- with local process deployment and management the same layerying idea could be leveraged","created_at":"2025-12-10T22:24:26Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T22:24:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/60#discussion_r2608425036","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/60","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608425036"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/60#discussion_r2608425036"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/60"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608425036/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":408,"original_line":408,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2607908674,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":211,"position":211,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608461554","pull_request_review_id":3564787291,"id":2608461554,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6befby","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@\n+syntax = \"proto3\";\n+\n+package module_orchestrator.v1.directory;\n+\n+import \"google/protobuf/empty.proto\";\n+\n+// DirectoryService provides service discovery for gRPC services.\n+// OoP modules use this to register themselves and discover other services.\n+service DirectoryService {\n+  // Resolve a gRPC service name to an endpoint URI\n+  rpc ResolveGrpcService(ResolveGrpcServiceRequest) returns (ResolveGrpcServiceResponse);","path":"proto/directory/v1/directory.proto","commit_id":"3df73358ee3583a26e64dcc390d34326f023b708","original_commit_id":"89c33a1548a8c165d0b406b13bdd01cdbf35eb01","user":{"login":"ast2074","id":192745410,"node_id":"U_kgDOC30Pwg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192745410?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074","html_url":"https://github.com/ast2074","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It could also fit to a set of REST API endpoints with common prefix / namespace (e.g. REST API of user management service etc.), or to a set of GraphQL schemas for the specific domain.\r\nI.e. if define 'service' not from impl perspective, but from the client perspective as 'a cohesive set of functions' or as a 'domain interface', then your directory service would be universal service registry for all the API options.","created_at":"2025-12-10T22:41:27Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T22:41:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/60#discussion_r2608461554","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/60","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608461554"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/60#discussion_r2608461554"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/60"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608461554/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":11,"original_line":11,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2607916634,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":11,"position":11,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608480939","pull_request_review_id":3564810431,"id":2608480939,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6bekKr","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,160 @@\n+//! Remote Accum Module\n+//!\n+//! A trivial example gRPC service that performs addition.\n+//! This module demonstrates the OoP (out-of-process) module pattern.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use anyhow::Result;\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use tonic::{Request, Response, Status};\n+\n+use modkit::context::ModuleCtx;\n+use modkit::contracts::{GrpcServiceModule, RegisterGrpcServiceFn};\n+use modkit_security::SecurityCtx;\n+use modkit_transport_grpc::extract_secctx;\n+\n+use crate::contracts::{RemoteAccumApi, RemoteAccumError};\n+use crate::grpc::{AccumService, AccumServiceServer, AddRequest, AddResponse, ACCUM_SERVICE_NAME};\n+\n+/// Facade modules for consumers\n+pub mod contracts {\n+    pub use remote_accum_contracts::*;\n+}\n+\n+pub mod grpc {\n+    pub use remote_accum_grpc::*; // Cargo maps remote_accum-grpc to remote_accum_grpc\n+}\n+\n+/// Remote accumulator module.\n+///\n+/// Implements the RemoteAccumApi trait to provide addition functionality.\n+/// Exposes the service via gRPC through the grpc_hub.\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"remote_accum\",\n+    capabilities = [grpc],\n+    client = crate::contracts::RemoteAccumApi\n+)]\n+pub struct RemoteAccumModule {\n+    // The local implementation wrapped as a trait object\n+    api: Arc<dyn RemoteAccumApi>,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for RemoteAccumModule {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            api: Arc::new(LocalAccumImpl),\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Local implementation of the accumulator logic.\n+struct LocalAccumImpl;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl RemoteAccumApi for LocalAccumImpl {\n+    async fn add(&self, _ctx: &SecurityCtx, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, RemoteAccumError> {","path":"examples/oop-modules/remote_accum/remote_accum/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"bdf2b54a65a9c95f1626957e55c5ac3dda694663","original_commit_id":"89c33a1548a8c165d0b406b13bdd01cdbf35eb01","user":{"login":"ast2074","id":192745410,"node_id":"U_kgDOC30Pwg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192745410?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074","html_url":"https://github.com/ast2074","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ast2074/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It would be nice to have a client module examples too: \r\n- client module working with local server module\r\n- client module working with same server module remotely\r\nDid i missed them?\r\n\r\nlocal_accum and remote_accum examples look like the examples of server module, packed to use locally or remotely...\r\nBut their local_accum-contracts and remote_accum-contracts are different.\r\nThen how could they be consumed by the same client without changing its code?","created_at":"2025-12-10T22:50:36Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T22:50:37Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/60#discussion_r2608480939","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/60","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608480939"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/60#discussion_r2608480939"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/60"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2608480939/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":56,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2607950581,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":56,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2611690911","pull_request_review_id":3568837398,"id":2611690911,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6bqz2f","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@\n+syntax = \"proto3\";\n+\n+package module_orchestrator.v1.directory;\n+\n+import \"google/protobuf/empty.proto\";\n+\n+// DirectoryService provides service discovery for gRPC services.\n+// OoP modules use this to register themselves and discover other services.\n+service DirectoryService {\n+  // Resolve a gRPC service name to an endpoint URI\n+  rpc ResolveGrpcService(ResolveGrpcServiceRequest) returns (ResolveGrpcServiceResponse);","path":"proto/directory/v1/directory.proto","commit_id":"3df73358ee3583a26e64dcc390d34326f023b708","original_commit_id":"89c33a1548a8c165d0b406b13bdd01cdbf35eb01","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.gith