as_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["account-management","agentic-ai","ai","benchmarks","cloud","genai","llm","microservices","middleware","modkit","multi-tenancy","multi-tier","rust","saas","security","serverless","xaas"],"visibility":"private","forks":19,"open_issues":263,"watchers":32,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/23"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/23/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/0d71046f6fb9cb219931678fdf8dbe13f050c631"}},"author_association":"MEMBER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483914256","pull_request_review_id":3407722500,"id":2483914256,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6UDYYQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,563 +1,279 @@\n-# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\r\n-\r\n-## Quick Start\r\n-\r\n-### Prerequisites\r\n-\r\n-- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\r\n-- **Git** for version control\r\n-- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\r\n-\r\n-### Development Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Clone the repository\r\n-git clone <repository-url>\r\n-cd hyperspot\r\n-\r\n-# Install Rust (if not already installed)\r\n-curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\r\n-\r\n-# Install required components\r\n-rustup component add clippy rustfmt\r\n-\r\n-# Build the project\r\n-cargo build\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-cargo test\r\n-\r\n-# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\r\n-cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Workspace Layout\r\n-\r\n-```\r\n-hyperspot/\r\n-├── apps/\r\n-│   └── hyperspot-server/     # Main server binary\r\n-├── modules/\r\n-│   └── api_ingress/          # HTTP gateway and OpenAPI provider\r\n-\r\n-├── libs/\r\n-│   ├── modkit/               # Core framework and traits\r\n-│   ├── db/                   # Database abstraction layer\r\n-│   └── runtime/              # Runtime utilities and config\r\n-├── config/                   # Configuration files\r\n-└── docs/                     # Documentation\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Development Workflow\r\n-\r\n-### 1. Create a Feature Branch\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Use descriptive branch names:\r\n-- `feature/user-authentication`\r\n-- `fix/memory-leak-in-router`\r\n-- `docs/api-gateway-examples`\r\n-- `refactor/entity-to-contract-conversions`\r\n-\r\n-### 2. Make Your Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow the coding standards and patterns described below.\r\n-\r\n-### 3. Run Quality Checks\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Format code (check only)\r\n-make fmt\r\n-\r\n-# Lint (deny warnings)\r\n-make clippy\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-make test\r\n-\r\n-# Full check (fmt + clippy + test + security)\r\n-make check\r\n-\r\n-# Security checks\r\n-make audit\r\n-make deny\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### 4. Commit Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow a structured commit message format:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-<type>(<module>): <description>\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-- `<type>`: change category (see table below)\r\n-- `<module>` (optional): the area touched (e.g., api_ingress, modkit, ecommerce)\r\n-- `<description>`: concise, imperative summary\r\n-\r\n-Accepted commit types:\r\n-\r\n-| Type       | Meaning                                                     |\r\n-|------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|\r\n-| feat       | A new feature                                               |\r\n-| fix        | A bug fix                                                   |\r\n-| tech       | A technical improvement                                     |\r\n-| cleanup    | Code cleanup                                                |\r\n-| refactor   | Code restructuring without functional changes               |\r\n-| test       | Adding or modifying tests                                   |\r\n-| docs       | Documentation updates                                       |\r\n-| style      | Code style changes (whitespace, formatting, etc.)           |\r\n-| chore      | Misc tasks (deps, tooling, scripts)                         |\r\n-| perf       | Performance improvements                                    |\r\n-| ci         | CI/CD configuration changes                                 |\r\n-| build      | Build system or dependency changes                          |\r\n-| revert     | Reverting a previous commit                                 |\r\n-| security   | Security fixes                                              |\r\n-| breaking   | Backward incompatible changes                               |\r\n-\r\n-Examples:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-feat(auth): add OAuth2 support for login\r\n-fix(ui): resolve button alignment issue on mobile\r\n-tech(database): add error abstraction for database and API errors\r\n-refactor(database): optimize query execution\r\n-test(api): add unit tests for user authentication\r\n-docs(readme): update installation instructions\r\n-style(css): apply consistent spacing in stylesheet\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Best practices:\r\n-\r\n-- Keep the title concise (ideally ≤ 50 chars)\r\n-- Use imperative mood (e.g., \"Fix bug\", not \"Fixed bug\")\r\n-- Make commits atomic (one logical change per commit)\r\n-- Add details in the body when necessary (what/why, not how)\r\n-- For breaking changes, either use `feat!:`/`fix!:` or include a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer\r\n-\r\n-New functionality development:\r\n-\r\n-- Follow the repository structure in `README.md`\r\n-- Prefer soft-deletion for entities; provide hard-deletion with retention routines\r\n-- Include unit tests (and integration tests when relevant)\r\n-\r\n-### 5. Push and Create PR\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git push origin feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Then create a Pull Request on GitHub with:\r\n-- Clear title and description\r\n-- Reference to related issues\r\n-- Test coverage information\r\n-- Breaking changes (if any)\r\n-\r\n-## Architecture Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Module Development\r\n-\r\n-#### Creating a New Module\r\n-\r\n-1. **Create module directory**:\r\n-   ```bash\r\n-   mkdir modules/my_module\r\n-   cd modules/my_module\r\n-   cargo init --lib\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Define module structure**:\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### API Design Standards\r\n-\r\n-#### REST Endpoint Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Use consistent resource naming**:\r\n-   - `/users` (plural nouns)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}` (path parameters)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}/posts` (nested resources)\r\n-\r\n-2. **HTTP methods**:\r\n-   - `GET` for reading data\r\n-   - `POST` for creating resources\r\n-   - `PUT` for updating entire resources\r\n-   - `PATCH` for partial updates\r\n-   - `DELETE` for removing resources\r\n-\r\n-3. **Status codes**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Success responses\r\n-   200 OK              // Successful GET, PUT, PATCH\r\n-   201 Created         // Successful POST\r\n-   204 No Content      // Successful DELETE\r\n-   \r\n-   // Client error responses\r\n-   400 Bad Request     // Invalid request data\r\n-   401 Unauthorized    // Authentication required\r\n-   403 Forbidden       // Insufficient permissions\r\n-   404 Not Found       // Resource doesn't exist\r\n-   409 Conflict        // Resource conflict\r\n-   422 Unprocessable   // Validation errors\r\n-   \r\n-   // Server error responses\r\n-   500 Internal Error  // Unexpected server error\r\n-   501 Not Implemented // Handler not implemented\r\n-   503 Service Unavail // Service temporarily down\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-#### Schema Design\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-## Testing Standards\r\n-\r\n-### Unit Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD \r\n-\r\n-### Integration Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### Test Coverage\r\n-\r\n-Aim for high test coverage:\r\n-- **Unit tests**: Test individual functions and methods\r\n-- **Integration tests**: Test module interactions\r\n-- **End-to-end tests**: Test complete request flows\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run tests with coverage (requires tarpaulin)\r\n-cargo install cargo-tarpaulin\r\n-cargo tarpaulin --out html\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Code Style\r\n-\r\n-### Formatting\r\n-\r\n-Use `rustfmt` with the project configuration:\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-cargo fmt -all\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Key formatting rules:\r\n-- **Line length**: 100 characters max\r\n-- **Indentation**: 4 spaces (no tabs)\r\n-- **Trailing commas**: Required in multi-line expressions\r\n-\r\n-### Naming Conventions\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Types: PascalCase\r\n-struct UserService;\r\n-enum ResponseStatus;\r\n-\r\n-// Functions and variables: snake_case\r\n-fn create_user() {}\r\n-let user_name = \"Alice\";\r\n-\r\n-// Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\r\n-const MAX_RETRIES: u32 = 3;\r\n-const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(30);\r\n-\r\n-// Module names: snake_case\r\n-mod user_service;\r\n-mod api_client;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Documentation\r\n-\r\n-#### Rustdoc Comments\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Service for managing user accounts\r\n-/// \r\n-/// Provides CRUD operations for users with proper validation\r\n-/// and error handling. All operations are async and thread-safe.\r\n-/// \r\n-/// # Examples\r\n-/// \r\n-/// ```rust\r\n-/// let service = UserService::new(db_pool);\r\n-/// let user = service.get_user(123).await?;\r\n-/// println!(\"User: {}\", user.name);\r\n-/// ```\r\n-pub struct UserService {\r\n-    /// Database connection pool\r\n-    pool: Arc<DbPool>,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-impl UserService {\r\n-    /// Create a new user with the given details\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Arguments\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `request` - User creation data including name and email\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Returns\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// Returns the created user with assigned ID, or an error if\r\n-    /// validation fails or the email already exists.\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Errors\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `ValidationError` - Invalid input data\r\n-    /// * `ConflictError` - Email already registered\r\n-    /// * `DatabaseError` - Database operation failed\r\n-    pub async fn create_user(&self, request: CreateUserRequest) -> Result<User, UserError> {\r\n-        // Implementation\r\n-    }\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-#### Error Documentation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Errors that can occur during user operations\r\n-#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\r\n-pub enum UserError {\r\n-    /// User input validation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\r\n-    Validation { message: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// User with given email already exists\r\n-    #[error(\"User with email {email} already exists\")]\r\n-    Conflict { email: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// Database operation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Database error: {0}\")]\r\n-    Database(#[from] sqlx::Error),\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Error Handling\r\n-\r\n-Use `anyhow` for application errors and `thiserror` for library errors:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use anyhow::{Context, Result};\r\n-\r\n-pub async fn process_user(id: u64) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    let user = database::get_user(id)\r\n-        .await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user from database\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    validate_user(&user)\r\n-        .context(\"User validation failed\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Performance Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Avoid blocking operations** in async context:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: blocking in async\r\n-   async fn bad_handler() {\r\n-       let data = std::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").unwrap();\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: use async I/O\r\n-   async fn good_handler() {\r\n-       let data = tokio::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").await?;\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Use efficient data structures**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: unnecessary allocations\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<String> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.clone()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: avoid clones when possible\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<&str> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.as_str()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-3. **Use appropriate synchronization**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Short-lived locks\r\n-   use parking_lot::{RwLock, Mutex};\r\n-   \r\n-   // Long-running async operations\r\n-   use tokio::sync::{RwLock as AsyncRwLock, Mutex as AsyncMutex};\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-## Debugging\r\n-\r\n-### Logging\r\n-\r\n-Use structured logging with `tracing`:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use tracing::{info, warn, error, debug, trace};\r\n-\r\n-#[tracing::instrument(skip(db))]\r\n-async fn process_user(user_id: u64, db: &Database) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    debug!(user_id, \"Starting user processing\");\r\n-    \r\n-    let user = db.get_user(user_id).await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    info!(user_id, user_name = %user.name, \"User retrieved successfully\");\r\n-    \r\n-    if user.is_inactive() {\r\n-        warn!(user_id, \"Processing inactive user\");\r\n-    }\r\n-    \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Environment Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Enable debug logging\r\n-export RUST_LOG=debug\r\n-\r\n-# Enable backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=1\r\n-\r\n-# For detailed backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=full\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Testing Tools\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run specific test\r\n-cargo test test_user_creation\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests with output\r\n-cargo test -- --nocapture\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests in single thread\r\n-cargo test -- --test-threads=1\r\n-\r\n-# Run ignored tests\r\n-cargo test -- --ignored\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Pull Request Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### PR Description Template\r\n-\r\n-```markdown\r\n-## Description\r\n-Brief description of the changes made.\r\n-\r\n-## Type of Change\r\n-- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n-- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n-- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\r\n-- [ ] Documentation update\r\n-\r\n-## Testing\r\n-- [ ] Unit tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Integration tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Manual testing completed\r\n-- [ ] New tests added for new functionality\r\n-\r\n-## Documentation\r\n-- [ ] Code is documented with rustdoc comments\r\n-- [ ] README updated (if applicable)\r\n-- [ ] API documentation updated (if applicable)\r\n-\r\n-## Checklist\r\n-- [ ] Code follows project style guidelines\r\n-- [ ] Self-review completed\r\n-- [ ] No linting errors (`cargo clippy`)\r\n-- [ ] Code is properly formatted (`cargo fmt`)\r\n-- [ ] Tests pass (`cargo test`)\r\n-\r\n-## Related Issues\r\n-Closes #issue_number\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Review Process\r\n-\r\n-1. **Automated checks** must pass (CI/CD pipeline)\r\n-2. **At least one approval** from maintainer required\r\n-3. **All conversations resolved** before merge\r\n-4. **Up-to-date with main** branch\r\n-\r\n-### Merge Strategy\r\n-\r\n-- **Squash and merge** for feature branches\r\n-- **Rebase and merge** for simple fixes\r\n-- **Merge commit** for release branches\r\n-\r\n-## Security Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Input Validation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use validator::{Validate, ValidationError};\r\n-\r\n-#[derive(Deserialize, Validate)]\r\n-pub struct CreateUserRequest {\r\n-    #[validate(length(min = 1, max = 100))]\r\n-    pub name: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(email)]\r\n-    pub email: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(custom = \"validate_password\")]\r\n-    pub password: String,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-fn validate_password(password: &str) -> Result<(), ValidationError> {\r\n-    if password.len() < 8 {\r\n-        return Err(ValidationError::new(\"Password too short\"));\r\n-    }\r\n-    Ok(())\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Secrets Management\r\n-\r\n-- **Never commit secrets** to version control\r\n-- **Use environment variables** for configuration\r\n-- **Rotate secrets regularly**\r\n-- **Use secure random generation** for tokens\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Bad: hardcoded secret\r\n-const API_KEY: &str = \"sk-1234567890abcdef\";\r\n-\r\n-// Good: environment variable\r\n-let api_key = std::env::var(\"API_KEY\")\r\n-    .context(\"API_KEY environment variable not set\")?;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Getting Help\r\n-\r\n-- **GitHub Issues**: For bug reports and feature requests\r\n-- **GitHub Discussions**: For questions and general discussion\r\n-- **Documentation**: Check existing docs first\r\n-- **Code Examples**: Look at existing modules for patterns\r\n-\r\n-## Contribution Areas\r\n-\r\n-We welcome contributions in:\r\n-\r\n-- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\r\n-- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\r\n-- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\r\n-- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\r\n-- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\r\n-- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for contributing to HyperSpot Server!\r\n+# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\n+\n+Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\n+\n+We welcome contributions in:\n+\n+- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\n+- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\n+- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\n+- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\n+- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\n+- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\n+\n+\n+## 1. Quick Start\n+\n+### 1.1 Prerequisites\n+\n+- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\n+- **Git** for version control\n+- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\n+\n+### 1.2 Development Setup\n+\n+```bash\n+# Clone the repository\n+git clone <repository-url>\n+cd hyperspot\n+\n+# Install Rust (if not already installed)\n+curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\n+\n+# Install required components\n+rustup component add clippy rustfmt\n+\n+# Build the project\n+cargo build\n+\n+# Run tests\n+cargo test\n+\n+# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\n+cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run","path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","original_commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","user":{"login":"modcrafter77","id":216291417,"node_id":"U_kgDODORYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216291417?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77","html_url":"https://github.com/modcrafter77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"For now we have no modules (except system like api_ingress) And If client wants to run  example project he should  to add --features=users-info-example (BEFORE --)\r\n\r\n","created_at":"2025-11-01T21:00:53Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T23:10:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483914256","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483914256"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483914256"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483914256/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":43,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":606,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483914704","pull_request_review_id":3407722500,"id":2483914704,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6UDYfQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,563 +1,279 @@\n-# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\r\n-\r\n-## Quick Start\r\n-\r\n-### Prerequisites\r\n-\r\n-- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\r\n-- **Git** for version control\r\n-- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\r\n-\r\n-### Development Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Clone the repository\r\n-git clone <repository-url>\r\n-cd hyperspot\r\n-\r\n-# Install Rust (if not already installed)\r\n-curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\r\n-\r\n-# Install required components\r\n-rustup component add clippy rustfmt\r\n-\r\n-# Build the project\r\n-cargo build\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-cargo test\r\n-\r\n-# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\r\n-cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Workspace Layout\r\n-\r\n-```\r\n-hyperspot/\r\n-├── apps/\r\n-│   └── hyperspot-server/     # Main server binary\r\n-├── modules/\r\n-│   └── api_ingress/          # HTTP gateway and OpenAPI provider\r\n-\r\n-├── libs/\r\n-│   ├── modkit/               # Core framework and traits\r\n-│   ├── db/                   # Database abstraction layer\r\n-│   └── runtime/              # Runtime utilities and config\r\n-├── config/                   # Configuration files\r\n-└── docs/                     # Documentation\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Development Workflow\r\n-\r\n-### 1. Create a Feature Branch\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Use descriptive branch names:\r\n-- `feature/user-authentication`\r\n-- `fix/memory-leak-in-router`\r\n-- `docs/api-gateway-examples`\r\n-- `refactor/entity-to-contract-conversions`\r\n-\r\n-### 2. Make Your Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow the coding standards and patterns described below.\r\n-\r\n-### 3. Run Quality Checks\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Format code (check only)\r\n-make fmt\r\n-\r\n-# Lint (deny warnings)\r\n-make clippy\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-make test\r\n-\r\n-# Full check (fmt + clippy + test + security)\r\n-make check\r\n-\r\n-# Security checks\r\n-make audit\r\n-make deny\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### 4. Commit Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow a structured commit message format:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-<type>(<module>): <description>\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-- `<type>`: change category (see table below)\r\n-- `<module>` (optional): the area touched (e.g., api_ingress, modkit, ecommerce)\r\n-- `<description>`: concise, imperative summary\r\n-\r\n-Accepted commit types:\r\n-\r\n-| Type       | Meaning                                                     |\r\n-|------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|\r\n-| feat       | A new feature                                               |\r\n-| fix        | A bug fix                                                   |\r\n-| tech       | A technical improvement                                     |\r\n-| cleanup    | Code cleanup                                                |\r\n-| refactor   | Code restructuring without functional changes               |\r\n-| test       | Adding or modifying tests                                   |\r\n-| docs       | Documentation updates                                       |\r\n-| style      | Code style changes (whitespace, formatting, etc.)           |\r\n-| chore      | Misc tasks (deps, tooling, scripts)                         |\r\n-| perf       | Performance improvements                                    |\r\n-| ci         | CI/CD configuration changes                                 |\r\n-| build      | Build system or dependency changes                          |\r\n-| revert     | Reverting a previous commit                                 |\r\n-| security   | Security fixes                                              |\r\n-| breaking   | Backward incompatible changes                               |\r\n-\r\n-Examples:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-feat(auth): add OAuth2 support for login\r\n-fix(ui): resolve button alignment issue on mobile\r\n-tech(database): add error abstraction for database and API errors\r\n-refactor(database): optimize query execution\r\n-test(api): add unit tests for user authentication\r\n-docs(readme): update installation instructions\r\n-style(css): apply consistent spacing in stylesheet\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Best practices:\r\n-\r\n-- Keep the title concise (ideally ≤ 50 chars)\r\n-- Use imperative mood (e.g., \"Fix bug\", not \"Fixed bug\")\r\n-- Make commits atomic (one logical change per commit)\r\n-- Add details in the body when necessary (what/why, not how)\r\n-- For breaking changes, either use `feat!:`/`fix!:` or include a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer\r\n-\r\n-New functionality development:\r\n-\r\n-- Follow the repository structure in `README.md`\r\n-- Prefer soft-deletion for entities; provide hard-deletion with retention routines\r\n-- Include unit tests (and integration tests when relevant)\r\n-\r\n-### 5. Push and Create PR\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git push origin feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Then create a Pull Request on GitHub with:\r\n-- Clear title and description\r\n-- Reference to related issues\r\n-- Test coverage information\r\n-- Breaking changes (if any)\r\n-\r\n-## Architecture Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Module Development\r\n-\r\n-#### Creating a New Module\r\n-\r\n-1. **Create module directory**:\r\n-   ```bash\r\n-   mkdir modules/my_module\r\n-   cd modules/my_module\r\n-   cargo init --lib\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Define module structure**:\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### API Design Standards\r\n-\r\n-#### REST Endpoint Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Use consistent resource naming**:\r\n-   - `/users` (plural nouns)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}` (path parameters)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}/posts` (nested resources)\r\n-\r\n-2. **HTTP methods**:\r\n-   - `GET` for reading data\r\n-   - `POST` for creating resources\r\n-   - `PUT` for updating entire resources\r\n-   - `PATCH` for partial updates\r\n-   - `DELETE` for removing resources\r\n-\r\n-3. **Status codes**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Success responses\r\n-   200 OK              // Successful GET, PUT, PATCH\r\n-   201 Created         // Successful POST\r\n-   204 No Content      // Successful DELETE\r\n-   \r\n-   // Client error responses\r\n-   400 Bad Request     // Invalid request data\r\n-   401 Unauthorized    // Authentication required\r\n-   403 Forbidden       // Insufficient permissions\r\n-   404 Not Found       // Resource doesn't exist\r\n-   409 Conflict        // Resource conflict\r\n-   422 Unprocessable   // Validation errors\r\n-   \r\n-   // Server error responses\r\n-   500 Internal Error  // Unexpected server error\r\n-   501 Not Implemented // Handler not implemented\r\n-   503 Service Unavail // Service temporarily down\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-#### Schema Design\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-## Testing Standards\r\n-\r\n-### Unit Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD \r\n-\r\n-### Integration Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### Test Coverage\r\n-\r\n-Aim for high test coverage:\r\n-- **Unit tests**: Test individual functions and methods\r\n-- **Integration tests**: Test module interactions\r\n-- **End-to-end tests**: Test complete request flows\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run tests with coverage (requires tarpaulin)\r\n-cargo install cargo-tarpaulin\r\n-cargo tarpaulin --out html\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Code Style\r\n-\r\n-### Formatting\r\n-\r\n-Use `rustfmt` with the project configuration:\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-cargo fmt -all\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Key formatting rules:\r\n-- **Line length**: 100 characters max\r\n-- **Indentation**: 4 spaces (no tabs)\r\n-- **Trailing commas**: Required in multi-line expressions\r\n-\r\n-### Naming Conventions\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Types: PascalCase\r\n-struct UserService;\r\n-enum ResponseStatus;\r\n-\r\n-// Functions and variables: snake_case\r\n-fn create_user() {}\r\n-let user_name = \"Alice\";\r\n-\r\n-// Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\r\n-const MAX_RETRIES: u32 = 3;\r\n-const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(30);\r\n-\r\n-// Module names: snake_case\r\n-mod user_service;\r\n-mod api_client;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Documentation\r\n-\r\n-#### Rustdoc Comments\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Service for managing user accounts\r\n-/// \r\n-/// Provides CRUD operations for users with proper validation\r\n-/// and error handling. All operations are async and thread-safe.\r\n-/// \r\n-/// # Examples\r\n-/// \r\n-/// ```rust\r\n-/// let service = UserService::new(db_pool);\r\n-/// let user = service.get_user(123).await?;\r\n-/// println!(\"User: {}\", user.name);\r\n-/// ```\r\n-pub struct UserService {\r\n-    /// Database connection pool\r\n-    pool: Arc<DbPool>,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-impl UserService {\r\n-    /// Create a new user with the given details\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Arguments\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `request` - User creation data including name and email\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Returns\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// Returns the created user with assigned ID, or an error if\r\n-    /// validation fails or the email already exists.\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Errors\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `ValidationError` - Invalid input data\r\n-    /// * `ConflictError` - Email already registered\r\n-    /// * `DatabaseError` - Database operation failed\r\n-    pub async fn create_user(&self, request: CreateUserRequest) -> Result<User, UserError> {\r\n-        // Implementation\r\n-    }\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-#### Error Documentation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Errors that can occur during user operations\r\n-#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\r\n-pub enum UserError {\r\n-    /// User input validation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\r\n-    Validation { message: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// User with given email already exists\r\n-    #[error(\"User with email {email} already exists\")]\r\n-    Conflict { email: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// Database operation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Database error: {0}\")]\r\n-    Database(#[from] sqlx::Error),\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Error Handling\r\n-\r\n-Use `anyhow` for application errors and `thiserror` for library errors:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use anyhow::{Context, Result};\r\n-\r\n-pub async fn process_user(id: u64) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    let user = database::get_user(id)\r\n-        .await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user from database\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    validate_user(&user)\r\n-        .context(\"User validation failed\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Performance Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Avoid blocking operations** in async context:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: blocking in async\r\n-   async fn bad_handler() {\r\n-       let data = std::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").unwrap();\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: use async I/O\r\n-   async fn good_handler() {\r\n-       let data = tokio::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").await?;\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Use efficient data structures**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: unnecessary allocations\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<String> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.clone()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: avoid clones when possible\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<&str> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.as_str()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-3. **Use appropriate synchronization**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Short-lived locks\r\n-   use parking_lot::{RwLock, Mutex};\r\n-   \r\n-   // Long-running async operations\r\n-   use tokio::sync::{RwLock as AsyncRwLock, Mutex as AsyncMutex};\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-## Debugging\r\n-\r\n-### Logging\r\n-\r\n-Use structured logging with `tracing`:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use tracing::{info, warn, error, debug, trace};\r\n-\r\n-#[tracing::instrument(skip(db))]\r\n-async fn process_user(user_id: u64, db: &Database) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    debug!(user_id, \"Starting user processing\");\r\n-    \r\n-    let user = db.get_user(user_id).await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    info!(user_id, user_name = %user.name, \"User retrieved successfully\");\r\n-    \r\n-    if user.is_inactive() {\r\n-        warn!(user_id, \"Processing inactive user\");\r\n-    }\r\n-    \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Environment Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Enable debug logging\r\n-export RUST_LOG=debug\r\n-\r\n-# Enable backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=1\r\n-\r\n-# For detailed backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=full\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Testing Tools\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run specific test\r\n-cargo test test_user_creation\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests with output\r\n-cargo test -- --nocapture\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests in single thread\r\n-cargo test -- --test-threads=1\r\n-\r\n-# Run ignored tests\r\n-cargo test -- --ignored\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Pull Request Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### PR Description Template\r\n-\r\n-```markdown\r\n-## Description\r\n-Brief description of the changes made.\r\n-\r\n-## Type of Change\r\n-- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n-- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n-- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\r\n-- [ ] Documentation update\r\n-\r\n-## Testing\r\n-- [ ] Unit tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Integration tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Manual testing completed\r\n-- [ ] New tests added for new functionality\r\n-\r\n-## Documentation\r\n-- [ ] Code is documented with rustdoc comments\r\n-- [ ] README updated (if applicable)\r\n-- [ ] API documentation updated (if applicable)\r\n-\r\n-## Checklist\r\n-- [ ] Code follows project style guidelines\r\n-- [ ] Self-review completed\r\n-- [ ] No linting errors (`cargo clippy`)\r\n-- [ ] Code is properly formatted (`cargo fmt`)\r\n-- [ ] Tests pass (`cargo test`)\r\n-\r\n-## Related Issues\r\n-Closes #issue_number\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Review Process\r\n-\r\n-1. **Automated checks** must pass (CI/CD pipeline)\r\n-2. **At least one approval** from maintainer required\r\n-3. **All conversations resolved** before merge\r\n-4. **Up-to-date with main** branch\r\n-\r\n-### Merge Strategy\r\n-\r\n-- **Squash and merge** for feature branches\r\n-- **Rebase and merge** for simple fixes\r\n-- **Merge commit** for release branches\r\n-\r\n-## Security Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Input Validation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use validator::{Validate, ValidationError};\r\n-\r\n-#[derive(Deserialize, Validate)]\r\n-pub struct CreateUserRequest {\r\n-    #[validate(length(min = 1, max = 100))]\r\n-    pub name: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(email)]\r\n-    pub email: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(custom = \"validate_password\")]\r\n-    pub password: String,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-fn validate_password(password: &str) -> Result<(), ValidationError> {\r\n-    if password.len() < 8 {\r\n-        return Err(ValidationError::new(\"Password too short\"));\r\n-    }\r\n-    Ok(())\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Secrets Management\r\n-\r\n-- **Never commit secrets** to version control\r\n-- **Use environment variables** for configuration\r\n-- **Rotate secrets regularly**\r\n-- **Use secure random generation** for tokens\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Bad: hardcoded secret\r\n-const API_KEY: &str = \"sk-1234567890abcdef\";\r\n-\r\n-// Good: environment variable\r\n-let api_key = std::env::var(\"API_KEY\")\r\n-    .context(\"API_KEY environment variable not set\")?;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Getting Help\r\n-\r\n-- **GitHub Issues**: For bug reports and feature requests\r\n-- **GitHub Discussions**: For questions and general discussion\r\n-- **Documentation**: Check existing docs first\r\n-- **Code Examples**: Look at existing modules for patterns\r\n-\r\n-## Contribution Areas\r\n-\r\n-We welcome contributions in:\r\n-\r\n-- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\r\n-- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\r\n-- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\r\n-- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\r\n-- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\r\n-- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for contributing to HyperSpot Server!\r\n+# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\n+\n+Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\n+\n+We welcome contributions in:\n+\n+- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\n+- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\n+- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\n+- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\n+- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\n+- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\n+\n+\n+## 1. Quick Start\n+\n+### 1.1 Prerequisites\n+\n+- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\n+- **Git** for version control\n+- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\n+\n+### 1.2 Development Setup\n+\n+```bash\n+# Clone the repository\n+git clone <repository-url>\n+cd hyperspot\n+\n+# Install Rust (if not already installed)\n+curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\n+\n+# Install required components\n+rustup component add clippy rustfmt\n+\n+# Build the project\n+cargo build\n+\n+# Run tests\n+cargo test\n+\n+# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\n+cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run","path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","original_commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","user":{"login":"modcrafter77","id":216291417,"node_id":"U_kgDODORYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216291417?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77","html_url":"https://github.com/modcrafter77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"second run is redundant at the end of command ","created_at":"2025-11-01T21:02:28Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T21:08:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483914704","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483914704"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483914704"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483914704/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":43,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":606,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483915277","pull_request_review_id":3407722500,"id":2483915277,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6UDYoN","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,563 +1,279 @@\n-# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\r\n-\r\n-## Quick Start\r\n-\r\n-### Prerequisites\r\n-\r\n-- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\r\n-- **Git** for version control\r\n-- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\r\n-\r\n-### Development Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Clone the repository\r\n-git clone <repository-url>\r\n-cd hyperspot\r\n-\r\n-# Install Rust (if not already installed)\r\n-curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\r\n-\r\n-# Install required components\r\n-rustup component add clippy rustfmt\r\n-\r\n-# Build the project\r\n-cargo build\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-cargo test\r\n-\r\n-# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\r\n-cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Workspace Layout\r\n-\r\n-```\r\n-hyperspot/\r\n-├── apps/\r\n-│   └── hyperspot-server/     # Main server binary\r\n-├── modules/\r\n-│   └── api_ingress/          # HTTP gateway and OpenAPI provider\r\n-\r\n-├── libs/\r\n-│   ├── modkit/               # Core framework and traits\r\n-│   ├── db/                   # Database abstraction layer\r\n-│   └── runtime/              # Runtime utilities and config\r\n-├── config/                   # Configuration files\r\n-└── docs/                     # Documentation\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Development Workflow\r\n-\r\n-### 1. Create a Feature Branch\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Use descriptive branch names:\r\n-- `feature/user-authentication`\r\n-- `fix/memory-leak-in-router`\r\n-- `docs/api-gateway-examples`\r\n-- `refactor/entity-to-contract-conversions`\r\n-\r\n-### 2. Make Your Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow the coding standards and patterns described below.\r\n-\r\n-### 3. Run Quality Checks\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Format code (check only)\r\n-make fmt\r\n-\r\n-# Lint (deny warnings)\r\n-make clippy\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-make test\r\n-\r\n-# Full check (fmt + clippy + test + security)\r\n-make check\r\n-\r\n-# Security checks\r\n-make audit\r\n-make deny\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### 4. Commit Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow a structured commit message format:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-<type>(<module>): <description>\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-- `<type>`: change category (see table below)\r\n-- `<module>` (optional): the area touched (e.g., api_ingress, modkit, ecommerce)\r\n-- `<description>`: concise, imperative summary\r\n-\r\n-Accepted commit types:\r\n-\r\n-| Type       | Meaning                                                     |\r\n-|------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|\r\n-| feat       | A new feature                                               |\r\n-| fix        | A bug fix                                                   |\r\n-| tech       | A technical improvement                                     |\r\n-| cleanup    | Code cleanup                                                |\r\n-| refactor   | Code restructuring without functional changes               |\r\n-| test       | Adding or modifying tests                                   |\r\n-| docs       | Documentation updates                                       |\r\n-| style      | Code style changes (whitespace, formatting, etc.)           |\r\n-| chore      | Misc tasks (deps, tooling, scripts)                         |\r\n-| perf       | Performance improvements                                    |\r\n-| ci         | CI/CD configuration changes                                 |\r\n-| build      | Build system or dependency changes                          |\r\n-| revert     | Reverting a previous commit                                 |\r\n-| security   | Security fixes                                              |\r\n-| breaking   | Backward incompatible changes                               |\r\n-\r\n-Examples:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-feat(auth): add OAuth2 support for login\r\n-fix(ui): resolve button alignment issue on mobile\r\n-tech(database): add error abstraction for database and API errors\r\n-refactor(database): optimize query execution\r\n-test(api): add unit tests for user authentication\r\n-docs(readme): update installation instructions\r\n-style(css): apply consistent spacing in stylesheet\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Best practices:\r\n-\r\n-- Keep the title concise (ideally ≤ 50 chars)\r\n-- Use imperative mood (e.g., \"Fix bug\", not \"Fixed bug\")\r\n-- Make commits atomic (one logical change per commit)\r\n-- Add details in the body when necessary (what/why, not how)\r\n-- For breaking changes, either use `feat!:`/`fix!:` or include a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer\r\n-\r\n-New functionality development:\r\n-\r\n-- Follow the repository structure in `README.md`\r\n-- Prefer soft-deletion for entities; provide hard-deletion with retention routines\r\n-- Include unit tests (and integration tests when relevant)\r\n-\r\n-### 5. Push and Create PR\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git push origin feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Then create a Pull Request on GitHub with:\r\n-- Clear title and description\r\n-- Reference to related issues\r\n-- Test coverage information\r\n-- Breaking changes (if any)\r\n-\r\n-## Architecture Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Module Development\r\n-\r\n-#### Creating a New Module\r\n-\r\n-1. **Create module directory**:\r\n-   ```bash\r\n-   mkdir modules/my_module\r\n-   cd modules/my_module\r\n-   cargo init --lib\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Define module structure**:\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### API Design Standards\r\n-\r\n-#### REST Endpoint Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Use consistent resource naming**:\r\n-   - `/users` (plural nouns)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}` (path parameters)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}/posts` (nested resources)\r\n-\r\n-2. **HTTP methods**:\r\n-   - `GET` for reading data\r\n-   - `POST` for creating resources\r\n-   - `PUT` for updating entire resources\r\n-   - `PATCH` for partial updates\r\n-   - `DELETE` for removing resources\r\n-\r\n-3. **Status codes**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Success responses\r\n-   200 OK              // Successful GET, PUT, PATCH\r\n-   201 Created         // Successful POST\r\n-   204 No Content      // Successful DELETE\r\n-   \r\n-   // Client error responses\r\n-   400 Bad Request     // Invalid request data\r\n-   401 Unauthorized    // Authentication required\r\n-   403 Forbidden       // Insufficient permissions\r\n-   404 Not Found       // Resource doesn't exist\r\n-   409 Conflict        // Resource conflict\r\n-   422 Unprocessable   // Validation errors\r\n-   \r\n-   // Server error responses\r\n-   500 Internal Error  // Unexpected server error\r\n-   501 Not Implemented // Handler not implemented\r\n-   503 Service Unavail // Service temporarily down\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-#### Schema Design\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-## Testing Standards\r\n-\r\n-### Unit Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD \r\n-\r\n-### Integration Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### Test Coverage\r\n-\r\n-Aim for high test coverage:\r\n-- **Unit tests**: Test individual functions and methods\r\n-- **Integration tests**: Test module interactions\r\n-- **End-to-end tests**: Test complete request flows\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run tests with coverage (requires tarpaulin)\r\n-cargo install cargo-tarpaulin\r\n-cargo tarpaulin --out html\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Code Style\r\n-\r\n-### Formatting\r\n-\r\n-Use `rustfmt` with the project configuration:\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-cargo fmt -all\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Key formatting rules:\r\n-- **Line length**: 100 characters max\r\n-- **Indentation**: 4 spaces (no tabs)\r\n-- **Trailing commas**: Required in multi-line expressions\r\n-\r\n-### Naming Conventions\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Types: PascalCase\r\n-struct UserService;\r\n-enum ResponseStatus;\r\n-\r\n-// Functions and variables: snake_case\r\n-fn create_user() {}\r\n-let user_name = \"Alice\";\r\n-\r\n-// Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\r\n-const MAX_RETRIES: u32 = 3;\r\n-const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(30);\r\n-\r\n-// Module names: snake_case\r\n-mod user_service;\r\n-mod api_client;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Documentation\r\n-\r\n-#### Rustdoc Comments\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Service for managing user accounts\r\n-/// \r\n-/// Provides CRUD operations for users with proper validation\r\n-/// and error handling. All operations are async and thread-safe.\r\n-/// \r\n-/// # Examples\r\n-/// \r\n-/// ```rust\r\n-/// let service = UserService::new(db_pool);\r\n-/// let user = service.get_user(123).await?;\r\n-/// println!(\"User: {}\", user.name);\r\n-/// ```\r\n-pub struct UserService {\r\n-    /// Database connection pool\r\n-    pool: Arc<DbPool>,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-impl UserService {\r\n-    /// Create a new user with the given details\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Arguments\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `request` - User creation data including name and email\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Returns\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// Returns the created user with assigned ID, or an error if\r\n-    /// validation fails or the email already exists.\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Errors\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `ValidationError` - Invalid input data\r\n-    /// * `ConflictError` - Email already registered\r\n-    /// * `DatabaseError` - Database operation failed\r\n-    pub async fn create_user(&self, request: CreateUserRequest) -> Result<User, UserError> {\r\n-        // Implementation\r\n-    }\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-#### Error Documentation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Errors that can occur during user operations\r\n-#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\r\n-pub enum UserError {\r\n-    /// User input validation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\r\n-    Validation { message: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// User with given email already exists\r\n-    #[error(\"User with email {email} already exists\")]\r\n-    Conflict { email: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// Database operation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Database error: {0}\")]\r\n-    Database(#[from] sqlx::Error),\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Error Handling\r\n-\r\n-Use `anyhow` for application errors and `thiserror` for library errors:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use anyhow::{Context, Result};\r\n-\r\n-pub async fn process_user(id: u64) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    let user = database::get_user(id)\r\n-        .await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user from database\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    validate_user(&user)\r\n-        .context(\"User validation failed\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Performance Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Avoid blocking operations** in async context:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: blocking in async\r\n-   async fn bad_handler() {\r\n-       let data = std::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").unwrap();\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: use async I/O\r\n-   async fn good_handler() {\r\n-       let data = tokio::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").await?;\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Use efficient data structures**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: unnecessary allocations\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<String> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.clone()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: avoid clones when possible\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<&str> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.as_str()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-3. **Use appropriate synchronization**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Short-lived locks\r\n-   use parking_lot::{RwLock, Mutex};\r\n-   \r\n-   // Long-running async operations\r\n-   use tokio::sync::{RwLock as AsyncRwLock, Mutex as AsyncMutex};\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-## Debugging\r\n-\r\n-### Logging\r\n-\r\n-Use structured logging with `tracing`:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use tracing::{info, warn, error, debug, trace};\r\n-\r\n-#[tracing::instrument(skip(db))]\r\n-async fn process_user(user_id: u64, db: &Database) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    debug!(user_id, \"Starting user processing\");\r\n-    \r\n-    let user = db.get_user(user_id).await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    info!(user_id, user_name = %user.name, \"User retrieved successfully\");\r\n-    \r\n-    if user.is_inactive() {\r\n-        warn!(user_id, \"Processing inactive user\");\r\n-    }\r\n-    \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Environment Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Enable debug logging\r\n-export RUST_LOG=debug\r\n-\r\n-# Enable backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=1\r\n-\r\n-# For detailed backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=full\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Testing Tools\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run specific test\r\n-cargo test test_user_creation\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests with output\r\n-cargo test -- --nocapture\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests in single thread\r\n-cargo test -- --test-threads=1\r\n-\r\n-# Run ignored tests\r\n-cargo test -- --ignored\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Pull Request Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### PR Description Template\r\n-\r\n-```markdown\r\n-## Description\r\n-Brief description of the changes made.\r\n-\r\n-## Type of Change\r\n-- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n-- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n-- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\r\n-- [ ] Documentation update\r\n-\r\n-## Testing\r\n-- [ ] Unit tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Integration tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Manual testing completed\r\n-- [ ] New tests added for new functionality\r\n-\r\n-## Documentation\r\n-- [ ] Code is documented with rustdoc comments\r\n-- [ ] README updated (if applicable)\r\n-- [ ] API documentation updated (if applicable)\r\n-\r\n-## Checklist\r\n-- [ ] Code follows project style guidelines\r\n-- [ ] Self-review completed\r\n-- [ ] No linting errors (`cargo clippy`)\r\n-- [ ] Code is properly formatted (`cargo fmt`)\r\n-- [ ] Tests pass (`cargo test`)\r\n-\r\n-## Related Issues\r\n-Closes #issue_number\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Review Process\r\n-\r\n-1. **Automated checks** must pass (CI/CD pipeline)\r\n-2. **At least one approval** from maintainer required\r\n-3. **All conversations resolved** before merge\r\n-4. **Up-to-date with main** branch\r\n-\r\n-### Merge Strategy\r\n-\r\n-- **Squash and merge** for feature branches\r\n-- **Rebase and merge** for simple fixes\r\n-- **Merge commit** for release branches\r\n-\r\n-## Security Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Input Validation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use validator::{Validate, ValidationError};\r\n-\r\n-#[derive(Deserialize, Validate)]\r\n-pub struct CreateUserRequest {\r\n-    #[validate(length(min = 1, max = 100))]\r\n-    pub name: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(email)]\r\n-    pub email: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(custom = \"validate_password\")]\r\n-    pub password: String,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-fn validate_password(password: &str) -> Result<(), ValidationError> {\r\n-    if password.len() < 8 {\r\n-        return Err(ValidationError::new(\"Password too short\"));\r\n-    }\r\n-    Ok(())\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Secrets Management\r\n-\r\n-- **Never commit secrets** to version control\r\n-- **Use environment variables** for configuration\r\n-- **Rotate secrets regularly**\r\n-- **Use secure random generation** for tokens\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Bad: hardcoded secret\r\n-const API_KEY: &str = \"sk-1234567890abcdef\";\r\n-\r\n-// Good: environment variable\r\n-let api_key = std::env::var(\"API_KEY\")\r\n-    .context(\"API_KEY environment variable not set\")?;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Getting Help\r\n-\r\n-- **GitHub Issues**: For bug reports and feature requests\r\n-- **GitHub Discussions**: For questions and general discussion\r\n-- **Documentation**: Check existing docs first\r\n-- **Code Examples**: Look at existing modules for patterns\r\n-\r\n-## Contribution Areas\r\n-\r\n-We welcome contributions in:\r\n-\r\n-- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\r\n-- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\r\n-- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\r\n-- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\r\n-- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\r\n-- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for contributing to HyperSpot Server!\r\n+# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\n+\n+Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\n+\n+We welcome contributions in:\n+\n+- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\n+- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\n+- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\n+- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\n+- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\n+- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\n+\n+\n+## 1. Quick Start\n+\n+### 1.1 Prerequisites\n+\n+- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\n+- **Git** for version control\n+- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\n+\n+### 1.2 Development Setup\n+\n+```bash\n+# Clone the repository\n+git clone <repository-url>\n+cd hyperspot\n+\n+# Install Rust (if not already installed)\n+curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\n+\n+# Install required components\n+rustup component add clippy rustfmt\n+\n+# Build the project\n+cargo build\n+\n+# Run tests\n+cargo test\n+\n+# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\n+cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run\n+```\n+\n+## 2. Development Workflow\n+\n+### 2.1. Create a Feature Branch or Fork\n+\n+```bash\n+git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\n+```\n+\n+Use descriptive branch names:\n+- `feature/user-authentication`\n+- `fix/memory-leak-in-router`\n+- `docs/api-gateway-examples`\n+- `refactor/entity-to-contract-conversions`\n+\n+As an alternative, you can fork the repository to your own GitHub account.\n+\n+\n+### 2.2. Make Your Changes\n+\n+Follow the coding standards and guidelines:\n+\n+1. See common [RUST.md](./guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md) guideline\n+2. When develop new REST API use [API.md](./guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md), [PAGINATION](./guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md), [STATUS_CODES](./guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md)\n+3. When develop new Module use [NEW_MODULE.md](./guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md)\n+4. For PlantUML diagrams see [PlantUML.md](./guidelines/DNA/diagrams/PlantUML.md)\n+5. Security [SECURITY.md](./guidelines/SECURITY.md)\n+\n+Always include unit tests when introducing new code.\n+\n+\n+### 2.3. Run Code Quality Checks\n+\n+Key formatting rules:","path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","commit_id":"0d71046f6fb9cb219931678fdf8dbe13f050c631","original_commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","user":{"login":"modcrafter77","id":216291417,"node_id":"U_kgDODORYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216291417?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77","html_url":"https://github.com/modcrafter77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I suggest to add simple cargo fmt --all and all formatting will be fixed.","created_at":"2025-11-01T21:04:41Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T21:08:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483915277","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483915277"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483915277"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483915277/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":80,"original_line":78,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":641,"position":643,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483915446","pull_request_review_id":3407722500,"id":2483915446,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6UDYq2","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,563 +1,279 @@\n-# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\r\n-\r\n-## Quick Start\r\n-\r\n-### Prerequisites\r\n-\r\n-- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\r\n-- **Git** for version control\r\n-- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\r\n-\r\n-### Development Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Clone the repository\r\n-git clone <repository-url>\r\n-cd hyperspot\r\n-\r\n-# Install Rust (if not already installed)\r\n-curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\r\n-\r\n-# Install required components\r\n-rustup component add clippy rustfmt\r\n-\r\n-# Build the project\r\n-cargo build\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-cargo test\r\n-\r\n-# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\r\n-cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Workspace Layout\r\n-\r\n-```\r\n-hyperspot/\r\n-├── apps/\r\n-│   └── hyperspot-server/     # Main server binary\r\n-├── modules/\r\n-│   └── api_ingress/          # HTTP gateway and OpenAPI provider\r\n-\r\n-├── libs/\r\n-│   ├── modkit/               # Core framework and traits\r\n-│   ├── db/                   # Database abstraction layer\r\n-│   └── runtime/              # Runtime utilities and config\r\n-├── config/                   # Configuration files\r\n-└── docs/                     # Documentation\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Development Workflow\r\n-\r\n-### 1. Create a Feature Branch\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Use descriptive branch names:\r\n-- `feature/user-authentication`\r\n-- `fix/memory-leak-in-router`\r\n-- `docs/api-gateway-examples`\r\n-- `refactor/entity-to-contract-conversions`\r\n-\r\n-### 2. Make Your Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow the coding standards and patterns described below.\r\n-\r\n-### 3. Run Quality Checks\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Format code (check only)\r\n-make fmt\r\n-\r\n-# Lint (deny warnings)\r\n-make clippy\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-make test\r\n-\r\n-# Full check (fmt + clippy + test + security)\r\n-make check\r\n-\r\n-# Security checks\r\n-make audit\r\n-make deny\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### 4. Commit Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow a structured commit message format:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-<type>(<module>): <description>\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-- `<type>`: change category (see table below)\r\n-- `<module>` (optional): the area touched (e.g., api_ingress, modkit, ecommerce)\r\n-- `<description>`: concise, imperative summary\r\n-\r\n-Accepted commit types:\r\n-\r\n-| Type       | Meaning                                                     |\r\n-|------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|\r\n-| feat       | A new feature                                               |\r\n-| fix        | A bug fix                                                   |\r\n-| tech       | A technical improvement                                     |\r\n-| cleanup    | Code cleanup                                                |\r\n-| refactor   | Code restructuring without functional changes               |\r\n-| test       | Adding or modifying tests                                   |\r\n-| docs       | Documentation updates                                       |\r\n-| style      | Code style changes (whitespace, formatting, etc.)           |\r\n-| chore      | Misc tasks (deps, tooling, scripts)                         |\r\n-| perf       | Performance improvements                                    |\r\n-| ci         | CI/CD configuration changes                                 |\r\n-| build      | Build system or dependency changes                          |\r\n-| revert     | Reverting a previous commit                                 |\r\n-| security   | Security fixes                                              |\r\n-| breaking   | Backward incompatible changes                               |\r\n-\r\n-Examples:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-feat(auth): add OAuth2 support for login\r\n-fix(ui): resolve button alignment issue on mobile\r\n-tech(database): add error abstraction for database and API errors\r\n-refactor(database): optimize query execution\r\n-test(api): add unit tests for user authentication\r\n-docs(readme): update installation instructions\r\n-style(css): apply consistent spacing in stylesheet\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Best practices:\r\n-\r\n-- Keep the title concise (ideally ≤ 50 chars)\r\n-- Use imperative mood (e.g., \"Fix bug\", not \"Fixed bug\")\r\n-- Make commits atomic (one logical change per commit)\r\n-- Add details in the body when necessary (what/why, not how)\r\n-- For breaking changes, either use `feat!:`/`fix!:` or include a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer\r\n-\r\n-New functionality development:\r\n-\r\n-- Follow the repository structure in `README.md`\r\n-- Prefer soft-deletion for entities; provide hard-deletion with retention routines\r\n-- Include unit tests (and integration tests when relevant)\r\n-\r\n-### 5. Push and Create PR\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git push origin feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Then create a Pull Request on GitHub with:\r\n-- Clear title and description\r\n-- Reference to related issues\r\n-- Test coverage information\r\n-- Breaking changes (if any)\r\n-\r\n-## Architecture Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Module Development\r\n-\r\n-#### Creating a New Module\r\n-\r\n-1. **Create module directory**:\r\n-   ```bash\r\n-   mkdir modules/my_module\r\n-   cd modules/my_module\r\n-   cargo init --lib\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Define module structure**:\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### API Design Standards\r\n-\r\n-#### REST Endpoint Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Use consistent resource naming**:\r\n-   - `/users` (plural nouns)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}` (path parameters)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}/posts` (nested resources)\r\n-\r\n-2. **HTTP methods**:\r\n-   - `GET` for reading data\r\n-   - `POST` for creating resources\r\n-   - `PUT` for updating entire resources\r\n-   - `PATCH` for partial updates\r\n-   - `DELETE` for removing resources\r\n-\r\n-3. **Status codes**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Success responses\r\n-   200 OK              // Successful GET, PUT, PATCH\r\n-   201 Created         // Successful POST\r\n-   204 No Content      // Successful DELETE\r\n-   \r\n-   // Client error responses\r\n-   400 Bad Request     // Invalid request data\r\n-   401 Unauthorized    // Authentication required\r\n-   403 Forbidden       // Insufficient permissions\r\n-   404 Not Found       // Resource doesn't exist\r\n-   409 Conflict        // Resource conflict\r\n-   422 Unprocessable   // Validation errors\r\n-   \r\n-   // Server error responses\r\n-   500 Internal Error  // Unexpected server error\r\n-   501 Not Implemented // Handler not implemented\r\n-   503 Service Unavail // Service temporarily down\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-#### Schema Design\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-## Testing Standards\r\n-\r\n-### Unit Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD \r\n-\r\n-### Integration Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### Test Coverage\r\n-\r\n-Aim for high test coverage:\r\n-- **Unit tests**: Test individual functions and methods\r\n-- **Integration tests**: Test module interactions\r\n-- **End-to-end tests**: Test complete request flows\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run tests with coverage (requires tarpaulin)\r\n-cargo install cargo-tarpaulin\r\n-cargo tarpaulin --out html\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Code Style\r\n-\r\n-### Formatting\r\n-\r\n-Use `rustfmt` with the project configuration:\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-cargo fmt -all\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Key formatting rules:\r\n-- **Line length**: 100 characters max\r\n-- **Indentation**: 4 spaces (no tabs)\r\n-- **Trailing commas**: Required in multi-line expressions\r\n-\r\n-### Naming Conventions\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Types: PascalCase\r\n-struct UserService;\r\n-enum ResponseStatus;\r\n-\r\n-// Functions and variables: snake_case\r\n-fn create_user() {}\r\n-let user_name = \"Alice\";\r\n-\r\n-// Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\r\n-const MAX_RETRIES: u32 = 3;\r\n-const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(30);\r\n-\r\n-// Module names: snake_case\r\n-mod user_service;\r\n-mod api_client;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Documentation\r\n-\r\n-#### Rustdoc Comments\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Service for managing user accounts\r\n-/// \r\n-/// Provides CRUD operations for users with proper validation\r\n-/// and error handling. All operations are async and thread-safe.\r\n-/// \r\n-/// # Examples\r\n-/// \r\n-/// ```rust\r\n-/// let service = UserService::new(db_pool);\r\n-/// let user = service.get_user(123).await?;\r\n-/// println!(\"User: {}\", user.name);\r\n-/// ```\r\n-pub struct UserService {\r\n-    /// Database connection pool\r\n-    pool: Arc<DbPool>,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-impl UserService {\r\n-    /// Create a new user with the given details\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Arguments\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `request` - User creation data including name and email\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Returns\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// Returns the created user with assigned ID, or an error if\r\n-    /// validation fails or the email already exists.\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Errors\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `ValidationError` - Invalid input data\r\n-    /// * `ConflictError` - Email already registered\r\n-    /// * `DatabaseError` - Database operation failed\r\n-    pub async fn create_user(&self, request: CreateUserRequest) -> Result<User, UserError> {\r\n-        // Implementation\r\n-    }\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-#### Error Documentation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Errors that can occur during user operations\r\n-#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\r\n-pub enum UserError {\r\n-    /// User input validation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\r\n-    Validation { message: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// User with given email already exists\r\n-    #[error(\"User with email {email} already exists\")]\r\n-    Conflict { email: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// Database operation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Database error: {0}\")]\r\n-    Database(#[from] sqlx::Error),\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Error Handling\r\n-\r\n-Use `anyhow` for application errors and `thiserror` for library errors:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use anyhow::{Context, Result};\r\n-\r\n-pub async fn process_user(id: u64) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    let user = database::get_user(id)\r\n-        .await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user from database\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    validate_user(&user)\r\n-        .context(\"User validation failed\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Performance Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Avoid blocking operations** in async context:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: blocking in async\r\n-   async fn bad_handler() {\r\n-       let data = std::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").unwrap();\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: use async I/O\r\n-   async fn good_handler() {\r\n-       let data = tokio::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").await?;\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Use efficient data structures**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: unnecessary allocations\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<String> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.clone()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: avoid clones when possible\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<&str> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.as_str()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-3. **Use appropriate synchronization**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Short-lived locks\r\n-   use parking_lot::{RwLock, Mutex};\r\n-   \r\n-   // Long-running async operations\r\n-   use tokio::sync::{RwLock as AsyncRwLock, Mutex as AsyncMutex};\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-## Debugging\r\n-\r\n-### Logging\r\n-\r\n-Use structured logging with `tracing`:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use tracing::{info, warn, error, debug, trace};\r\n-\r\n-#[tracing::instrument(skip(db))]\r\n-async fn process_user(user_id: u64, db: &Database) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    debug!(user_id, \"Starting user processing\");\r\n-    \r\n-    let user = db.get_user(user_id).await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    info!(user_id, user_name = %user.name, \"User retrieved successfully\");\r\n-    \r\n-    if user.is_inactive() {\r\n-        warn!(user_id, \"Processing inactive user\");\r\n-    }\r\n-    \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Environment Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Enable debug logging\r\n-export RUST_LOG=debug\r\n-\r\n-# Enable backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=1\r\n-\r\n-# For detailed backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=full\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Testing Tools\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run specific test\r\n-cargo test test_user_creation\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests with output\r\n-cargo test -- --nocapture\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests in single thread\r\n-cargo test -- --test-threads=1\r\n-\r\n-# Run ignored tests\r\n-cargo test -- --ignored\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Pull Request Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### PR Description Template\r\n-\r\n-```markdown\r\n-## Description\r\n-Brief description of the changes made.\r\n-\r\n-## Type of Change\r\n-- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n-- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n-- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\r\n-- [ ] Documentation update\r\n-\r\n-## Testing\r\n-- [ ] Unit tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Integration tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Manual testing completed\r\n-- [ ] New tests added for new functionality\r\n-\r\n-## Documentation\r\n-- [ ] Code is documented with rustdoc comments\r\n-- [ ] README updated (if applicable)\r\n-- [ ] API documentation updated (if applicable)\r\n-\r\n-## Checklist\r\n-- [ ] Code follows project style guidelines\r\n-- [ ] Self-review completed\r\n-- [ ] No linting errors (`cargo clippy`)\r\n-- [ ] Code is properly formatted (`cargo fmt`)\r\n-- [ ] Tests pass (`cargo test`)\r\n-\r\n-## Related Issues\r\n-Closes #issue_number\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Review Process\r\n-\r\n-1. **Automated checks** must pass (CI/CD pipeline)\r\n-2. **At least one approval** from maintainer required\r\n-3. **All conversations resolved** before merge\r\n-4. **Up-to-date with main** branch\r\n-\r\n-### Merge Strategy\r\n-\r\n-- **Squash and merge** for feature branches\r\n-- **Rebase and merge** for simple fixes\r\n-- **Merge commit** for release branches\r\n-\r\n-## Security Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Input Validation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use validator::{Validate, ValidationError};\r\n-\r\n-#[derive(Deserialize, Validate)]\r\n-pub struct CreateUserRequest {\r\n-    #[validate(length(min = 1, max = 100))]\r\n-    pub name: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(email)]\r\n-    pub email: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(custom = \"validate_password\")]\r\n-    pub password: String,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-fn validate_password(password: &str) -> Result<(), ValidationError> {\r\n-    if password.len() < 8 {\r\n-        return Err(ValidationError::new(\"Password too short\"));\r\n-    }\r\n-    Ok(())\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Secrets Management\r\n-\r\n-- **Never commit secrets** to version control\r\n-- **Use environment variables** for configuration\r\n-- **Rotate secrets regularly**\r\n-- **Use secure random generation** for tokens\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Bad: hardcoded secret\r\n-const API_KEY: &str = \"sk-1234567890abcdef\";\r\n-\r\n-// Good: environment variable\r\n-let api_key = std::env::var(\"API_KEY\")\r\n-    .context(\"API_KEY environment variable not set\")?;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Getting Help\r\n-\r\n-- **GitHub Issues**: For bug reports and feature requests\r\n-- **GitHub Discussions**: For questions and general discussion\r\n-- **Documentation**: Check existing docs first\r\n-- **Code Examples**: Look at existing modules for patterns\r\n-\r\n-## Contribution Areas\r\n-\r\n-We welcome contributions in:\r\n-\r\n-- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\r\n-- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\r\n-- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\r\n-- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\r\n-- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\r\n-- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for contributing to HyperSpot Server!\r\n+# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\n+\n+Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\n+\n+We welcome contributions in:\n+\n+- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\n+- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\n+- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\n+- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\n+- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\n+- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\n+\n+\n+## 1. Quick Start\n+\n+### 1.1 Prerequisites\n+\n+- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\n+- **Git** for version control\n+- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\n+\n+### 1.2 Development Setup\n+\n+```bash\n+# Clone the repository\n+git clone <repository-url>\n+cd hyperspot\n+\n+# Install Rust (if not already installed)\n+curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\n+\n+# Install required components\n+rustup component add clippy rustfmt\n+\n+# Build the project\n+cargo build\n+\n+# Run tests\n+cargo test\n+\n+# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\n+cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run\n+```\n+\n+## 2. Development Workflow\n+\n+### 2.1. Create a Feature Branch or Fork\n+\n+```bash\n+git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\n+```\n+\n+Use descriptive branch names:\n+- `feature/user-authentication`\n+- `fix/memory-leak-in-router`\n+- `docs/api-gateway-examples`\n+- `refactor/entity-to-contract-conversions`\n+\n+As an alternative, you can fork the repository to your own GitHub account.\n+\n+\n+### 2.2. Make Your Changes\n+\n+Follow the coding standards and guidelines:\n+\n+1. See common [RUST.md](./guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md) guideline\n+2. When develop new REST API use [API.md](./guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md), [PAGINATION](./guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md), [STATUS_CODES](./guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md)\n+3. When develop new Module use [NEW_MODULE.md](./guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md)\n+4. For PlantUML diagrams see [PlantUML.md](./guidelines/DNA/diagrams/PlantUML.md)\n+5. Security [SECURITY.md](./guidelines/SECURITY.md)\n+\n+Always include unit tests when introducing new code.\n+\n+\n+### 2.3. Run Code Quality Checks\n+\n+Key formatting rules:\n+- **Line length**: 100 characters max\n+- **Indentation**: 4 spaces (no tabs)\n+- **Trailing commas**: Required in multi-line expressions\n+\n+Run static analysis checks:\n+\n+```bash\n+# Run the complete quality check suite: formatting, linting, tests, and security\n+make check\n+\n+# (Optional) Run security checks individually\n+make audit\n+make deny\n+```\n+\n+Run the unit tests:\n+\n+```bash\n+# Run tests with output shown\n+cargo test -- --nocapture\n+\n+# Run tests in a single thread\n+cargo test -- --test-threads=1\n+\n+# Run tests marked as ignored\n+cargo test -- --ignored\n+```\n+\n+Aim for high test coverage:\n+- **Unit tests**: Test individual functions and methods\n+- **Integration tests**: Test module interactions\n+- **End-to-end tests**: Test complete request flows\n+\n+```bash\n+# Run tests with coverage (requires tarpaulin)\n+cargo install cargo-tarpaulin","path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","original_commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","user":{"login":"modcrafter77","id":216291417,"node_id":"U_kgDODORYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216291417?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77","html_url":"https://github.com/modcrafter77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Did we check it? ","created_at":"2025-11-01T21:05:24Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T23:10:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483915446","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483915446"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483915446"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483915446/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":114,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":677,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483916692","pull_request_review_id":3407722500,"id":2483916692,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6UDY-U","diff_hunk":"","path":"guidelines/SECURITY.md","commit_id":"0d71046f6fb9cb219931678fdf8dbe13f050c631","original_commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","user":{"login":"modcrafter77","id":216291417,"node_id":"U_kgDODORYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216291417?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77","html_url":"https://github.com/modcrafter77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Do we want to add some comments about secure orm here? Or merge secure-orm.md file into this file","created_at":"2025-11-01T21:07:14Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T21:08:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483916692","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483916692"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483916692"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483916692/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483917593","pull_request_review_id":3407722500,"id":2483917593,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6UDZMZ","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,4 +1,7 @@\n # GUIDELINES\n \n-1. When develop new REST API use [API_GUIDELINE.md](./API_GUIDELINE.md)\n-2. When develop new Module use [NEW_MODULE.md](./NEW_MODULE.md)\n+1. See common [RUST.md](./DNA/languages/RUST.md) guideline\n+2. When develop new REST API use [API.md](./DNA/REST/API.md), [PAGINATION](./DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md), [STATUS_CODES](./DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md)\n+3. When develop new Module use [NEW_MODULE.md](./NEW_MODULE.md)\n+4. For PlantUML diagrams see [PlantUML.md](./DNA/diagrams/PlantUML.md)","path":"guidelines/README.md","commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","original_commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","user":{"login":"modcrafter77","id":216291417,"node_id":"U_kgDODORYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216291417?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77","html_url":"https://github.com/modcrafter77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I suggest to use Mermaid instead of PlantUML. It's modern and github renders it w/o any issues.","created_at":"2025-11-01T21:08:02Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T21:14:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483917593","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483917593"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483917593"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483917593/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":6,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":8,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483987536","pull_request_review_id":3407818052,"id":2483987536,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6UDqRQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,563 +1,279 @@\n-# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\r\n-\r\n-## Quick Start\r\n-\r\n-### Prerequisites\r\n-\r\n-- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\r\n-- **Git** for version control\r\n-- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\r\n-\r\n-### Development Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Clone the repository\r\n-git clone <repository-url>\r\n-cd hyperspot\r\n-\r\n-# Install Rust (if not already installed)\r\n-curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\r\n-\r\n-# Install required components\r\n-rustup component add clippy rustfmt\r\n-\r\n-# Build the project\r\n-cargo build\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-cargo test\r\n-\r\n-# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\r\n-cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Workspace Layout\r\n-\r\n-```\r\n-hyperspot/\r\n-├── apps/\r\n-│   └── hyperspot-server/     # Main server binary\r\n-├── modules/\r\n-│   └── api_ingress/          # HTTP gateway and OpenAPI provider\r\n-\r\n-├── libs/\r\n-│   ├── modkit/               # Core framework and traits\r\n-│   ├── db/                   # Database abstraction layer\r\n-│   └── runtime/              # Runtime utilities and config\r\n-├── config/                   # Configuration files\r\n-└── docs/                     # Documentation\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Development Workflow\r\n-\r\n-### 1. Create a Feature Branch\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Use descriptive branch names:\r\n-- `feature/user-authentication`\r\n-- `fix/memory-leak-in-router`\r\n-- `docs/api-gateway-examples`\r\n-- `refactor/entity-to-contract-conversions`\r\n-\r\n-### 2. Make Your Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow the coding standards and patterns described below.\r\n-\r\n-### 3. Run Quality Checks\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Format code (check only)\r\n-make fmt\r\n-\r\n-# Lint (deny warnings)\r\n-make clippy\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-make test\r\n-\r\n-# Full check (fmt + clippy + test + security)\r\n-make check\r\n-\r\n-# Security checks\r\n-make audit\r\n-make deny\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### 4. Commit Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow a structured commit message format:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-<type>(<module>): <description>\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-- `<type>`: change category (see table below)\r\n-- `<module>` (optional): the area touched (e.g., api_ingress, modkit, ecommerce)\r\n-- `<description>`: concise, imperative summary\r\n-\r\n-Accepted commit types:\r\n-\r\n-| Type       | Meaning                                                     |\r\n-|------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|\r\n-| feat       | A new feature                                               |\r\n-| fix        | A bug fix                                                   |\r\n-| tech       | A technical improvement                                     |\r\n-| cleanup    | Code cleanup                                                |\r\n-| refactor   | Code restructuring without functional changes               |\r\n-| test       | Adding or modifying tests                                   |\r\n-| docs       | Documentation updates                                       |\r\n-| style      | Code style changes (whitespace, formatting, etc.)           |\r\n-| chore      | Misc tasks (deps, tooling, scripts)                         |\r\n-| perf       | Performance improvements                                    |\r\n-| ci         | CI/CD configuration changes                                 |\r\n-| build      | Build system or dependency changes                          |\r\n-| revert     | Reverting a previous commit                                 |\r\n-| security   | Security fixes                                              |\r\n-| breaking   | Backward incompatible changes                               |\r\n-\r\n-Examples:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-feat(auth): add OAuth2 support for login\r\n-fix(ui): resolve button alignment issue on mobile\r\n-tech(database): add error abstraction for database and API errors\r\n-refactor(database): optimize query execution\r\n-test(api): add unit tests for user authentication\r\n-docs(readme): update installation instructions\r\n-style(css): apply consistent spacing in stylesheet\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Best practices:\r\n-\r\n-- Keep the title concise (ideally ≤ 50 chars)\r\n-- Use imperative mood (e.g., \"Fix bug\", not \"Fixed bug\")\r\n-- Make commits atomic (one logical change per commit)\r\n-- Add details in the body when necessary (what/why, not how)\r\n-- For breaking changes, either use `feat!:`/`fix!:` or include a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer\r\n-\r\n-New functionality development:\r\n-\r\n-- Follow the repository structure in `README.md`\r\n-- Prefer soft-deletion for entities; provide hard-deletion with retention routines\r\n-- Include unit tests (and integration tests when relevant)\r\n-\r\n-### 5. Push and Create PR\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git push origin feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Then create a Pull Request on GitHub with:\r\n-- Clear title and description\r\n-- Reference to related issues\r\n-- Test coverage information\r\n-- Breaking changes (if any)\r\n-\r\n-## Architecture Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Module Development\r\n-\r\n-#### Creating a New Module\r\n-\r\n-1. **Create module directory**:\r\n-   ```bash\r\n-   mkdir modules/my_module\r\n-   cd modules/my_module\r\n-   cargo init --lib\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Define module structure**:\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### API Design Standards\r\n-\r\n-#### REST Endpoint Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Use consistent resource naming**:\r\n-   - `/users` (plural nouns)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}` (path parameters)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}/posts` (nested resources)\r\n-\r\n-2. **HTTP methods**:\r\n-   - `GET` for reading data\r\n-   - `POST` for creating resources\r\n-   - `PUT` for updating entire resources\r\n-   - `PATCH` for partial updates\r\n-   - `DELETE` for removing resources\r\n-\r\n-3. **Status codes**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Success responses\r\n-   200 OK              // Successful GET, PUT, PATCH\r\n-   201 Created         // Successful POST\r\n-   204 No Content      // Successful DELETE\r\n-   \r\n-   // Client error responses\r\n-   400 Bad Request     // Invalid request data\r\n-   401 Unauthorized    // Authentication required\r\n-   403 Forbidden       // Insufficient permissions\r\n-   404 Not Found       // Resource doesn't exist\r\n-   409 Conflict        // Resource conflict\r\n-   422 Unprocessable   // Validation errors\r\n-   \r\n-   // Server error responses\r\n-   500 Internal Error  // Unexpected server error\r\n-   501 Not Implemented // Handler not implemented\r\n-   503 Service Unavail // Service temporarily down\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-#### Schema Design\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-## Testing Standards\r\n-\r\n-### Unit Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD \r\n-\r\n-### Integration Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### Test Coverage\r\n-\r\n-Aim for high test coverage:\r\n-- **Unit tests**: Test individual functions and methods\r\n-- **Integration tests**: Test module interactions\r\n-- **End-to-end tests**: Test complete request flows\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run tests with coverage (requires tarpaulin)\r\n-cargo install cargo-tarpaulin\r\n-cargo tarpaulin --out html\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Code Style\r\n-\r\n-### Formatting\r\n-\r\n-Use `rustfmt` with the project configuration:\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-cargo fmt -all\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Key formatting rules:\r\n-- **Line length**: 100 characters max\r\n-- **Indentation**: 4 spaces (no tabs)\r\n-- **Trailing commas**: Required in multi-line expressions\r\n-\r\n-### Naming Conventions\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Types: PascalCase\r\n-struct UserService;\r\n-enum ResponseStatus;\r\n-\r\n-// Functions and variables: snake_case\r\n-fn create_user() {}\r\n-let user_name = \"Alice\";\r\n-\r\n-// Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\r\n-const MAX_RETRIES: u32 = 3;\r\n-const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(30);\r\n-\r\n-// Module names: snake_case\r\n-mod user_service;\r\n-mod api_client;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Documentation\r\n-\r\n-#### Rustdoc Comments\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Service for managing user accounts\r\n-/// \r\n-/// Provides CRUD operations for users with proper validation\r\n-/// and error handling. All operations are async and thread-safe.\r\n-/// \r\n-/// # Examples\r\n-/// \r\n-/// ```rust\r\n-/// let service = UserService::new(db_pool);\r\n-/// let user = service.get_user(123).await?;\r\n-/// println!(\"User: {}\", user.name);\r\n-/// ```\r\n-pub struct UserService {\r\n-    /// Database connection pool\r\n-    pool: Arc<DbPool>,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-impl UserService {\r\n-    /// Create a new user with the given details\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Arguments\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `request` - User creation data including name and email\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Returns\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// Returns the created user with assigned ID, or an error if\r\n-    /// validation fails or the email already exists.\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Errors\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `ValidationError` - Invalid input data\r\n-    /// * `ConflictError` - Email already registered\r\n-    /// * `DatabaseError` - Database operation failed\r\n-    pub async fn create_user(&self, request: CreateUserRequest) -> Result<User, UserError> {\r\n-        // Implementation\r\n-    }\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-#### Error Documentation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Errors that can occur during user operations\r\n-#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\r\n-pub enum UserError {\r\n-    /// User input validation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\r\n-    Validation { message: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// User with given email already exists\r\n-    #[error(\"User with email {email} already exists\")]\r\n-    Conflict { email: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// Database operation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Database error: {0}\")]\r\n-    Database(#[from] sqlx::Error),\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Error Handling\r\n-\r\n-Use `anyhow` for application errors and `thiserror` for library errors:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use anyhow::{Context, Result};\r\n-\r\n-pub async fn process_user(id: u64) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    let user = database::get_user(id)\r\n-        .await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user from database\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    validate_user(&user)\r\n-        .context(\"User validation failed\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Performance Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Avoid blocking operations** in async context:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: blocking in async\r\n-   async fn bad_handler() {\r\n-       let data = std::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").unwrap();\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: use async I/O\r\n-   async fn good_handler() {\r\n-       let data = tokio::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").await?;\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Use efficient data structures**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: unnecessary allocations\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<String> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.clone()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: avoid clones when possible\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<&str> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.as_str()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-3. **Use appropriate synchronization**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Short-lived locks\r\n-   use parking_lot::{RwLock, Mutex};\r\n-   \r\n-   // Long-running async operations\r\n-   use tokio::sync::{RwLock as AsyncRwLock, Mutex as AsyncMutex};\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-## Debugging\r\n-\r\n-### Logging\r\n-\r\n-Use structured logging with `tracing`:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use tracing::{info, warn, error, debug, trace};\r\n-\r\n-#[tracing::instrument(skip(db))]\r\n-async fn process_user(user_id: u64, db: &Database) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    debug!(user_id, \"Starting user processing\");\r\n-    \r\n-    let user = db.get_user(user_id).await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    info!(user_id, user_name = %user.name, \"User retrieved successfully\");\r\n-    \r\n-    if user.is_inactive() {\r\n-        warn!(user_id, \"Processing inactive user\");\r\n-    }\r\n-    \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Environment Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Enable debug logging\r\n-export RUST_LOG=debug\r\n-\r\n-# Enable backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=1\r\n-\r\n-# For detailed backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=full\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Testing Tools\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run specific test\r\n-cargo test test_user_creation\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests with output\r\n-cargo test -- --nocapture\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests in single thread\r\n-cargo test -- --test-threads=1\r\n-\r\n-# Run ignored tests\r\n-cargo test -- --ignored\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Pull Request Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### PR Description Template\r\n-\r\n-```markdown\r\n-## Description\r\n-Brief description of the changes made.\r\n-\r\n-## Type of Change\r\n-- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n-- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n-- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\r\n-- [ ] Documentation update\r\n-\r\n-## Testing\r\n-- [ ] Unit tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Integration tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Manual testing completed\r\n-- [ ] New tests added for new functionality\r\n-\r\n-## Documentation\r\n-- [ ] Code is documented with rustdoc comments\r\n-- [ ] README updated (if applicable)\r\n-- [ ] API documentation updated (if applicable)\r\n-\r\n-## Checklist\r\n-- [ ] Code follows project style guidelines\r\n-- [ ] Self-review completed\r\n-- [ ] No linting errors (`cargo clippy`)\r\n-- [ ] Code is properly formatted (`cargo fmt`)\r\n-- [ ] Tests pass (`cargo test`)\r\n-\r\n-## Related Issues\r\n-Closes #issue_number\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Review Process\r\n-\r\n-1. **Automated checks** must pass (CI/CD pipeline)\r\n-2. **At least one approval** from maintainer required\r\n-3. **All conversations resolved** before merge\r\n-4. **Up-to-date with main** branch\r\n-\r\n-### Merge Strategy\r\n-\r\n-- **Squash and merge** for feature branches\r\n-- **Rebase and merge** for simple fixes\r\n-- **Merge commit** for release branches\r\n-\r\n-## Security Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Input Validation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use validator::{Validate, ValidationError};\r\n-\r\n-#[derive(Deserialize, Validate)]\r\n-pub struct CreateUserRequest {\r\n-    #[validate(length(min = 1, max = 100))]\r\n-    pub name: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(email)]\r\n-    pub email: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(custom = \"validate_password\")]\r\n-    pub password: String,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-fn validate_password(password: &str) -> Result<(), ValidationError> {\r\n-    if password.len() < 8 {\r\n-        return Err(ValidationError::new(\"Password too short\"));\r\n-    }\r\n-    Ok(())\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Secrets Management\r\n-\r\n-- **Never commit secrets** to version control\r\n-- **Use environment variables** for configuration\r\n-- **Rotate secrets regularly**\r\n-- **Use secure random generation** for tokens\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Bad: hardcoded secret\r\n-const API_KEY: &str = \"sk-1234567890abcdef\";\r\n-\r\n-// Good: environment variable\r\n-let api_key = std::env::var(\"API_KEY\")\r\n-    .context(\"API_KEY environment variable not set\")?;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Getting Help\r\n-\r\n-- **GitHub Issues**: For bug reports and feature requests\r\n-- **GitHub Discussions**: For questions and general discussion\r\n-- **Documentation**: Check existing docs first\r\n-- **Code Examples**: Look at existing modules for patterns\r\n-\r\n-## Contribution Areas\r\n-\r\n-We welcome contributions in:\r\n-\r\n-- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\r\n-- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\r\n-- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\r\n-- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\r\n-- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\r\n-- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for contributing to HyperSpot Server!\r\n+# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\n+\n+Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\n+\n+We welcome contributions in:\n+\n+- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\n+- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\n+- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\n+- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\n+- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\n+- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\n+\n+\n+## 1. Quick Start\n+\n+### 1.1 Prerequisites\n+\n+- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\n+- **Git** for version control\n+- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\n+\n+### 1.2 Development Setup\n+\n+```bash\n+# Clone the repository\n+git clone <repository-url>\n+cd hyperspot\n+\n+# Install Rust (if not already installed)\n+curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\n+\n+# Install required components\n+rustup component add clippy rustfmt\n+\n+# Build the project\n+cargo build\n+\n+# Run tests\n+cargo test\n+\n+# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\n+cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run\n+```\n+\n+## 2. Development Workflow\n+\n+### 2.1. Create a Feature Branch or Fork\n+\n+```bash\n+git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\n+```\n+\n+Use descriptive branch names:\n+- `feature/user-authentication`\n+- `fix/memory-leak-in-router`\n+- `docs/api-gateway-examples`\n+- `refactor/entity-to-contract-conversions`\n+\n+As an alternative, you can fork the repository to your own GitHub account.\n+\n+\n+### 2.2. Make Your Changes\n+\n+Follow the coding standards and guidelines:\n+\n+1. See common [RUST.md](./guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md) guideline\n+2. When develop new REST API use [API.md](./guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md), [PAGINATION](./guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md), [STATUS_CODES](./guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md)\n+3. When develop new Module use [NEW_MODULE.md](./guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md)\n+4. For PlantUML diagrams see [PlantUML.md](./guidelines/DNA/diagrams/PlantUML.md)\n+5. Security [SECURITY.md](./guidelines/SECURITY.md)\n+\n+Always include unit tests when introducing new code.\n+\n+\n+### 2.3. Run Code Quality Checks\n+\n+Key formatting rules:","path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","commit_id":"0d71046f6fb9cb219931678fdf8dbe13f050c631","original_commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Yes, we have a note in 4 lines below, that in order to test all the changes one need to run\r\n```\r\nmake check\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe `check` is an alias for `fmt` `clippy` `test` `security`, that includes fmt --all","created_at":"2025-11-01T23:01:28Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T23:01:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483987536","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483987536"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483987536"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483987536/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":80,"original_line":78,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2483915277,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":641,"position":643,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483988078","pull_request_review_id":3407818664,"id":2483988078,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6UDqZu","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,4 +1,7 @@\n # GUIDELINES\n \n-1. When develop new REST API use [API_GUIDELINE.md](./API_GUIDELINE.md)\n-2. When develop new Module use [NEW_MODULE.md](./NEW_MODULE.md)\n+1. See common [RUST.md](./DNA/languages/RUST.md) guideline\n+2. When develop new REST API use [API.md](./DNA/REST/API.md), [PAGINATION](./DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md), [STATUS_CODES](./DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md)\n+3. When develop new Module use [NEW_MODULE.md](./NEW_MODULE.md)\n+4. For PlantUML diagrams see [PlantUML.md](./DNA/diagrams/PlantUML.md)","path":"guidelines/README.md","commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","original_commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Noted, removed reference to PlantUML for now","created_at":"2025-11-01T23:04:01Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T23:04:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483988078","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483988078"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2483988078"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2483988078/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":6,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2483917593,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":8,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2484009603","pull_request_review_id":3407840295,"id":2484009603,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6UDvqD","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,563 +1,279 @@\n-# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\r\n-\r\n-## Quick Start\r\n-\r\n-### Prerequisites\r\n-\r\n-- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\r\n-- **Git** for version control\r\n-- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\r\n-\r\n-### Development Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Clone the repository\r\n-git clone <repository-url>\r\n-cd hyperspot\r\n-\r\n-# Install Rust (if not already installed)\r\n-curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\r\n-\r\n-# Install required components\r\n-rustup component add clippy rustfmt\r\n-\r\n-# Build the project\r\n-cargo build\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-cargo test\r\n-\r\n-# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\r\n-cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Workspace Layout\r\n-\r\n-```\r\n-hyperspot/\r\n-├── apps/\r\n-│   └── hyperspot-server/     # Main server binary\r\n-├── modules/\r\n-│   └── api_ingress/          # HTTP gateway and OpenAPI provider\r\n-\r\n-├── libs/\r\n-│   ├── modkit/               # Core framework and traits\r\n-│   ├── db/                   # Database abstraction layer\r\n-│   └── runtime/              # Runtime utilities and config\r\n-├── config/                   # Configuration files\r\n-└── docs/                     # Documentation\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Development Workflow\r\n-\r\n-### 1. Create a Feature Branch\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Use descriptive branch names:\r\n-- `feature/user-authentication`\r\n-- `fix/memory-leak-in-router`\r\n-- `docs/api-gateway-examples`\r\n-- `refactor/entity-to-contract-conversions`\r\n-\r\n-### 2. Make Your Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow the coding standards and patterns described below.\r\n-\r\n-### 3. Run Quality Checks\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Format code (check only)\r\n-make fmt\r\n-\r\n-# Lint (deny warnings)\r\n-make clippy\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-make test\r\n-\r\n-# Full check (fmt + clippy + test + security)\r\n-make check\r\n-\r\n-# Security checks\r\n-make audit\r\n-make deny\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### 4. Commit Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow a structured commit message format:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-<type>(<module>): <description>\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-- `<type>`: change category (see table below)\r\n-- `<module>` (optional): the area touched (e.g., api_ingress, modkit, ecommerce)\r\n-- `<description>`: concise, imperative summary\r\n-\r\n-Accepted commit types:\r\n-\r\n-| Type       | Meaning                                                     |\r\n-|------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|\r\n-| feat       | A new feature                                               |\r\n-| fix        | A bug fix                                                   |\r\n-| tech       | A technical improvement                                     |\r\n-| cleanup    | Code cleanup                                                |\r\n-| refactor   | Code restructuring without functional changes               |\r\n-| test       | Adding or modifying tests                                   |\r\n-| docs       | Documentation updates                                       |\r\n-| style      | Code style changes (whitespace, formatting, etc.)           |\r\n-| chore      | Misc tasks (deps, tooling, scripts)                         |\r\n-| perf       | Performance improvements                                    |\r\n-| ci         | CI/CD configuration changes                                 |\r\n-| build      | Build system or dependency changes                          |\r\n-| revert     | Reverting a previous commit                                 |\r\n-| security   | Security fixes                                              |\r\n-| breaking   | Backward incompatible changes                               |\r\n-\r\n-Examples:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-feat(auth): add OAuth2 support for login\r\n-fix(ui): resolve button alignment issue on mobile\r\n-tech(database): add error abstraction for database and API errors\r\n-refactor(database): optimize query execution\r\n-test(api): add unit tests for user authentication\r\n-docs(readme): update installation instructions\r\n-style(css): apply consistent spacing in stylesheet\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Best practices:\r\n-\r\n-- Keep the title concise (ideally ≤ 50 chars)\r\n-- Use imperative mood (e.g., \"Fix bug\", not \"Fixed bug\")\r\n-- Make commits atomic (one logical change per commit)\r\n-- Add details in the body when necessary (what/why, not how)\r\n-- For breaking changes, either use `feat!:`/`fix!:` or include a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer\r\n-\r\n-New functionality development:\r\n-\r\n-- Follow the repository structure in `README.md`\r\n-- Prefer soft-deletion for entities; provide hard-deletion with retention routines\r\n-- Include unit tests (and integration tests when relevant)\r\n-\r\n-### 5. Push and Create PR\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git push origin feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Then create a Pull Request on GitHub with:\r\n-- Clear title and description\r\n-- Reference to related issues\r\n-- Test coverage information\r\n-- Breaking changes (if any)\r\n-\r\n-## Architecture Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Module Development\r\n-\r\n-#### Creating a New Module\r\n-\r\n-1. **Create module directory**:\r\n-   ```bash\r\n-   mkdir modules/my_module\r\n-   cd modules/my_module\r\n-   cargo init --lib\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Define module structure**:\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### API Design Standards\r\n-\r\n-#### REST Endpoint Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Use consistent resource naming**:\r\n-   - `/users` (plural nouns)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}` (path parameters)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}/posts` (nested resources)\r\n-\r\n-2. **HTTP methods**:\r\n-   - `GET` for reading data\r\n-   - `POST` for creating resources\r\n-   - `PUT` for updating entire resources\r\n-   - `PATCH` for partial updates\r\n-   - `DELETE` for removing resources\r\n-\r\n-3. **Status codes**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Success responses\r\n-   200 OK              // Successful GET, PUT, PATCH\r\n-   201 Created         // Successful POST\r\n-   204 No Content      // Successful DELETE\r\n-   \r\n-   // Client error responses\r\n-   400 Bad Request     // Invalid request data\r\n-   401 Unauthorized    // Authentication required\r\n-   403 Forbidden       // Insufficient permissions\r\n-   404 Not Found       // Resource doesn't exist\r\n-   409 Conflict        // Resource conflict\r\n-   422 Unprocessable   // Validation errors\r\n-   \r\n-   // Server error responses\r\n-   500 Internal Error  // Unexpected server error\r\n-   501 Not Implemented // Handler not implemented\r\n-   503 Service Unavail // Service temporarily down\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-#### Schema Design\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-## Testing Standards\r\n-\r\n-### Unit Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD \r\n-\r\n-### Integration Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### Test Coverage\r\n-\r\n-Aim for high test coverage:\r\n-- **Unit tests**: Test individual functions and methods\r\n-- **Integration tests**: Test module interactions\r\n-- **End-to-end tests**: Test complete request flows\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run tests with coverage (requires tarpaulin)\r\n-cargo install cargo-tarpaulin\r\n-cargo tarpaulin --out html\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Code Style\r\n-\r\n-### Formatting\r\n-\r\n-Use `rustfmt` with the project configuration:\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-cargo fmt -all\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Key formatting rules:\r\n-- **Line length**: 100 characters max\r\n-- **Indentation**: 4 spaces (no tabs)\r\n-- **Trailing commas**: Required in multi-line expressions\r\n-\r\n-### Naming Conventions\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Types: PascalCase\r\n-struct UserService;\r\n-enum ResponseStatus;\r\n-\r\n-// Functions and variables: snake_case\r\n-fn create_user() {}\r\n-let user_name = \"Alice\";\r\n-\r\n-// Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\r\n-const MAX_RETRIES: u32 = 3;\r\n-const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(30);\r\n-\r\n-// Module names: snake_case\r\n-mod user_service;\r\n-mod api_client;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Documentation\r\n-\r\n-#### Rustdoc Comments\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Service for managing user accounts\r\n-/// \r\n-/// Provides CRUD operations for users with proper validation\r\n-/// and error handling. All operations are async and thread-safe.\r\n-/// \r\n-/// # Examples\r\n-/// \r\n-/// ```rust\r\n-/// let service = UserService::new(db_pool);\r\n-/// let user = service.get_user(123).await?;\r\n-/// println!(\"User: {}\", user.name);\r\n-/// ```\r\n-pub struct UserService {\r\n-    /// Database connection pool\r\n-    pool: Arc<DbPool>,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-impl UserService {\r\n-    /// Create a new user with the given details\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Arguments\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `request` - User creation data including name and email\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Returns\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// Returns the created user with assigned ID, or an error if\r\n-    /// validation fails or the email already exists.\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Errors\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `ValidationError` - Invalid input data\r\n-    /// * `ConflictError` - Email already registered\r\n-    /// * `DatabaseError` - Database operation failed\r\n-    pub async fn create_user(&self, request: CreateUserRequest) -> Result<User, UserError> {\r\n-        // Implementation\r\n-    }\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-#### Error Documentation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Errors that can occur during user operations\r\n-#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\r\n-pub enum UserError {\r\n-    /// User input validation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\r\n-    Validation { message: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// User with given email already exists\r\n-    #[error(\"User with email {email} already exists\")]\r\n-    Conflict { email: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// Database operation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Database error: {0}\")]\r\n-    Database(#[from] sqlx::Error),\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Error Handling\r\n-\r\n-Use `anyhow` for application errors and `thiserror` for library errors:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use anyhow::{Context, Result};\r\n-\r\n-pub async fn process_user(id: u64) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    let user = database::get_user(id)\r\n-        .await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user from database\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    validate_user(&user)\r\n-        .context(\"User validation failed\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Performance Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Avoid blocking operations** in async context:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: blocking in async\r\n-   async fn bad_handler() {\r\n-       let data = std::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").unwrap();\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: use async I/O\r\n-   async fn good_handler() {\r\n-       let data = tokio::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").await?;\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Use efficient data structures**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: unnecessary allocations\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<String> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.clone()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: avoid clones when possible\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<&str> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.as_str()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-3. **Use appropriate synchronization**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Short-lived locks\r\n-   use parking_lot::{RwLock, Mutex};\r\n-   \r\n-   // Long-running async operations\r\n-   use tokio::sync::{RwLock as AsyncRwLock, Mutex as AsyncMutex};\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-## Debugging\r\n-\r\n-### Logging\r\n-\r\n-Use structured logging with `tracing`:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use tracing::{info, warn, error, debug, trace};\r\n-\r\n-#[tracing::instrument(skip(db))]\r\n-async fn process_user(user_id: u64, db: &Database) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    debug!(user_id, \"Starting user processing\");\r\n-    \r\n-    let user = db.get_user(user_id).await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    info!(user_id, user_name = %user.name, \"User retrieved successfully\");\r\n-    \r\n-    if user.is_inactive() {\r\n-        warn!(user_id, \"Processing inactive user\");\r\n-    }\r\n-    \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Environment Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Enable debug logging\r\n-export RUST_LOG=debug\r\n-\r\n-# Enable backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=1\r\n-\r\n-# For detailed backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=full\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Testing Tools\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run specific test\r\n-cargo test test_user_creation\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests with output\r\n-cargo test -- --nocapture\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests in single thread\r\n-cargo test -- --test-threads=1\r\n-\r\n-# Run ignored tests\r\n-cargo test -- --ignored\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Pull Request Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### PR Description Template\r\n-\r\n-```markdown\r\n-## Description\r\n-Brief description of the changes made.\r\n-\r\n-## Type of Change\r\n-- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n-- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n-- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\r\n-- [ ] Documentation update\r\n-\r\n-## Testing\r\n-- [ ] Unit tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Integration tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Manual testing completed\r\n-- [ ] New tests added for new functionality\r\n-\r\n-## Documentation\r\n-- [ ] Code is documented with rustdoc comments\r\n-- [ ] README updated (if applicable)\r\n-- [ ] API documentation updated (if applicable)\r\n-\r\n-## Checklist\r\n-- [ ] Code follows project style guidelines\r\n-- [ ] Self-review completed\r\n-- [ ] No linting errors (`cargo clippy`)\r\n-- [ ] Code is properly formatted (`cargo fmt`)\r\n-- [ ] Tests pass (`cargo test`)\r\n-\r\n-## Related Issues\r\n-Closes #issue_number\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Review Process\r\n-\r\n-1. **Automated checks** must pass (CI/CD pipeline)\r\n-2. **At least one approval** from maintainer required\r\n-3. **All conversations resolved** before merge\r\n-4. **Up-to-date with main** branch\r\n-\r\n-### Merge Strategy\r\n-\r\n-- **Squash and merge** for feature branches\r\n-- **Rebase and merge** for simple fixes\r\n-- **Merge commit** for release branches\r\n-\r\n-## Security Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Input Validation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use validator::{Validate, ValidationError};\r\n-\r\n-#[derive(Deserialize, Validate)]\r\n-pub struct CreateUserRequest {\r\n-    #[validate(length(min = 1, max = 100))]\r\n-    pub name: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(email)]\r\n-    pub email: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(custom = \"validate_password\")]\r\n-    pub password: String,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-fn validate_password(password: &str) -> Result<(), ValidationError> {\r\n-    if password.len() < 8 {\r\n-        return Err(ValidationError::new(\"Password too short\"));\r\n-    }\r\n-    Ok(())\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Secrets Management\r\n-\r\n-- **Never commit secrets** to version control\r\n-- **Use environment variables** for configuration\r\n-- **Rotate secrets regularly**\r\n-- **Use secure random generation** for tokens\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Bad: hardcoded secret\r\n-const API_KEY: &str = \"sk-1234567890abcdef\";\r\n-\r\n-// Good: environment variable\r\n-let api_key = std::env::var(\"API_KEY\")\r\n-    .context(\"API_KEY environment variable not set\")?;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Getting Help\r\n-\r\n-- **GitHub Issues**: For bug reports and feature requests\r\n-- **GitHub Discussions**: For questions and general discussion\r\n-- **Documentation**: Check existing docs first\r\n-- **Code Examples**: Look at existing modules for patterns\r\n-\r\n-## Contribution Areas\r\n-\r\n-We welcome contributions in:\r\n-\r\n-- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\r\n-- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\r\n-- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\r\n-- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\r\n-- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\r\n-- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for contributing to HyperSpot Server!\r\n+# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\n+\n+Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\n+\n+We welcome contributions in:\n+\n+- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\n+- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\n+- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\n+- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\n+- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\n+- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\n+\n+\n+## 1. Quick Start\n+\n+### 1.1 Prerequisites\n+\n+- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\n+- **Git** for version control\n+- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\n+\n+### 1.2 Development Setup\n+\n+```bash\n+# Clone the repository\n+git clone <repository-url>\n+cd hyperspot\n+\n+# Install Rust (if not already installed)\n+curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\n+\n+# Install required components\n+rustup component add clippy rustfmt\n+\n+# Build the project\n+cargo build\n+\n+# Run tests\n+cargo test\n+\n+# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\n+cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run\n+```\n+\n+## 2. Development Workflow\n+\n+### 2.1. Create a Feature Branch or Fork\n+\n+```bash\n+git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\n+```\n+\n+Use descriptive branch names:\n+- `feature/user-authentication`\n+- `fix/memory-leak-in-router`\n+- `docs/api-gateway-examples`\n+- `refactor/entity-to-contract-conversions`\n+\n+As an alternative, you can fork the repository to your own GitHub account.\n+\n+\n+### 2.2. Make Your Changes\n+\n+Follow the coding standards and guidelines:\n+\n+1. See common [RUST.md](./guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md) guideline\n+2. When develop new REST API use [API.md](./guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md), [PAGINATION](./guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md), [STATUS_CODES](./guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md)\n+3. When develop new Module use [NEW_MODULE.md](./guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md)\n+4. For PlantUML diagrams see [PlantUML.md](./guidelines/DNA/diagrams/PlantUML.md)\n+5. Security [SECURITY.md](./guidelines/SECURITY.md)\n+\n+Always include unit tests when introducing new code.\n+\n+\n+### 2.3. Run Code Quality Checks\n+\n+Key formatting rules:\n+- **Line length**: 100 characters max\n+- **Indentation**: 4 spaces (no tabs)\n+- **Trailing commas**: Required in multi-line expressions\n+\n+Run static analysis checks:\n+\n+```bash\n+# Run the complete quality check suite: formatting, linting, tests, and security\n+make check\n+\n+# (Optional) Run security checks individually\n+make audit\n+make deny\n+```\n+\n+Run the unit tests:\n+\n+```bash\n+# Run tests with output shown\n+cargo test -- --nocapture\n+\n+# Run tests in a single thread\n+cargo test -- --test-threads=1\n+\n+# Run tests marked as ignored\n+cargo test -- --ignored\n+```\n+\n+Aim for high test coverage:\n+- **Unit tests**: Test individual functions and methods\n+- **Integration tests**: Test module interactions\n+- **End-to-end tests**: Test complete request flows\n+\n+```bash\n+# Run tests with coverage (requires tarpaulin)\n+cargo install cargo-tarpaulin","path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","original_commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"You are right, it's Linux only. Lets just mention 'make coverage' here and make this for now:\r\n\r\n```\r\ncoverage:\r\n        @echo \"Code coverage is not implemented yet\"\r\n        @exit -1\r\n```","created_at":"2025-11-01T23:43:26Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T23:43:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2484009603","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2484009603"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2484009603"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2484009603/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":114,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2483915446,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":677,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2484010123","pull_request_review_id":3407841289,"id":2484010123,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6UDvyL","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,563 +1,279 @@\n-# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\r\n-\r\n-## Quick Start\r\n-\r\n-### Prerequisites\r\n-\r\n-- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\r\n-- **Git** for version control\r\n-- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\r\n-\r\n-### Development Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Clone the repository\r\n-git clone <repository-url>\r\n-cd hyperspot\r\n-\r\n-# Install Rust (if not already installed)\r\n-curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\r\n-\r\n-# Install required components\r\n-rustup component add clippy rustfmt\r\n-\r\n-# Build the project\r\n-cargo build\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-cargo test\r\n-\r\n-# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\r\n-cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Workspace Layout\r\n-\r\n-```\r\n-hyperspot/\r\n-├── apps/\r\n-│   └── hyperspot-server/     # Main server binary\r\n-├── modules/\r\n-│   └── api_ingress/          # HTTP gateway and OpenAPI provider\r\n-\r\n-├── libs/\r\n-│   ├── modkit/               # Core framework and traits\r\n-│   ├── db/                   # Database abstraction layer\r\n-│   └── runtime/              # Runtime utilities and config\r\n-├── config/                   # Configuration files\r\n-└── docs/                     # Documentation\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Development Workflow\r\n-\r\n-### 1. Create a Feature Branch\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Use descriptive branch names:\r\n-- `feature/user-authentication`\r\n-- `fix/memory-leak-in-router`\r\n-- `docs/api-gateway-examples`\r\n-- `refactor/entity-to-contract-conversions`\r\n-\r\n-### 2. Make Your Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow the coding standards and patterns described below.\r\n-\r\n-### 3. Run Quality Checks\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Format code (check only)\r\n-make fmt\r\n-\r\n-# Lint (deny warnings)\r\n-make clippy\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests\r\n-make test\r\n-\r\n-# Full check (fmt + clippy + test + security)\r\n-make check\r\n-\r\n-# Security checks\r\n-make audit\r\n-make deny\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### 4. Commit Changes\r\n-\r\n-Follow a structured commit message format:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-<type>(<module>): <description>\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-- `<type>`: change category (see table below)\r\n-- `<module>` (optional): the area touched (e.g., api_ingress, modkit, ecommerce)\r\n-- `<description>`: concise, imperative summary\r\n-\r\n-Accepted commit types:\r\n-\r\n-| Type       | Meaning                                                     |\r\n-|------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|\r\n-| feat       | A new feature                                               |\r\n-| fix        | A bug fix                                                   |\r\n-| tech       | A technical improvement                                     |\r\n-| cleanup    | Code cleanup                                                |\r\n-| refactor   | Code restructuring without functional changes               |\r\n-| test       | Adding or modifying tests                                   |\r\n-| docs       | Documentation updates                                       |\r\n-| style      | Code style changes (whitespace, formatting, etc.)           |\r\n-| chore      | Misc tasks (deps, tooling, scripts)                         |\r\n-| perf       | Performance improvements                                    |\r\n-| ci         | CI/CD configuration changes                                 |\r\n-| build      | Build system or dependency changes                          |\r\n-| revert     | Reverting a previous commit                                 |\r\n-| security   | Security fixes                                              |\r\n-| breaking   | Backward incompatible changes                               |\r\n-\r\n-Examples:\r\n-\r\n-```text\r\n-feat(auth): add OAuth2 support for login\r\n-fix(ui): resolve button alignment issue on mobile\r\n-tech(database): add error abstraction for database and API errors\r\n-refactor(database): optimize query execution\r\n-test(api): add unit tests for user authentication\r\n-docs(readme): update installation instructions\r\n-style(css): apply consistent spacing in stylesheet\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Best practices:\r\n-\r\n-- Keep the title concise (ideally ≤ 50 chars)\r\n-- Use imperative mood (e.g., \"Fix bug\", not \"Fixed bug\")\r\n-- Make commits atomic (one logical change per commit)\r\n-- Add details in the body when necessary (what/why, not how)\r\n-- For breaking changes, either use `feat!:`/`fix!:` or include a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer\r\n-\r\n-New functionality development:\r\n-\r\n-- Follow the repository structure in `README.md`\r\n-- Prefer soft-deletion for entities; provide hard-deletion with retention routines\r\n-- Include unit tests (and integration tests when relevant)\r\n-\r\n-### 5. Push and Create PR\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-git push origin feature/your-feature-name\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Then create a Pull Request on GitHub with:\r\n-- Clear title and description\r\n-- Reference to related issues\r\n-- Test coverage information\r\n-- Breaking changes (if any)\r\n-\r\n-## Architecture Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Module Development\r\n-\r\n-#### Creating a New Module\r\n-\r\n-1. **Create module directory**:\r\n-   ```bash\r\n-   mkdir modules/my_module\r\n-   cd modules/my_module\r\n-   cargo init --lib\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Define module structure**:\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### API Design Standards\r\n-\r\n-#### REST Endpoint Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Use consistent resource naming**:\r\n-   - `/users` (plural nouns)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}` (path parameters)\r\n-   - `/users/{id}/posts` (nested resources)\r\n-\r\n-2. **HTTP methods**:\r\n-   - `GET` for reading data\r\n-   - `POST` for creating resources\r\n-   - `PUT` for updating entire resources\r\n-   - `PATCH` for partial updates\r\n-   - `DELETE` for removing resources\r\n-\r\n-3. **Status codes**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Success responses\r\n-   200 OK              // Successful GET, PUT, PATCH\r\n-   201 Created         // Successful POST\r\n-   204 No Content      // Successful DELETE\r\n-   \r\n-   // Client error responses\r\n-   400 Bad Request     // Invalid request data\r\n-   401 Unauthorized    // Authentication required\r\n-   403 Forbidden       // Insufficient permissions\r\n-   404 Not Found       // Resource doesn't exist\r\n-   409 Conflict        // Resource conflict\r\n-   422 Unprocessable   // Validation errors\r\n-   \r\n-   // Server error responses\r\n-   500 Internal Error  // Unexpected server error\r\n-   501 Not Implemented // Handler not implemented\r\n-   503 Service Unavail // Service temporarily down\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-#### Schema Design\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-## Testing Standards\r\n-\r\n-### Unit Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD \r\n-\r\n-### Integration Tests\r\n-\r\n-TBD\r\n-\r\n-### Test Coverage\r\n-\r\n-Aim for high test coverage:\r\n-- **Unit tests**: Test individual functions and methods\r\n-- **Integration tests**: Test module interactions\r\n-- **End-to-end tests**: Test complete request flows\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run tests with coverage (requires tarpaulin)\r\n-cargo install cargo-tarpaulin\r\n-cargo tarpaulin --out html\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Code Style\r\n-\r\n-### Formatting\r\n-\r\n-Use `rustfmt` with the project configuration:\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-cargo fmt -all\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Key formatting rules:\r\n-- **Line length**: 100 characters max\r\n-- **Indentation**: 4 spaces (no tabs)\r\n-- **Trailing commas**: Required in multi-line expressions\r\n-\r\n-### Naming Conventions\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Types: PascalCase\r\n-struct UserService;\r\n-enum ResponseStatus;\r\n-\r\n-// Functions and variables: snake_case\r\n-fn create_user() {}\r\n-let user_name = \"Alice\";\r\n-\r\n-// Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\r\n-const MAX_RETRIES: u32 = 3;\r\n-const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(30);\r\n-\r\n-// Module names: snake_case\r\n-mod user_service;\r\n-mod api_client;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Documentation\r\n-\r\n-#### Rustdoc Comments\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Service for managing user accounts\r\n-/// \r\n-/// Provides CRUD operations for users with proper validation\r\n-/// and error handling. All operations are async and thread-safe.\r\n-/// \r\n-/// # Examples\r\n-/// \r\n-/// ```rust\r\n-/// let service = UserService::new(db_pool);\r\n-/// let user = service.get_user(123).await?;\r\n-/// println!(\"User: {}\", user.name);\r\n-/// ```\r\n-pub struct UserService {\r\n-    /// Database connection pool\r\n-    pool: Arc<DbPool>,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-impl UserService {\r\n-    /// Create a new user with the given details\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Arguments\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `request` - User creation data including name and email\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Returns\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// Returns the created user with assigned ID, or an error if\r\n-    /// validation fails or the email already exists.\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// # Errors\r\n-    /// \r\n-    /// * `ValidationError` - Invalid input data\r\n-    /// * `ConflictError` - Email already registered\r\n-    /// * `DatabaseError` - Database operation failed\r\n-    pub async fn create_user(&self, request: CreateUserRequest) -> Result<User, UserError> {\r\n-        // Implementation\r\n-    }\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-#### Error Documentation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-/// Errors that can occur during user operations\r\n-#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\r\n-pub enum UserError {\r\n-    /// User input validation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\r\n-    Validation { message: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// User with given email already exists\r\n-    #[error(\"User with email {email} already exists\")]\r\n-    Conflict { email: String },\r\n-    \r\n-    /// Database operation failed\r\n-    #[error(\"Database error: {0}\")]\r\n-    Database(#[from] sqlx::Error),\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Error Handling\r\n-\r\n-Use `anyhow` for application errors and `thiserror` for library errors:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use anyhow::{Context, Result};\r\n-\r\n-pub async fn process_user(id: u64) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    let user = database::get_user(id)\r\n-        .await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user from database\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    validate_user(&user)\r\n-        .context(\"User validation failed\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Performance Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-1. **Avoid blocking operations** in async context:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: blocking in async\r\n-   async fn bad_handler() {\r\n-       let data = std::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").unwrap();\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: use async I/O\r\n-   async fn good_handler() {\r\n-       let data = tokio::fs::read_to_string(\"file.txt\").await?;\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-2. **Use efficient data structures**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Bad: unnecessary allocations\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<String> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.clone()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   \r\n-   // Good: avoid clones when possible\r\n-   fn process_items(items: &[Item]) -> Vec<&str> {\r\n-       items.iter().map(|item| item.name.as_str()).collect()\r\n-   }\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-3. **Use appropriate synchronization**:\r\n-   ```rust\r\n-   // Short-lived locks\r\n-   use parking_lot::{RwLock, Mutex};\r\n-   \r\n-   // Long-running async operations\r\n-   use tokio::sync::{RwLock as AsyncRwLock, Mutex as AsyncMutex};\r\n-   ```\r\n-\r\n-## Debugging\r\n-\r\n-### Logging\r\n-\r\n-Use structured logging with `tracing`:\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use tracing::{info, warn, error, debug, trace};\r\n-\r\n-#[tracing::instrument(skip(db))]\r\n-async fn process_user(user_id: u64, db: &Database) -> Result<User> {\r\n-    debug!(user_id, \"Starting user processing\");\r\n-    \r\n-    let user = db.get_user(user_id).await\r\n-        .context(\"Failed to fetch user\")?;\r\n-        \r\n-    info!(user_id, user_name = %user.name, \"User retrieved successfully\");\r\n-    \r\n-    if user.is_inactive() {\r\n-        warn!(user_id, \"Processing inactive user\");\r\n-    }\r\n-    \r\n-    Ok(user)\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Environment Setup\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Enable debug logging\r\n-export RUST_LOG=debug\r\n-\r\n-# Enable backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=1\r\n-\r\n-# For detailed backtraces\r\n-export RUST_BACKTRACE=full\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Testing Tools\r\n-\r\n-```bash\r\n-# Run specific test\r\n-cargo test test_user_creation\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests with output\r\n-cargo test -- --nocapture\r\n-\r\n-# Run tests in single thread\r\n-cargo test -- --test-threads=1\r\n-\r\n-# Run ignored tests\r\n-cargo test -- --ignored\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Pull Request Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### PR Description Template\r\n-\r\n-```markdown\r\n-## Description\r\n-Brief description of the changes made.\r\n-\r\n-## Type of Change\r\n-- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n-- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n-- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\r\n-- [ ] Documentation update\r\n-\r\n-## Testing\r\n-- [ ] Unit tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Integration tests pass\r\n-- [ ] Manual testing completed\r\n-- [ ] New tests added for new functionality\r\n-\r\n-## Documentation\r\n-- [ ] Code is documented with rustdoc comments\r\n-- [ ] README updated (if applicable)\r\n-- [ ] API documentation updated (if applicable)\r\n-\r\n-## Checklist\r\n-- [ ] Code follows project style guidelines\r\n-- [ ] Self-review completed\r\n-- [ ] No linting errors (`cargo clippy`)\r\n-- [ ] Code is properly formatted (`cargo fmt`)\r\n-- [ ] Tests pass (`cargo test`)\r\n-\r\n-## Related Issues\r\n-Closes #issue_number\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Review Process\r\n-\r\n-1. **Automated checks** must pass (CI/CD pipeline)\r\n-2. **At least one approval** from maintainer required\r\n-3. **All conversations resolved** before merge\r\n-4. **Up-to-date with main** branch\r\n-\r\n-### Merge Strategy\r\n-\r\n-- **Squash and merge** for feature branches\r\n-- **Rebase and merge** for simple fixes\r\n-- **Merge commit** for release branches\r\n-\r\n-## Security Guidelines\r\n-\r\n-### Input Validation\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-use validator::{Validate, ValidationError};\r\n-\r\n-#[derive(Deserialize, Validate)]\r\n-pub struct CreateUserRequest {\r\n-    #[validate(length(min = 1, max = 100))]\r\n-    pub name: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(email)]\r\n-    pub email: String,\r\n-    \r\n-    #[validate(custom = \"validate_password\")]\r\n-    pub password: String,\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n-fn validate_password(password: &str) -> Result<(), ValidationError> {\r\n-    if password.len() < 8 {\r\n-        return Err(ValidationError::new(\"Password too short\"));\r\n-    }\r\n-    Ok(())\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Secrets Management\r\n-\r\n-- **Never commit secrets** to version control\r\n-- **Use environment variables** for configuration\r\n-- **Rotate secrets regularly**\r\n-- **Use secure random generation** for tokens\r\n-\r\n-```rust\r\n-// Bad: hardcoded secret\r\n-const API_KEY: &str = \"sk-1234567890abcdef\";\r\n-\r\n-// Good: environment variable\r\n-let api_key = std::env::var(\"API_KEY\")\r\n-    .context(\"API_KEY environment variable not set\")?;\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-## Getting Help\r\n-\r\n-- **GitHub Issues**: For bug reports and feature requests\r\n-- **GitHub Discussions**: For questions and general discussion\r\n-- **Documentation**: Check existing docs first\r\n-- **Code Examples**: Look at existing modules for patterns\r\n-\r\n-## Contribution Areas\r\n-\r\n-We welcome contributions in:\r\n-\r\n-- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\r\n-- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\r\n-- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\r\n-- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\r\n-- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\r\n-- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\r\n-\r\n-Thank you for contributing to HyperSpot Server!\r\n+# Contributing to HyperSpot Server\n+\n+Thank you for your interest in contributing to HyperSpot Server! This document provides guidelines and information for contributors.\n+\n+We welcome contributions in:\n+\n+- **New modules**: Add functionality to the platform\n+- **Bug fixes**: Fix issues in existing code\n+- **Documentation**: Improve guides and examples\n+- **Testing**: Add test coverage and improve test quality\n+- **Performance**: Optimize critical paths\n+- **Developer experience**: Improve tooling and workflows\n+\n+\n+## 1. Quick Start\n+\n+### 1.1 Prerequisites\n+\n+- **Rust stable** with Cargo (Edition 2021)\n+- **Git** for version control\n+- **Your favorite editor** (VS Code with rust-analyzer recommended)\n+\n+### 1.2 Development Setup\n+\n+```bash\n+# Clone the repository\n+git clone <repository-url>\n+cd hyperspot\n+\n+# Install Rust (if not already installed)\n+curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\n+\n+# Install required components\n+rustup component add clippy rustfmt\n+\n+# Build the project\n+cargo build\n+\n+# Run tests\n+cargo test\n+\n+# Start the development server (SQLite quickstart)\n+cargo run --bin hyperspot-server -- --config config/quickstart.yaml run","path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","original_commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"OK, noted","created_at":"2025-11-01T23:44:39Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T23:44:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2484010123","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2484010123"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2484010123"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2484010123/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":43,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2483914256,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":606,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2484011819","pull_request_review_id":3407845587,"id":2484011819,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6UDwMr","diff_hunk":"","path":"guidelines/SECURITY.md","commit_id":"0d71046f6fb9cb219931678fdf8dbe13f050c631","original_commit_id":"4473c8e8530f3cd3e883db0b4305ad993c16a213","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Noted","created_at":"2025-11-01T23:50:01Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T23:50:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2484011819","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2484011819"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/23#discussion_r2484011819"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/23"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2484011819/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2483916692,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"}],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":22,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/22","source_state":"closed","source_author":"modcrafter77","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #22] refactor(auth):","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"refactor_auth","pr_head_sha":"63900548b30fbac3db0e787324ed9d2ea9eefe8a","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"modcrafter77","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/22","id":2964583496,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs6ws_RI","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/22","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/22.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/22.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/22","number":22,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"refactor(auth):","user":{"login":"modcrafter77","id":216291417,"node_id":"U_kgDODORYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216291417?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77","html_url":"https://github.com/modcrafter77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Removed the unnecessary `AuthMode` wrapper struct and simplified the authentication system to use `Arc<dyn ClaimsPlugin>` directly throughout the codebase.\r\n- The `api_ingress` module has been migrated from the deprecated `JwksValidator` to the new `AuthDispatcher` system. The legacy `TokenValidator` trait has been deprecated and is no longer used.\r\n- per-route rate limiting, in-flight concurrency control, and CORS configuration features added to the API ingress module.\r\n- all \"routed\" authentication configuration mode from the `modkit-auth` crate are removed","created_at":"2025-10-30T20:29:39Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T14:41:52Z","closed_at":"2025-11-01T14:41:52Z","merged_at":"2025-11-01T14:41:52Z","merge_commit_sha":"1420869abe69dba48a6327b938aa53004fe27767","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/22/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/22/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/22/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/63900548b30fbac3db0e787324ed9d2ea9eefe8a","head":{"label":"modcrafter77:refactor_auth","ref":"refactor_auth","sha":"63900548b30fbac3db0e787324ed9d2ea9eefe8a","user":{"login":"modcrafter77","id":216291417,"node_id":"U_kgDODORYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216291417?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77","html_url":"https://github.com/modcrafter77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1048641237,"node_id":"R_kgDOPoD-1Q","name":"hyperspot","full_name":"modcrafter77/hyperspot","private":false,"owner":{"login":"modcrafter77","id":216291417,"node_id":"U_kgDODORYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216291417?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77","html_url":"https://github.com/modcrafter77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/modcrafter77/orgs","repos_